owers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/disputes-chargebacks-manager/commits/e0dc509480e9993f19cd9dc91bd90d11eebd7a1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:54:15Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:54:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#14)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"51cd3f6b01c1b66a863dee5bc1dc0f440b988948","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/disputes-chargebacks-manager/git/trees/51cd3f6b01c1b66a863dee5bc1dc0f440b988948"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/disputes-chargebacks-manager/git/commits/e0dc509480e9993f19cd9dc91bd90d11eebd7a1b","verification":{"payload":"tree 51cd3f6b01c1b66a863dee5bc1dc0f440b988948\nparent 24d819cda089cd6a6e58325d8f5e70874e58e5e6\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787673255 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787673255 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#14)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbqnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhZAQAJOjRaPt+JJyOU/bq/KBCOeH\n/u1Vak6Fpu65pzYkrd4XUnTjxUjuVMF/EsdxSIBxpr+kBO1li5tgx6eJdTxAlGoC\nWSY0NnMC9KFnDHxMhxE/Th4bRQbIsw85MTGmBF7WL4hu3jKEZwm05xmZzHkaO2DZ\nqzVhuajYMYqB6GWWuuvNkUWZIGoprRC8ZjgtNlb7Q2mGnZjsK8XnEGxgBHjQBtFp\nCbLY/dkvgGUZyAWrBXLNjn1dvNLRrO+io9fcyab8cM/rkw77gnt2uuAA/Lftx32X\nGY2cNUHNhe1PPSWqlCnJY87TOeaMAQ6EzN5ye8bTqYulegVDwDWyjFyI6i/LVYf2\nz338xhSyPZuJlcTsvN5PccqM0QSQUNY8K0vSG8ynNDfJnsJypWbZiainD0Zz1DCX\nJuqS3AURVxBwT60h3jG9bjrM9vf37W3VOzibZ9tLQR/