"url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/75607c96543db2f46a825b7a12c107be477e8e99","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDc1NjA3Yzk2NTQzZGIyZjQ2YTgyNWI3YTEyYzEwN2JlNDc3ZThlOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/3f41739279aea7ef6054302f909aae6cad3d818a","sha":"3f41739279aea7ef6054302f909aae6cad3d818a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/3f41739279aea7ef6054302f909aae6cad3d818a"}],"sha":"75607c96543db2f46a825b7a12c107be477e8e99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/75607c96543db2f46a825b7a12c107be477e8e99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/3f41739279aea7ef6054302f909aae6cad3d818a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:23:16Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:46:12Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Adopt the fleet''s GitHub Actions gate, alongside the Cloud Build one\n\nPart of the fleet''s move off paid Cloud Build, which bills SGD ~3.94/day for work that calls no\nGoogle Cloud API, reads no secret and holds no deploy authority. Actions runs the same work free\non a public repository. Proved on account-takeover-investigator first: both jobs green, 138s of\nwall clock against Cloud Build''s 266s, running the same run-grc-ci in the same reviewed image.\n\nNothing about branch protection changes here. `pr-<repo> (portable-genai-ci-sg)` remains the\nonly REQUIRED check, so this reports alongside it and cannot block a merge while it is proved.\n\nGENERATED, not written: org-metadata/scripts/render-actions-callers.py emits this from the same\nci/gcp/repository-policy.json entry the Cloud Build trigger is built from, and its --check mode\nfails on drift. The 196 workflow files retired on 2026-09-01 rotted because each was maintained\nby hand; this one has no hand to rot by.","tree":{"sha":"57dab500de46976be82cbfb9054fd56a7adb1e11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/57dab500de46976be82cbfb9054fd56a7adb1e11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/3f41739279aea7ef6054302f909aae6cad3d818a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/3f41739279aea7ef6054302f909aae6cad3d818a","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDNmNDE3MzkyNzlhZWE3ZWY2MDU0MzAyZjkwOWFhZTZjYWQzZDgxOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/873689161b9df4257b14a29d83760d2b782cae8f","sha":"873689161b9df4257b14a29d83760d2b782cae8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/873689161b9df4257b14a29d83760d2b782cae8f"}],"sha":"3f41739279aea7ef6054302f909aae6cad3d818a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/3f41739279aea7ef6054302f909aae6cad3d818a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/873689161b9df4257b14a29d83760d2b782cae8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:07:30Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:18:02Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name what actually runs the demo surface, not a deleted workflow\n\nThe demo surface claimed a `demo-gate` workflow ran it on every push. That\nworkflow was deleted with the rest when GitHub Actions were retired as\nunrunnable, so the claim named a runner that could not run and nothing said so.\n\n`scripts/README.md` went further and said `make demo-selftest` and\n`make portability` \"run in CI on every push\". They ran nowhere. The headless arc\nsurvived only because `tests/unit/test_demo_surface.py` drives the same code\ninside `make gate`; the portability tour had no automated runner at all, and\nonly its existence was asserted.\n\nBoth now run in the hosted Cloud Build check: they are named in this\nrepository''s job contract in `org-metadata/ci/gcp/repository-policy.json`, so\nthe sentence is true again rather than deleted. They cost well under a second\neach.\n\nAlso corrected in the same pass: \"No stub service\" overstated the offline\nclaim. The engine has no stub, but the generation port is bound to an offline\nmodel stub that carries the word in its own model id. The demo shows that on\nscreen, so the prose should not contradict it.","tree":{"sha":"a28c8258f9c5d8a87e8c5b6a2dfbe9387f85bb55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/a28c8258f9c5d8a87e8c5b6a2dfbe9387f85bb55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/873689161b9df4257b14a29d83760d2b782cae8f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/873689161b9df4257b14a29d83760d2b782cae8f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDg3MzY4OTE2MWI5ZGY0MjU3YjE0YTI5ZDgzNzYwZDJiNzgyY2FlOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/d7898907395d1b81ae0fd4b61fba7c7d569e8433","sha":"d7898907395d1b81ae0fd4b61fba7c7d569e8433","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/d7898907395d1b81ae0fd4b61fba7c7d569e8433"}],"sha":"873689161b9df4257b14a29d83760d2b782cae8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/873689161b9df4257b14a29d83760d2b782cae8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/d7898907395d1b81ae0fd4b61fba7c7d569e8433/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T10:23:48Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T10:30:00Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Correct the stale drop_ui.py description\n\n`scripts/README.md` said `drop_ui.py` removes the UI \"together with its npm dependabot ecosystem\nand its CI job\". The CI job half stopped being true when the GitHub Actions workflows were\nretired: `drop_ui.py` no longer deletes a `ui-gate.yaml`, because there is none to delete.\n\nProse that describes behaviour the code no longer has is how a reader learns to distrust the\nwhole file, so this says what the script does now and why the other half went.","tree":{"sha":"5bc7882de8c50a4d7b94c64f56d7a8bb62aa4c1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/5bc7882de8c50a4d7b94c64f56d7a8bb62aa4c1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/d7898907395d1b81ae0fd4b61fba7c7d569e8433","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/d7898907395d1b81ae0fd4b61fba7c7d569e8433","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKGQ3ODk4OTA3Mzk1ZDFiODFhZTBmZDRiNjFmYmE3YzdkNTY5ZTg0MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/41c19efa8fe0134d97f616ccc939de454263bd1c","sha":"41c19efa8fe0134d97f616ccc939de454263bd1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/41c19efa8fe0134d97f616ccc939de454263bd1c"}],"sha":"d7898907395d1b81ae0fd4b61fba7c7d569e8433","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/d7898907395d1b81ae0fd4b61fba7c7d569e8433"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/41c19efa8fe0134d97f616ccc939de454263bd1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T09:19:56Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T09:36:45Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Retire the GitHub Actions workflows, which had never run\n\nGitHub Actions are disabled for the whole organization\n(`enabled_repositories: \"none\"`), so every workflow file in this repository had\nnever executed and could not. The required check is the hosted Cloud Build\ntrigger, which already runs this repository''s gate, its ui-check where it has a\nUI, its terraform test, lint-gcp, and the IAP negative matrix against the\nruntime lockfile.\n\nUnrunnable configuration rots unobserved, and this had. The workflows still\npinned python 3.12 and 3.13 long after the fleet moved to 3.14, and the shared\nhard gate derived its environment prefix with a pattern that could not match any\nrepository whose prefix contains an underscore.\n\nRemoved:\n- .github/workflows/\n- the tests that asserted the contents of those files, and the test modules that\n  existed only to guard them\n- the github-actions dependabot ecosystem, which now has nothing left to pin\n\nKept, and repointed rather than deleted: every assertion that guarded something\nstill enforced. Where a test checked several things and only some were about a\nworkflow, the workflow lines were removed and the rest left standing.\n\nControl claims that cited a workflow as their evidence now name what actually\nenforces them. Where nothing does, they say so: the scheduled corpus refresh,\nthe managed release path and the promotion gate have no automated runner, which\nwas already true and is now written down.","tree":{"sha":"0a771e665100b6e1fa8d87155b51c32cd387ba56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/0a771e665100b6e1fa8d87155b51c32cd387ba56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/41c19efa8fe0134d97f616ccc939de454263bd1c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/41c19efa8fe0134d97f616ccc939de454263bd1c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDQxYzE5ZWZhOGZlMDEzNGQ5N2Y2MTZjY2M5MzlkZTQ1NDI2M2JkMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/56a7debd3135a49b5b52ad62f4f7f70c82a6fe9d","sha":"56a7debd3135a49b5b52ad62f4f7f70c82a6fe9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/56a7debd3135a49b5b52ad62f4f7f70c82a6fe9d"}],"sha":"41c19efa8fe0134d97f616ccc939de454263bd1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/41c19efa8fe0134d97f616ccc939de454263bd1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/56a7debd3135a49b5b52ad62f4f7f70c82a6fe9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:54:34Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:04:35Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump ruff in the python-minor-patch group across 1 directory\n\nBumps the python-minor-patch group with 1 update in the / directory: [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff).\n\n\nUpdates `ruff` from 0.16.4 to 0.16.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/compare/0.16.4...0.16.5)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: ruff\n  dependency-version: 0.16.5\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: python-minor-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","tree":{"sha":"50173e49879194e07555031da5fc4636e46b120b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/50173e49879194e07555031da5fc4636e46b120b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/56a7debd3135a49b5b52ad62f4f7f70c82a6fe9d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/56a7debd3135a49b5b52ad62f4f7f70c82a6fe9d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDU2YTdkZWJkMzEzNWE0OWI1YjUyYWQ2MmY0ZjdmNzBjODJhNmZlOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/e8a1095444a0c1896f2a639e971c1c97426465d8","sha":"e8a1095444a0c1896f2a639e971c1c97426465d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/e8a1095444a0c1896f2a639e971c1c97426465d8"}],"sha":"56a7debd3135a49b5b52ad62f4f7f70c82a6fe9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/56a7debd3135a49b5b52ad62f4f7f70c82a6fe9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/e8a1095444a0c1896f2a639e971c1c97426465d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T00:20:28Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:04:28Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump the npm-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 3 updates\n\nBumps the npm-minor-patch group with 3 updates in the /ui directory: [next](https://github.com/vercel/next.js), [@types/node](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/node) and [@types/react-dom](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react-dom).\n\n\nUpdates `next` from 16.3.1 to 16.3.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/compare/v16.3.1...v16.3.3)\n\nUpdates `@types/node` from 26.2.0 to 26.4.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/node)\n\nUpdates `@types/react-dom` from 19.2.4 to 19.2.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react-dom)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@types/node\"\n  dependency-version: 26.3.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react-dom\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.5\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: next\n  dependency-version: 16.3.2\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","tree":{"sha":"74f2d2a2369f009f0dce21d615fa10cb3ceec072","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/74f2d2a2369f009f0dce21d615fa10cb3ceec072"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/e8a1095444a0c1896f2a639e971c1c97426465d8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/e8a1095444a0c1896f2a639e971c1c97426465d8","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKGU4YTEwOTU0NDRhMGMxODk2ZjJhNjM5ZTk3MWMxYzk3NDI2NDY1ZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/dd8920dbf62ce7c7bbd89c72c3f2bcaa4f142bef","sha":"dd8920dbf62ce7c7bbd89c72c3f2bcaa4f142bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/dd8920dbf62ce7c7bbd89c72c3f2bcaa4f142bef"}],"sha":"e8a1095444a0c1896f2a639e971c1c97426465d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/e8a1095444a0c1896f2a639e971c1c97426465d8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/dd8920dbf62ce7c7bbd89c72c3f2bcaa4f142bef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:17:50Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:18:11Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Stop next dev writing a second working agreement into ui/\n\n`next dev` generates `ui/AGENTS.md` and `ui/CLAUDE.md` and leaves them behind.\nThe catalog''s convention is that AGENTS.md is the working agreement and it is\nthe ONLY one, with no tool-specific alias, and this repo already carries its own\nat the root: the generated pair is a second agreement plus exactly the alias\nthe convention forbids. The generated prose also contains an em-dash, which\n`make docs-check` fails on.\n\nNeither file had reached this tree yet, so this shuts the door first.\nDeleting them by hand does not hold either, because the next `next dev` writes\nthem again. This is a template defect, not a per-repo one.\n\n`agentRules` is a top-level NextConfig option in the pinned next 16.3.x, not an\nexperimental one (config-shared.d.ts, default true; the writer is\nserver/lib/generate-agent-files.js, called behind an isDev check, which is why\nthe CI production build never surfaced it). Setting it false in\nui/next.config.mjs turns the generation off at the source.\n\nThe guard lives in\n`tests/unit/test_ui_surface.py`\nand has two halves. Asserting the flag catches its removal; asserting both\nfiles are ABSENT catches a framework bump that renames or drops the option,\nwhich the flag assertion alone would sail straight through.\n\nSame change as hex-service-template PR 15, which carries the proof: a repo\nrendered, installed and started on the same next version with agent detection\non, before and after. Before, both files and the generation line in the log;\nafter, neither. Verified here by this repo''s own offline gate.","tree":{"sha":"b2cb8d6ddf258829764726e6a1288ca5752dbda3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/b2cb8d6ddf258829764726e6a1288ca5752dbda3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/dd8920dbf62ce7c7bbd89c72c3f2bcaa4f142bef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/dd8920dbf62ce7c7bbd89c72c3f2bcaa4f142bef","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKGRkODkyMGRiZjYyY2U3YzdiYmQ4OWM3MmMzZjJiY2FhNGYxNDJiZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/960e403fff7e37bfd61e9ee8aa460951893f5c5e","sha":"960e403fff7e37bfd61e9ee8aa460951893f5c5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/960e403fff7e37bfd61e9ee8aa460951893f5c5e"}],"sha":"dd8920dbf62ce7c7bbd89c72c3f2bcaa4f142bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/dd8920dbf62ce7c7bbd89c72c3f2bcaa4f142bef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/960e403fff7e37bfd61e9ee8aa460951893f5c5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:44:56Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:52:10Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Let mypy see the Google SDKs it had been resolving to nothing\n\nThe hosted `lint_gcp` job type-checks this tree against its RUNTIME lock, which is the only\ncheck in the fleet that can see the cloud adapters at all: the offline gate installs the dev\nlock, which carries no Google Cloud SDK, so mypy resolved `google.*` to nothing and reported\nnothing about the code that talks to the cloud. That job has been **non-blocking** since\n2026-08-30 while its findings were worked through. It is blocking now, and this is the\nrepository half of that promotion.\n\n**What was left before this could happen was upstream typing, and the answer is MORE type\nchecking rather than a suppression.** Two settings, in this repository''s own `pyproject.toml`\nrather than in the CI runner:\n\n* **`follow_untyped_imports = true`, scoped to `google.*`.** mypy now ANALYSES a dependency\n  that ships no `py.typed` instead of skipping it. Measured rather than argued: a bogus method\n  planted on a `google.cloud.storage` client is reported by **nothing** under the old\n  configuration and is an `attr-defined` error under this one -- the same defect class that\n  turned out to be real in `disputes-chargebacks-manager`, which called a `SessionsClient`\n  method that does not exist.\n* **`untyped_calls_exclude = [\"google\"]`.** This drops one complaint -- *\"this callee has no\n  annotations\"* -- and nothing else. `disallow_untyped_calls` exists to stop typed code calling\n  OUR untyped code; aimed at a third-party release it is a demand no work in this repository can\n  satisfy, and proto-plus generates every message `__init__` without annotations. Falsified\n  before it was trusted: with the exclusion in place, a planted nonexistent method still reports\n  `attr-defined` and a planted wrong argument type still reports `arg-type` naming the real\n  expected type.\n\n**They live here and not in the runner on purpose.** Two checks reading different configuration\nis what produced the one-line contradiction that blocked this promotion for a day: in\n`human-review-console` a `# type: ignore` was REQUIRED by the offline gate and reported UNUSED by\nlint-gcp. The offline gate and the hosted job now read the same `[tool.mypy]` and differ only in\nwhich packages are installed, which is the property the SDK declaration in this file already\nexisted to hold.\n\n**The scope on `follow_untyped_imports` is not tidiness.** Set globally it also follows the 3.14\nstandard library, where mypy 2.3.1 cannot parse CPython''s own `annotationlib.py`: `agent-registry`\nreported `Invalid syntax` in a standard-library file and **checked nothing at all**. That was\nfound by running all fifty-two trees rather than the three the shape had been validated on.\n`google.protobuf.*` is then excluded from following INSIDE that scope, because a generated `_pb2`\nmodule builds its classes at import time through a descriptor builder, so mypy reading the source\nreports `Module has no attribute \"Timestamp\"` for a class that plainly exists.\n\n**The mypy floor was legacy and is raised to `>=2.3.1`.** `>=1.10` was not neutral: both settings\nabove arrived in mypy 1.14, so the floor permitted a resolution that would not understand the\nfile configuring it. The lock already pins `mypy==2.3.1`, so this was latent rather than live.\n\nWhat this tree reports now, both checks, cold cache:\n\n| check | environment | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lint_gcp` | runtime lock (`requirements-gcp.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 65 source files` |\n| offline gate | dev lock (`requirements-dev.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 65 source files` |\n\nGate:  501 passed, 1 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"d07bc588245a1d46887219381aabbcde1debaf5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/d07bc588245a1d46887219381aabbcde1debaf5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/960e403fff7e37bfd61e9ee8aa460951893f5c5e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/960e403fff7e37bfd61e9ee8aa460951893f5c5e","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDk2MGU0MDNmZmY3ZTM3YmZkNjFlOWVlOGFhNDYwOTUxODkzZjVjNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/afb3a9dc0bc87fa21b5601422c942fa6732209bb","sha":"afb3a9dc0bc87fa21b5601422c942fa6732209bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/afb3a9dc0bc87fa21b5601422c942fa6732209bb"}],"sha":"960e403fff7e37bfd61e9ee8aa460951893f5c5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/960e403fff7e37bfd61e9ee8aa460951893f5c5e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/afb3a9dc0bc87fa21b5601422c942fa6732209bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T03:56:21Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:05:53Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Read the managed model id from where each service actually keeps it\n\nThe provenance banner resolved the managed model id from a constant declared on the\nbound adapter, and **twenty-five of thirty-eight trees answered `managed-model-unnamed`**.\n\nReading them showed the resolver was looking in the wrong place rather than the trees being\nsilent. Most of the fleet pins the id in SETTINGS, under a name chosen per repository:\n`models.reasoning`, `narrator_model`, `generation_model`, `narration_model`, `drafting_model`.\nOne kept it as a literal inside the model call. Twelve bind a managed adapter that is a\ndeployment-wired placeholder and raises rather than generating, so there is no model to name.\n\n`_GENERATOR_MODEL_ATTR` now names that settings path once per tree, beside `_GENERATOR_PORT`,\nand the resolver reads it before falling back to an adapter constant. The banner reads the same\nvalue the adapter passes to the model call rather than a second copy that drifts.\n\nThis tree keeps no settings field for it, so the adapter constant and the placeholder branch decide the answer.\n\nWhat this tree now reports:\n\n| profile | `runtime` | `generator_model` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `local` | `local` | `deterministic-offline-stub` |\n| `gcp` | `gcp` | `managed-not-implemented` |\n| `onprem` | `local` | `onprem-not-implemented` |\n\n**Two answers replace the placeholder, because they say different things.**\n`managed-not-implemented` means the managed path refuses rather than generating.\n`managed-model-unset` means the settings field exists and this deployment has not pinned a\nmodel — actionable, and different from a repository that names none. `managed-model-unnamed`\nsurvives only as a defensive fallback and **no tree reaches it any more.**\n\n**`managed-not-implemented` is the only answer that is INFERRED rather than read, so it\nis the only one that can be wrong**, and it now has a guard: a tree claiming it must not call a\nmodel API. That guard took three attempts, and each failure was found by falsifying rather than\nby reading:\n\n1. Asserting the adapter \"raises\" passed a deliberately broken `soc-fraud-fusion`, which\n   generates and also raises on bad input. Too weak.\n2. It had already let a real mis-classification through. **`conversation-qa-scorecard` calls\n   `generate_content`** and raises only when its model is unconfigured; it had been grouped with\n   the placeholders on the strength of that raise. Its model is named now, and its banner reports\n   `gemini-3.5-flash` instead of claiming the path is unimplemented.\n3. The check read the DEFAULT profile, where the answer is the offline stub, so it returned\n   before checking anything and passed the broken tree again. It reads the managed profile now.\n\nFalsified in both directions at the end: clearing `soc-fraud-fusion`''s settings path makes it\nfail with *\"reports managed-not-implemented but calls ''generate_content''\"*, and restoring it\nclears it.\n\nGate: 501 passed, 1 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"f278cc6ec932836de31f57e7f09ce178ca86ba0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/f278cc6ec932836de31f57e7f09ce178ca86ba0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/afb3a9dc0bc87fa21b5601422c942fa6732209bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/afb3a9dc0bc87fa21b5601422c942fa6732209bb","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKGFmYjNhOWRjMGJjODdmYTIxYjU2MDE0MjJjOTQyZmE2NzMyMjA5YmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/ff3ccd261e68b7317ff6a5ac7faf0422d345f661","sha":"ff3ccd261e68b7317ff6a5ac7faf0422d345f661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/ff3ccd261e68b7317ff6a5ac7faf0422d345f661"}],"sha":"afb3a9dc0bc87fa21b5601422c942fa6732209bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/afb3a9dc0bc87fa21b5601422c942fa6732209bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/ff3ccd261e68b7317ff6a5ac7faf0422d345f661/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T02:29:08Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T02:35:51Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"State where this console runs and which model answers, on every page\n\nEvery served console now names, at the top of every page, WHERE it is running and\nWHICH model answers. That is the org decision of 2026-08-30, and this tree is one of the\nthirty-eight that had not adopted it.\n\n**Not cosmetic.** These systems are demonstrated on a laptop and on a deployment, sometimes\nin the same hour, and a screenshot of one is indistinguishable from the other. A viewer who\ncannot tell which they are looking at cannot tell whether what they are reading came from a\nmanaged model or from a deterministic offline stub, and that is exactly the confusion an\naudit-first pitch cannot afford. The page says it, always, instead of the presenter saying\nit sometimes.\n\n**Both halves come from the service, on `/healthz`.** Nothing in the browser infers either.\nA console that read its own runtime from `window.location` would be right until the day the\ndeployment served through a proxy, and wrong silently after that.\n\nWhat this tree now reports:\n\n| profile | `runtime` | `generator_model` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `local` | `local` | `deterministic-offline-stub` |\n| `gcp` | `gcp` | `managed-model-unnamed` |\n| `onprem` | `local` | `onprem-not-implemented` |\n\n**`generator_model` is read off the BINDING, not kept as a second settings string.** A\nsettings field would be a claim ABOUT the binding, and the two drift the first time somebody\nrebinds a profile without remembering the second field. `_GENERATOR_PORT` names the port\nwhose active binding decides the answer, so rebinding it changes the banner in the same edit.\n\nThis tree''s managed adapter pins no model id anywhere, so the managed profile answers\n`managed-model-unnamed`. That is not a placeholder for a nicer string: it truthfully says a\nmanaged generator is bound and this repository does not name which model it calls. Inventing\nan id would be exactly the fiction the banner exists to prevent, and the honest answer makes\nthe gap visible instead.\n\n**The vocabulary distinguishes four things that are genuinely different**, because a reviewer\napproving an escalation is entitled to know which one they are reading:\n`deterministic-offline-stub` (a model-shaped port bound to a stub), `no-model` (no such port\nexists at all), `onprem-not-implemented` (the port exists and refuses), and a real model id.\n`runtime` states where the PROCESS runs, so `onprem` reads `local` -- a managed model call\ndoes not make a process cloud-hosted.\n\n`tests/unit/test_provenance_banner_contract.py` asserts agreement with the profile rather\nthan mere presence, because a banner that is present and wrong is worse than none: it turns\n\"the viewer does not know\" into \"the viewer has been told the wrong thing\". Falsified rather\nthan assumed -- making an offline profile report a Gemini id fails it with *\"the ''local''\nprofile reports ''gemini-3.5-flash'', which reads as a managed model answering a request that\nnever left the machine\"*, and reverting clears it.\n\nThe component and the `.provenance-banner` style are copied from the render-verified\n`hex-service-template`, and it is mounted in the LAYOUT rather than in a page: \"at the top of\nevery page\" is a property of the console, and a page that forgot it would be the one a\nscreenshot came from.\n\nGate: 499 passed, 1 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"d1c82991c89eb7e065f0b245152e7e425390a941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/d1c82991c89eb7e065f0b245152e7e425390a941"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/ff3ccd261e68b7317ff6a5ac7faf0422d345f661","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/ff3ccd261e68b7317ff6a5ac7faf0422d345f661","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKGZmM2NjZDI2MWU2OGI3MzE3ZmY2YTVhYzdmYWYwNDIyZDM0NWY2NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/28028fd6f79f315d95c571cbf002622e8ae2bf7b","sha":"28028fd6f79f315d95c571cbf002622e8ae2bf7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/28028fd6f79f315d95c571cbf002622e8ae2bf7b"}],"sha":"ff3ccd261e68b7317ff6a5ac7faf0422d345f661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/ff3ccd261e68b7317ff6a5ac7faf0422d345f661"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/28028fd6f79f315d95c571cbf002622e8ae2bf7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T01:22:04Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T01:27:03Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Migrate off the retired google-generativeai SDK\n\n`google-generativeai` is retired; `google-genai` replaces it. Found fleet-wide from the\none tree the widened lint-gcp job named, `obligations-control-mapping`, which reported\n`Module \"google.generativeai\" does not explicitly export attribute \"GenerativeModel\"`.\n\nThe adapter refuses rather than answering, so only the import root moves; there is no\ncall shape to port. The import still has to be right, because it IS the refusal the\nparity suite asserts: an import of a distribution that no longer exists would raise\nModuleNotFoundError for the wrong reason.\n\nThe old path is DELETED rather than kept behind a fallback, per the currency standing\ndecision: a dual-mode here would be the exact shape that decision exists to refuse.\n\n**The second defect is the declaration, and it is the more serious one.** This tree\nimported a generative-AI SDK that was declared NOWHERE -- absent from the `gcp` extra and\nfrom the lock, while the adapter is bound as the `gcp` implementation in\n`config/settings.yaml`. The port was DEAD on the managed profile and invisible, because\nthe import is lazy: the module imports clean and fails only on use. That is the same class\nthe lint-gcp job found in thirty trees on 2026-08-31, and this import was not among them\nbecause the sweep looked for `google.cloud.*`. It is declared now.\n\nFalsified rather than assumed. The offline gate never imports the SDK, so a green gate\nproves nothing about the SDK swap. `lint-gcp` was reproduced locally against every tree\n(dev-pinned mypy, --python-executable at a venv built from the runtime lock, cold cache,\nthe dev lock''s types-* stubs installed) and reports two findings, both the known untyped-upstream class in `audit.py` -- and nothing at all for\nthe migrated adapter.\n\nThat a clean report means anything was itself checked, in `rcsa-kri-erm`, by breaking it\non purpose: calling `generate_contents` and passing a `nonexistent_field` config argument\nproduced `\"Models\" has no attribute \"generate_contents\"` and `Unexpected keyword argument`,\nand restoring the file cleared both. mypy is resolving the real SDK types rather than\n`Any`, which is the check that catches calling a method the client does not have.\n\nThe lock is purely additive: five pins in (`google-genai` and its four transitive), ZERO\nexisting pins changed version, and `requirements-dev.lock` byte-identical.\n\nGate: lint clean, 489 passed, 1 skipped, eval PASS.","tree":{"sha":"d200e57d29b93b2a6a4acaef58728340d62f9725","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/d200e57d29b93b2a6a4acaef58728340d62f9725"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/28028fd6f79f315d95c571cbf002622e8ae2bf7b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/28028fd6f79f315d95c571cbf002622e8ae2bf7b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDI4MDI4ZmQ2Zjc5ZjMxNWQ5NWM1NzFjYmYwMDI2MjJlOGFlMmJmN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/9d8dec2e0b804b1ec0d47ada515d590c43a6b26a","sha":"9d8dec2e0b804b1ec0d47ada515d590c43a6b26a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/9d8dec2e0b804b1ec0d47ada515d590c43a6b26a"}],"sha":"28028fd6f79f315d95c571cbf002622e8ae2bf7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/28028fd6f79f315d95c571cbf002622e8ae2bf7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/9d8dec2e0b804b1ec0d47ada515d590c43a6b26a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T22:18:25Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T22:22:19Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Declare the client libraries the bound cloud adapters import\n\nThe `lint-gcp` job was widened from its four pilot trees to every tree carrying a\n`requirements-gcp.lock`, and run locally against each. This repository was one of **thirty of\nfifty-three** where it found the same defect: a Google Cloud client library that a bound adapter\nimports and that is declared **nowhere** — not in the `gcp` extra, not in the lock.\n\nNothing noticed because the imports are lazy. The module imports clean and the port fails only on\nuse, so the adapter is DEAD on the managed profile while every gate stays green. That is precisely\nthe blindness this job exists to remove: `make lint` installs the dev lock alone, so mypy resolves\n`google.cloud.*` to `Any` and reports nothing about the code that talks to the cloud.\n\nThe fix is a declaration, not a suppression. Each distribution is added to the `gcp` extra with a\nfloor equal to the major that actually resolved — written after resolving rather than guessed\nbefore it, because a floor invented in advance either guesses or permits a resolution predating\neverything the adapter was written against.\n\n**The lock change is purely additive: zero existing pins changed**, checked across all thirty\ntrees. `requirements-dev.lock` is untouched, so the offline gate installs exactly what it did.\n\nVerified by re-running the job against a runtime venv built from the new lock: the findings this\ncloses are gone. What remains fleet-wide is upstream untypedness in `google-cloud-logging` and\n`google.auth` (`Call to untyped function`), which is a property of those libraries rather than of\nthis tree, and is why the job stays non-blocking for now.\n\nGate: this repository''s own CI-declared target passes.","tree":{"sha":"d8749e6bf62f500ca88de1185ee78bf0c5a44972","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/d8749e6bf62f500ca88de1185ee78bf0c5a44972"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/9d8dec2e0b804b1ec0d47ada515d590c43a6b26a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/9d8dec2e0b804b1ec0d47ada515d590c43a6b26a","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDlkOGRlYzJlMGI4MDRiMWVjMGQ0N2FkYTUxNWQ1OTBjNDNhNmIyNmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/26ed8982497b19e8bc5939fbc1e6a88ecb321236","sha":"26ed8982497b19e8bc5939fbc1e6a88ecb321236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/26ed8982497b19e8bc5939fbc1e6a88ecb321236"}],"sha":"9d8dec2e0b804b1ec0d47ada515d590c43a6b26a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/9d8dec2e0b804b1ec0d47ada515d590c43a6b26a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/26ed8982497b19e8bc5939fbc1e6a88ecb321236/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:17:43Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:39:24Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Adopt hex-service-kit v0.0.6\n\nThe 0.0.6 identity knobs -- machine_tenants, subject_from, refuse_unmapped_tenant and a\nhuman-subject allowlist -- have been released and unadopted since 2026-08-28. Every one\ndefaults to what this repository already does, so this bump is the version move and\nnothing else: no behaviour changes until an adopter says so.\n\nThe lockfiles pin the 40-character commit the tag resolved to, not the tag, so what\ninstalls cannot change without a diff.","tree":{"sha":"6b0752ed871523421487a8d7167866a4062577c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/6b0752ed871523421487a8d7167866a4062577c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/26ed8982497b19e8bc5939fbc1e6a88ecb321236","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/26ed8982497b19e8bc5939fbc1e6a88ecb321236","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDI2ZWQ4OTgyNDk3YjE5ZThiYzU5MzlmYmMxZTZhODhlY2IzMjEyMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/5c9b9548ff1fea5f7e5eed0924d7aff90fa3af13","sha":"5c9b9548ff1fea5f7e5eed0924d7aff90fa3af13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/5c9b9548ff1fea5f7e5eed0924d7aff90fa3af13"}],"sha":"26ed8982497b19e8bc5939fbc1e6a88ecb321236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/26ed8982497b19e8bc5939fbc1e6a88ecb321236"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/5c9b9548ff1fea5f7e5eed0924d7aff90fa3af13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T08:56:58Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T09:31:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the platform environment variables for what they are\n\nThe HRZ_ prefix is a retired catalog code. It named nothing an operator could look up:\nHRZ_HUMAN_REVIEW_URL, HRZ7_S2S_TOKEN and HRZ_REGISTRY_* say which internal identifier a\nservice used to carry, not which service they address. The names now say that directly --\nHUMAN_REVIEW_URL, HUMAN_REVIEW_S2S_TOKEN, AGENT_REGISTRY_*, KNOWLEDGE_BASE_URL,\nGUARDRAIL_GATEWAY_URL, QUALITY_GATE_URL, OBSERVABILITY_URL, AUDIT_URL -- so a\n`.env` file can be read without the catalog open beside it.\n\nNothing about the wire contract changes; these are the names of the values, not the\nvalues. Two repositories that had gone their own way (a repo-scoped review-console URL,\na second spelling of the knowledge-base URL) join the fleet-standard names rather than\nkeeping a private variant with the code stripped out.\n\nThe review-kit call site now names the credential environment variables EXPLICITLY\ninstead of inheriting the kit''s defaults. review-kit is a commit-pinned git dependency,\nso its defaults are frozen at the pinned version: leaving them implicit would mean this\nrepository could not rename its own environment variables without a coordinated release\nof the kit and a pin bump here. Renaming the variables while relying on those defaults\nwould have failed closed at run time -- the operator sets the new name, the pinned kit\nreads the old one, and the submission goes out unauthenticated or is refused.","tree":{"sha":"d968b50a0591046f0b803c14262cca862f50f58a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/d968b50a0591046f0b803c14262cca862f50f58a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/5c9b9548ff1fea5f7e5eed0924d7aff90fa3af13","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/5c9b9548ff1fea5f7e5eed0924d7aff90fa3af13","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDVjOWI5NTQ4ZmYxZmVhNWY3ZTVlZWQwOTI0ZDdhZmY5MGZhM2FmMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/bd6159be2edbddfad0c8084c55be99f6b8866be2","sha":"bd6159be2edbddfad0c8084c55be99f6b8866be2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/bd6159be2edbddfad0c8084c55be99f6b8866be2"}],"sha":"5c9b9548ff1fea5f7e5eed0924d7aff90fa3af13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/5c9b9548ff1fea5f7e5eed0924d7aff90fa3af13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/bd6159be2edbddfad0c8084c55be99f6b8866be2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:58:37Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:01:56Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"README: the gate renders the plugin now, so say so\n\nThe quick-start line and the copyable gate command both described the offline\ngate as lint + type + test + eval. `make plugin` joined it when this repo was\npackaged as a skills-only Agent Plugin, so both understated what CI runs and the\ncopyable block no longer reproduced the gate.\n\nThe block was executed verbatim after the edit and exits 0, ending with the\nplugin render, so it is a command a reader can run rather than a description of\none.\n\nmake gate: exit 0.","tree":{"sha":"a32011927b194c129529d604a1a2a6354ad6ce3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/a32011927b194c129529d604a1a2a6354ad6ce3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/bd6159be2edbddfad0c8084c55be99f6b8866be2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/bd6159be2edbddfad0c8084c55be99f6b8866be2","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKGJkNjE1OWJlMmVkYmRkZmFkMGM4MDg0YzU1YmU5OWY2Yjg4NjZiZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/5db30641f6ae92566b738c7bef2ab34b77d6d347","sha":"5db30641f6ae92566b738c7bef2ab34b77d6d347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/5db30641f6ae92566b738c7bef2ab34b77d6d347"}],"sha":"bd6159be2edbddfad0c8084c55be99f6b8866be2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/bd6159be2edbddfad0c8084c55be99f6b8866be2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/5db30641f6ae92566b738c7bef2ab34b77d6d347/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:26:00Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:29:35Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Lock jsonschema so the manifest guard runs in CI\n\nCI installs from requirements-*.lock, not from pyproject.toml, so adding\njsonschema to the dev extra alone left the guard unable to import there. It\npassed locally and failed on arrival, which is the same shape as a gate that is\na COMMAND rather than a directory.\n\nRecompiled through scripts/lock.py (the documented path, which restores the\ntag = commit header uv pip compile destroys). jsonschema and its three\ntransitive pins are the only additions; no unrelated version moved.","tree":{"sha":"1475f92f19872443d14e14deb783537b673144d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/1475f92f19872443d14e14deb783537b673144d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/5db30641f6ae92566b738c7bef2ab34b77d6d347","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/5db30641f6ae92566b738c7bef2ab34b77d6d347","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDVkYjMwNjQxZjZhZTkyNTY2YjczOGM3YmVmMmFiMzRiNzdkNmQzNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/5a9cc0694c4a1b63ef6a42b861696f19bdb570ab","sha":"5a9cc0694c4a1b63ef6a42b861696f19bdb570ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/5a9cc0694c4a1b63ef6a42b861696f19bdb570ab"}],"sha":"5db30641f6ae92566b738c7bef2ab34b77d6d347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/5db30641f6ae92566b738c7bef2ab34b77d6d347"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/5a9cc0694c4a1b63ef6a42b861696f19bdb570ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:19:25Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:29:35Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Package this repo as a skills-only Agent Plugin\n\nPhase 4 of the Agent Plugins work. This tree declares no governed tool catalog,\nso it packages what it does have: its vendored skills, and no MCP server.\n\nscripts/render_plugin.py is the template''s, with the two names substituted rather\nthan reimplemented, so this repo and every repo generated from now on render the\nsame way. Nothing is hand-authored: identity comes from the A2A agent card the\nrepo already publishes and keywords from what that card says the agent can do. A\nmanifest typed out by hand is a second description of the service, and a second\ndescription is one that can be wrong.\n\nSkills and an MCP server are both DETECTED rather than assumed. Declaring a\nserver no module answers would be the declared-and-unperformable defect one layer\nout: a client would install the plugin and spawn a process that is not there.\n\njsonschema is a HARD dev dependency, not an optional one, so the manifest\nvalidation can never skip into green.\n\nProved red both ways: advertising a server unconditionally fails the no-server\nguard, and hand-authoring the keywords fails the derived-from-declarations guard.\n\nmake gate: exit 0. make plugin renders 6 skills, 0 servers.","tree":{"sha":"859bf9e0f1fd30e4393a5eb6261e673a10f58c3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/859bf9e0f1fd30e4393a5eb6261e673a10f58c3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/5a9cc0694c4a1b63ef6a42b861696f19bdb570ab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/5a9cc0694c4a1b63ef6a42b861696f19bdb570ab","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDVhOWNjMDY5NGM0YTFiNjNlZjZhNDJiODYxNjk2ZjE5YmRiNTcwYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/247687bfdac482d9895ff6897c1a47b4283141dc","sha":"247687bfdac482d9895ff6897c1a47b4283141dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/247687bfdac482d9895ff6897c1a47b4283141dc"}],"sha":"5a9cc0694c4a1b63ef6a42b861696f19bdb570ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/5a9cc0694c4a1b63ef6a42b861696f19bdb570ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/247687bfdac482d9895ff6897c1a47b4283141dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:54:57Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:59:54Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: hex-service-kit v0.0.5","tree":{"sha":"1e3f592916e42d87b1afde416b6c9de324dbe50e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/1e3f592916e42d87b1afde416b6c9de324dbe50e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/247687bfdac482d9895ff6897c1a47b4283141dc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/247687bfdac482d9895ff6897c1a47b4283141dc","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDI0NzY4N2JmZGFjNDgyZDk4OTVmZjY4OTdjMWE0N2I0MjgzMTQxZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/0bed702fe703199c9090238bc0e828cbc7089fda","sha":"0bed702fe703199c9090238bc0e828cbc7089fda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/0bed702fe703199c9090238bc0e828cbc7089fda"}],"sha":"247687bfdac482d9895ff6897c1a47b4283141dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/247687bfdac482d9895ff6897c1a47b4283141dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/0bed702fe703199c9090238bc0e828cbc7089fda/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:12:05Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:12:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Adopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#15)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6cfe184461363619b2e2e1e2e0c7b92bb0dc4719","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/6cfe184461363619b2e2e1e2e0c7b92bb0dc4719"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/0bed702fe703199c9090238bc0e828cbc7089fda","verification":{"payload":"tree 6cfe184461363619b2e2e1e2e0c7b92bb0dc4719\nparent 0f97af3c8e0643a6071324369a7939c167735bfb\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787706725 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787706725 +0800\n\nAdopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#15)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjj1lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARnQQACEDnaKvqHDrldztbnfRmn6M\n0Niz+NpC+dAzYP9OqhLoiXGOBhDKLjuVJZhhwaI+mpf/d+9LY/toE49HSEVe8PYQ\nhYy+ob4rsDluhUGgTJVcKR365Lbr9F8Iu3dzsyVoSBlmXJ6hS362mSKhT/6Q2HZs\nGJn9vzJJyto9qiqm25Ly3iC1xsUYRcSBRaI7RaccVUoWp1nCGzrg3zSyn1TEbgBa\n+Rcamr22R9SXiEKPjRxUjJ8wiMW0zWryoRhPomzkPVfaaWMjCFubjegiNk4B8a8z\nvCJIpagQ6tFOP4Idwonc0ZooP+Enenu7zuHXjxau7teW5EB0726SCYO6bW+7QLzS\n39XckIYwwg7ysUY93jv5eVFibwsawVglP7NDsiOZRGsTWTvCKb7jAuRGvWERh5ZY\nuJ/9PpI78jWkz4iGZ8JAgxQhjrdHBp48ZhRq0ZwaCPw0uen8mWxG3y2Xf4wYosGp\nB9FlafILyT7G1Yw65v4HigFcZk5y6K6jx9PWlv1k/ZPek0bw3BCgFERaBAqsA8Xn\nawXCPwKIoYSJKWtD+2zCiLGS1K/6QxzntnKUIFwxebMM+DQxEUrzwk8hovby8tHu\ncM/OfLDcqsqDsdkJuSvg6pH1QTKDBPJ4bUaaLex8xnyF8yzDm8hYu5OphcyDPQaV\nDgi+eAJUo7Vzq3kmIncJ\n=V18B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T01:12:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/0bed702fe703199c9090238bc0e828cbc7089fda","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDBiZWQ3MDJmZTcwMzE5OWM5MDkwMjM4YmMwZTgyOGNiYzcwODlmZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/0f97af3c8e0643a6071324369a7939c167735bfb","sha":"0f97af3c8e0643a6071324369a7939c167735bfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/0f97af3c8e0643a6071324369a7939c167735bfb"}],"sha":"0bed702fe703199c9090238bc0e828cbc7089fda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/0bed702fe703199c9090238bc0e828cbc7089fda"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/0f97af3c8e0643a6071324369a7939c167735bfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:48:05Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:48:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#14)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"41be46a148857ee1620e1d1100c396cab555f63f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/41be46a148857ee1620e1d1100c396cab555f63f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/0f97af3c8e0643a6071324369a7939c167735bfb","verification":{"payload":"tree 41be46a148857ee1620e1d1100c396cab555f63f\nparent ad0bac3b62b8c72cded4bd0a386f1d8991ae3545\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672885 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672885 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#14)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbk1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU70QAHHBzMwLdF00+ady4UwFQl9z\n/fj2KadkzvV+a/ktumuc37TgG21AyXDiSukSb6X1Iiamq6ZZMa8MGd6UXzWFYsdt\nbHJLST3ATrEU6+bT6pyqiclhW85rUbiEikwByacHT5EcF4NHfH8U8UmR7inmWbYT\niA8FTm4/Xg/Nc5Tq3IVn3Z0X5nDRuaIE+VDScDr4vS7GQgvHVjnj3xF81DDtgTG/\n1TqjpEievqfwBrMJmQs6deJ00Ax0yna/hK1AWB0Wply8TibXYlBogRvmfdphRBMq\nQMiULGaa0lasx9Ni0OW7/bSeBBesqn2RvlVmn5gNw573NwclSM4b3ocUOa0Rvgqu\nwAdqR2J6JUmDmzwqBFb0GX1Bz+hyMEsZYm56wUZjP6OM92EWVyaUglHIF9c0bIk8\nQmU2AUmtnkza0NlUMFMuPFKfC+c/cTpdgiglPHfdo3b3aUFJDx2vcXQ44tESURN2\nqZ3Ea/vyC+UfPpitqPqd//kMvN3k3PbFDdQKSq2AU+qzlGuTU+uBW0+uOhdeCYoU\nr6PCfjPTl7eMzhvWzW71rxHt7nrbQJH02a/ihYBwxMRWBoYF29kAQyFLE8+p40lP\n0IVQjnF/Fojc79yhUYwlVVx+9l6my+eiiwaL/WIS+s6mH5BnU+lwmKjveW7VVCzk\nvhbDpi3+Qg62mIRVz+d5\n=PUXt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:48:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/0f97af3c8e0643a6071324369a7939c167735bfb","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKDBmOTdhZjNjOGUwNjQzYTYwNzEzMjQzNjlhNzkzOWMxNjc3MzViZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/ad0bac3b62b8c72cded4bd0a386f1d8991ae3545","sha":"ad0bac3b62b8c72cded4bd0a386f1d8991ae3545","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/ad0bac3b62b8c72cded4bd0a386f1d8991ae3545"}],"sha":"0f97af3c8e0643a6071324369a7939c167735bfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/0f97af3c8e0643a6071324369a7939c167735bfb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/ad0bac3b62b8c72cded4bd0a386f1d8991ae3545/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:15:10Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:15:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#13)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 474 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","tree":{"sha":"2392ad13363146f21550adef05405dceb37934ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/2392ad13363146f21550adef05405dceb37934ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/ad0bac3b62b8c72cded4bd0a386f1d8991ae3545","verification":{"payload":"tree 2392ad13363146f21550adef05405dceb37934ac\nparent 3c62317432d30c9defeaf01ebb02a90ac170bcf4\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787670910 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787670910 +0800\n\nBind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#13)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 474 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbF/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAzEQADqXMDcYV004wBGd1S+Aozg0\nuZ/FKQGXE67hqBKBkKgTtQJny8zOAdYbir8TURpK8s2ST31hvtS7SzOXjdl0KbmE\n0HaVWQ4d5jUw48Y/HUrANJy9ZwRoI+BWoUK/X/gwsaXfYaDCEgwyMeq3A28bDIEC\ngvX/6AqRZuY190oCLDO5E+JSytcgQQ8n9tTGsbE1cZhOLJUo8Uh9STy+cZ0XHcGR\nAP2/NZRe7i4+IA0AE82gzR/Lnj1N4W0OBUtlbXf2M2M8msP42dEp39wdOEyqW+pG\nQzqMCp/whqq0MUUWr8ecpYp7lQW8XzDJlzCktWIg43v2sgrV61t5aEjUWo6jsRVQ\nFAf+6FJLac9E4h7VRIPX+WCNDDJvRFCoRDnmA6fSA5kjpQNzxJ+LAkLXqX2f7sWG\nBnJhfpluocla9dkRkIeRxvHGMTs5ZOC/s9xCwI2wvrZSSr4vD7Ve4t4ypXnqKdOB\nxtSNlwzODuaobrCdVtqVPR+xJN773PicO1Zp6d0AQ1uzTor0+6f2RFRGG/cqtqcb\n5GJz2ggvP/WSBwKWYiyJrfUa0e6wjewKP3vDO94vPcVl1Y3MABc/dOj5aglLGTZ0\nYKb1QwLHSYwjNvBHvpIrpqNsRdjWXCKgj8uTWSeKlO+WnjC96VNUWEV4ZN3bYMhE\nans8nMeznGSv7aTiyeGC\n=I7gN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:15:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/ad0bac3b62b8c72cded4bd0a386f1d8991ae3545","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAEdoAKGFkMGJhYzNiNjJiOGM3MmNkZWQ0YmQwYTM4NmYxZDg5OTFhZTM1NDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commit/3c62317432d30c9defeaf01ebb02a90ac170bcf4","sha":"3c62317432d30c9defeaf01ebb02a90ac170bcf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/3c62317432d30c9defeaf01ebb02a90ac170bcf4"}],"sha":"ad0bac3b62b8c72cded4bd0a386f1d8991ae3545","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/ad0bac3b62b8c72cded4bd0a386f1d8991ae3545"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/commits/3c62317432d30c9defeaf01ebb02a90ac170bcf4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:58:14Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:58:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Re-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#12)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0bac93d3390eb14acc1b98faa2daac524d9f0155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/trees/0bac93d3390eb14acc1b98faa2daac524d9f0155"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/recon-breaks-engine/git/commits/3c62317432d30c9defeaf01ebb02a90ac170bcf4","verification":{"payload":"tree 0bac93d3390eb14acc1b98faa2daac524d9f0155\nparent 6f5d878366de59fcc3afdfd66cc69341f883a58a\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787644694 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787644694 +0800\n\nRe-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#12)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjUsWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACBIQAKHCGocREor6TJG5rdQJiMub\nVgK2/1+VVJbcIWYNmpvtBQ/mOnynGWdfsvUh0tLc3f++slOYv/3UhfTg5MhmMXlj\ni9c0rkG4wW2irrmKqV/67yajhmKTJvkZWrPlS2pYHS1Va+pIOaupkaoiiifH2n8p\n1WbTB7UpOoZ8IdfdnSvh7jFpwU9AQY0DsKpdTiY7extyikfYuoCmVFWBEeQljJAs\ng/e9IQLX3AbHO9UGv73XHR4vjE6Rf6+N0oRXkv0BF2mZqQd9AQeq9EcQ3IRkRN8N\n8gI7Ll9je5Zf+9coZsIQ1mktwccx7VmngCsjoOSdt5R6q/hsxgB8Zx9IYIsHml34\neEZjcfl2KauGWHWUKDen9LAl1zx/Qlj+vbI+TvKLtJTS+CddBOtEnKgxjlsc56pK\nw5gkw9vHZ7zJXzsnUA3YiYmc6RaVQ0OWbk2r0Qu16qyJ5bYCPoqoJZvY4pd75k75\n2RoTlMjmiPOi9Dfho8sAGsL0cTcPaR98FTUCW5OiKPVR4YQBppzRgtY5wCHJcKco\nNwysEdKC4AXk9K7