me":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:46:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#14)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"a8fc3ed5439b2f466b4b4faf0428eff53cefa0a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/git/trees/a8fc3ed5439b2f466b4b4faf0428eff53cefa0a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/git/commits/781a383fa107d6adc060a086780745f9417ad283","verification":{"payload":"tree a8fc3ed5439b2f466b4b4faf0428eff53cefa0a5\nparent be85c9c6ea0c4a6fa018e8782127079a881e2c68\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672805 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672805 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#14)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbjlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3LcQAH0g0d+AgmyEPYBNlVv1VXFH\nPZgDvWTdKSeMCVC+96ZmxPaFPyLZIGLN/ssE7k/4K0Ln1SSWFyuAILGUr9Re+qC5\n1j2sDwj7NbHHmyE2vrDk41i8BH5voQGihvyAvMWwTEoAYgA/++EckM/Ljy9rOmX5\n3MjzKPyVdFp17xJkFUFIW4K8NVLhZSX8GYxLZB1YOSTLOt17iY5TMhbGXxx+WyeE\nSVesZiaVLIQ2cZv3AFSBumjBtzNL7XK34MU/liw5aZCzurBUw9o7C1Wxpp6ghr2s\n+WzeMuy/5b48mwdOwEslQ9x+fKvm+S/1gdMYZfHDJZKk1qkApXxE1Yc+/ipfELn+\nfOVzDNooDN2Fotl6xTEnLhw1cEzOicaYju9qH348X3XFP70mqDTtPipJPO6nEGlZ\nvfHJynKkCokGX9ZG2GQ2hei9rI1b8o3jDt/NQT4HLPaaUswtZeVPYqKKGzhLrEtD\nRvpR5NcjHfAVPUxn1fw328hzhUnVmDRSQY21oOQfxXvO/jJVtCAlGexaJ8PWtEn+\nH2kNvWg0BlZJ3N4NwqTqn0MDuKHa++cRmieBTE/Cq4wkyGcm6q3gyCKqvk2NoApU\nAHc85qzueDWVp84rPmjlrXq3IAJhrWFqD7q71ttqTgW/IP3ltOG10/0pHXDP74HE\nRGTJNb8Q9ZCp+prWCbpZ\n=xCaU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:46:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commit/781a383fa107d6adc060a086780745f9417ad283","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAs9oAKDc4MWEzODNmYTEwN2Q2YWRjMDYwYTA4Njc4MDc0NWY5NDE3YWQyODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commit/be85c9c6ea0c4a6fa018e8782127079a881e2c68","sha":"be85c9c6ea0c4a6fa018e8782127079a881e2c68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commits/be85c9c6ea0c4a6fa018e8782127079a881e2c68"}],"sha":"781a383fa107d6adc060a086780745f9417ad283","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commits/781a383fa107d6adc060a086780745f9417ad283"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commits/be85c9c6ea0c4a6fa018e8782127079a881e2c68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:12:17Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:12:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#13)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 476 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","tree":{"sha":"13135dfafa036e37adb78bc1acff4f5d1d4d2a9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/git/trees/13135dfafa036e37adb78bc1acff4f5d1d4d2a9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/git/commits/be85c9c6ea0c4a6fa018e8782127079a881e2c68","verification":{"payload":"tree 13135dfafa036e37adb78bc1acff4f5d1d4d2a9a\nparent 3a3232c61e663d44684e58202aaa44cff9d9ed78\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787670737 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787670737 +0800\n\nBind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#13)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 476 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbDRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIcYQADa6a82ZJawVhnTYu4ALlX0Z\nsHB8sIm9tig/LLHPn7cXxyEIRQD+AsiCvNbXG3udK/sv7G19eWzug2rn04kc2zjL\nt3Zar5lKJJiLpQM+etjAIdlUwa++bESRI1/DHzDTajGhGIlP4K5lZZCjkiBNKqGp\ntS4XG3KQ+PNym9HDgI2DdNVg8hqF4WvKmMJdOzPAbsDqGiELZhVbD+NMeyvujE/+\nPPNBI2IFRhKw6iifVx9m4FRwAFrV3SP0/a5Tboa0snDr5Y6VzTsB6EjokWQfCYKg\nkBvIZNlPpWlJz3q1cl41AhMK2WKl0i8dQ9S9UFT3lZzABJ7M3PkfgwOvJBANjm2M\nBwoFqo6QziSJVSjuMOTExEMTtIitW0PgbttaWR8TKzknJvFiIreT4CmLQN6Mmiqa\nVhPHfvEhZ2BPEJkWwPfSnJoJWbnnmdAPej5SjeoG87dU2pg1QHIutFMH0JGRyil7\ngKSl7p9XhYu41mlE6E4iZHr2DFocWaKwwPextSLE42BY2lKgok4zBE3h+YAdbj5S\n7/0bfcqSTX/dzBLkAonL2YbRM6PLEOJ/lk9lkE2h4RCFlLYImo7fO3+yCRs55O6h\nk+t/RBUhd/XzasSBBGAcqYHeo6Ni9X2FVpuouK2Yv3FF0cjixLKXUhKGytXAb46e\n6FJpTn5+CHOjZN+KKKs7\n=12My\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:12:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commit/be85c9c6ea0c4a6fa018e8782127079a881e2c68","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAs9oAKGJlODVjOWM2ZWEwYzRhNmZhMDE4ZTg3ODIxMjcwNzlhODgxZTJjNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commit/3a3232c61e663d44684e58202aaa44cff9d9ed78","sha":"3a3232c61e663d44684e58202aaa44cff9d9ed78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commits/3a3232c61e663d44684e58202aaa44cff9d9ed78"}],"sha":"be85c9c6ea0c4a6fa018e8782127079a881e2c68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commits/be85c9c6ea0c4a6fa018e8782127079a881e2c68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commits/3a3232c61e663d44684e58202aaa44cff9d9ed78/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:55:10Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:55:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Re-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#12)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cfef6fe9384d1d4a36ea352f4447cb20b290d632","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/git/trees/cfef6fe9384d1d4a36ea352f4447cb20b290d632"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/git/commits/3a3232c61e663d44684e58202aaa44cff9d9ed78","verification":{"payload":"tree cfef6fe9384d1d4a36ea352f4447cb20b290d632\nparent 58118c64fb4eb7e617176d4da5dabf4258d0b4f2\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787644510 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787644510 +0800\n\nRe-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#12)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjUpeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyDIQAK2uUspJjICxB5E2wcUwYsqc\nApx22nY4AU7DwYFCYRU6WtdtyRfdKGfT4DNxMsptFglF5ITRUhN8yS4Luz/FfhKa\nKyysGehjMM0SZwUa5h6iNTOTbQykx+85b10yzqJlW3DRvGNWEhXEsnRTiBjgzZyy\n5BdNowKDIdA//fpV7xy4ufatSdiJU1EEjdNMTFz8S+w8jN7GE61aB4sXfps14OYh\nYIaCcKFD12fzufwLVgl6S9YOTqN87IkZynkJknvh+SdGfcijk7gSfhR3txA5zjfS\n6s2ZgiybrrUD+zpq+MijllyIpEpRALstjpZXP3xoUIMGQpwrPHuQNPbmrYYKfLQX\nEAU1uW8vVo/laP6AIW9wcQkMl94IJVXz6Uoruz+iGYPtpR4X3vKuchjOI9U4ICtv\nwcWDbvCJOOFxVfz0acquBuUpLJqFdWwxruG0hCJ1AQi7WQ0IeY6QCt+o8T/u/vNj\njfbIjJ7zab62OJd9FboyWAk5PnnoSZihGVPBq8PqQabpemxR6E9gVYb2sWJThCjG\n1FKWiFIHu9MOacRWc6pmrOdiQCQ7Y9i44iV3tN5dVQHZCD1Fjijiwt+XJOBmHLns\nLUMNJHUAF2dXRre3LWL8iYrrHM6dJjIzEmmJ0mzImeB9u8JrwNOKAB57vSJb58P1\nHdR38NgcbUsQmKkFhhrB\n=REDH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T07:55:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commit/3a3232c61e663d44684e58202aaa44cff9d9ed78","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiAs9oAKDNhMzIzMmM2MWU2NjNkNDQ2ODRlNTgyMDJhYWE0NGNmZjlkOWVkNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commit/58118c64fb4eb7e617176d4da5dabf4258d0b4f2","sha":"58118c64fb4eb7e617176d4da5dabf4258d0b4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commits/58118c64fb4eb7e617176d4da5dabf4258d0b4f2"}],"sha":"3a3232c61e663d44684e58202aaa44cff9d9ed78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conflicts-gifts-pad-register/commits/3a3232c61e663d44684e58202aaa44cff9d9ed78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashis