ommit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:50:50Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:54:15Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump ruff in the python-minor-patch group across 1 directory\n\nBumps the python-minor-patch group with 1 update in the / directory: [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff).\n\n\nUpdates `ruff` from 0.16.3 to 0.16.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/compare/0.16.3...0.16.5)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: ruff\n  dependency-version: 0.16.4\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: python-minor-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","tree":{"sha":"163183c89a1d520a77b915a93b8e1ac2ff25588c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/163183c89a1d520a77b915a93b8e1ac2ff25588c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/f23c1fb70960efd29202483f9f293f46b9233306","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/f23c1fb70960efd29202483f9f293f46b9233306","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiBcdoAKGYyM2MxZmI3MDk2MGVmZDI5MjAyNDgzZjlmMjkzZjQ2YjkyMzMzMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/19fc36c7310caa46a90d085b14d50e62dcc6ffce","sha":"19fc36c7310caa46a90d085b14d50e62dcc6ffce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/19fc36c7310caa46a90d085b14d50e62dcc6ffce"}],"sha":"f23c1fb70960efd29202483f9f293f46b9233306","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/f23c1fb70960efd29202483f9f293f46b9233306"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/19fc36c7310caa46a90d085b14d50e62dcc6ffce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:42:46Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:48:22Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Let mypy see the Google SDKs it had been resolving to nothing\n\nThe hosted `lint_gcp` job type-checks this tree against its RUNTIME lock, which is the only\ncheck in the fleet that can see the cloud adapters at all: the offline gate installs the dev\nlock, which carries no Google Cloud SDK, so mypy resolved `google.*` to nothing and reported\nnothing about the code that talks to the cloud. That job has been **non-blocking** since\n2026-08-30 while its findings were worked through. It is blocking now, and this is the\nrepository half of that promotion.\n\n**What was left before this could happen was upstream typing, and the answer is MORE type\nchecking rather than a suppression.** Two settings, in this repository''s own `pyproject.toml`\nrather than in the CI runner:\n\n* **`follow_untyped_imports = true`, scoped to `google.*`.** mypy now ANALYSES a dependency\n  that ships no `py.typed` instead of skipping it. Measured rather than argued: a bogus method\n  planted on a `google.cloud.storage` client is reported by **nothing** under the old\n  configuration and is an `attr-defined` error under this one -- the same defect class that\n  turned out to be real in `disputes-chargebacks-manager`, which called a `SessionsClient`\n  method that does not exist.\n* **`untyped_calls_exclude = [\"google\"]`.** This drops one complaint -- *\"this callee has no\n  annotations\"* -- and nothing else. `disallow_untyped_calls` exists to stop typed code calling\n  OUR untyped code; aimed at a third-party release it is a demand no work in this repository can\n  satisfy, and proto-plus generates every message `__init__` without annotations. Falsified\n  before it was trusted: with the exclusion in place, a planted nonexistent method still reports\n  `attr-defined` and a planted wrong argument type still reports `arg-type` naming the real\n  expected type.\n\n**They live here and not in the runner on purpose.** Two checks reading different configuration\nis what produced the one-line contradiction that blocked this promotion for a day: in\n`human-review-console` a `# type: ignore` was REQUIRED by the offline gate and reported UNUSED by\nlint-gcp. The offline gate and the hosted job now read the same `[tool.mypy]` and differ only in\nwhich packages are installed, which is the property the SDK declaration in this file already\nexisted to hold.\n\n**The scope on `follow_untyped_imports` is not tidiness.** Set globally it also follows the 3.14\nstandard library, where mypy 2.3.1 cannot parse CPython''s own `annotationlib.py`: `agent-registry`\nreported `Invalid syntax` in a standard-library file and **checked nothing at all**. That was\nfound by running all fifty-two trees rather than the three the shape had been validated on.\n`google.protobuf.*` is then excluded from following INSIDE that scope, because a generated `_pb2`\nmodule builds its classes at import time through a descriptor builder, so mypy reading the source\nreports `Module has no attribute \"Timestamp\"` for a class that plainly exists.\n\n**The mypy floor was legacy and is raised to `>=2.3.1`.** `>=1.10` was not neutral: both settings\nabove arrived in mypy 1.14, so the floor permitted a resolution that would not understand the\nfile configuring it. The lock already pins `mypy==2.3.1`, so this was latent rather than live.\n\nWhat this tree reports now, both checks, cold cache:\n\n| check | environment | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lint_gcp` | runtime lock (`requirements-gcp.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 70 source files` |\n| offline gate | dev lock (`requirements-dev.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 70 source files` |\n\nGate:  503 passed, 11 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"b8a113116133db24555a011d6e3dc6ad9bf44fb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/b8a113116133db24555a011d6e3dc6ad9bf44fb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/19fc36c7310caa46a90d085b14d50e62dcc6ffce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/19fc36c7310caa46a90d085b14d50e62dcc6ffce","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiBcdoAKDE5ZmMzNmM3MzEwY2FhNDZhOTBkMDg1YjE0ZDUwZTYyZGNjNmZmY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/ddc840f12992a9c756caafe417f390b0c90363bf","sha":"ddc840f12992a9c756caafe417f390b0c90363bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/ddc840f12992a9c756caafe417f390b0c90363bf"}],"sha":"19fc36c7310caa46a90d085b14d50e62dcc6ffce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/19fc36c7310caa46a90d085b14d50e62dcc6ffce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/ddc840f12992a9c756caafe417f390b0c90363bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T01:21:37Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T01:26:26Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Migrate off the retired google-generativeai SDK\n\n`google-generativeai` is retired; `google-genai` replaces it. Found fleet-wide from the\none tree the widened lint-gcp job named, `obligations-control-mapping`, which reported\n`Module \"google.generativeai\" does not explicitly export attribute \"GenerativeModel\"`.\n\nThe call shape differs, so this is a migration and not a pin bump: a stateful\n`GenerativeModel` holding the system instruction becomes a client plus a per-call\n`GenerateContentConfig` that carries it. The client is constructed with NO arguments,\nwhich is what the retired SDK also did -- credentials and backend come from the\nenvironment, so a deployment can point this at either the Gemini Developer API or Vertex\n(`GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI`) without a code change here.\n\nThe old path is DELETED rather than kept behind a fallback, per the currency standing\ndecision: a dual-mode here would be the exact shape that decision exists to refuse.\n\n**The second defect is the declaration, and it is the more serious one.** This tree\nimported a generative-AI SDK that was declared NOWHERE -- absent from the `gcp` extra and\nfrom the lock, while the adapter is bound as the `gcp` implementation in\n`config/settings.yaml`. The port was DEAD on the managed profile and invisible, because\nthe import is lazy: the module imports clean and fails only on use. That is the same class\nthe lint-gcp job found in thirty trees on 2026-08-31, and this import was not among them\nbecause the sweep looked for `google.cloud.*`. It is declared now.\n\nFalsified rather than assumed. The offline gate never imports the SDK, so a green gate\nproves nothing about the SDK swap. `lint-gcp` was reproduced locally against every tree\n(dev-pinned mypy, --python-executable at a venv built from the runtime lock, cold cache,\nthe dev lock''s types-* stubs installed) and reports five findings, all the known untyped-upstream class: `fetch_id_token` in three adapters and `Client`/`logger` in `audit.py` -- and nothing at all for\nthe migrated adapter.\n\nThat a clean report means anything was itself checked, in `rcsa-kri-erm`, by breaking it\non purpose: calling `generate_contents` and passing a `nonexistent_field` config argument\nproduced `\"Models\" has no attribute \"generate_contents\"` and `Unexpected keyword argument`,\nand restoring the file cleared both. mypy is resolving the real SDK types rather than\n`Any`, which is the check that catches calling a method the client does not have.\n\nThe lock is purely additive: five pins in (`google-genai` and its four transitive), ZERO\nexisting pins changed version, and `requirements-dev.lock` byte-identical.\n\nGate: lint clean, 503 passed, 11 skipped, eval PASS.","tree":{"sha":"4cff9ea95865224d7564a2b146c41c667cf4949c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/4cff9ea95865224d7564a2b146c41c667cf4949c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/ddc840f12992a9c756caafe417f390b0c90363bf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/ddc840f12992a9c756caafe417f390b0c90363bf","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiBcdoAKGRkYzg0MGYxMjk5MmE5Yzc1NmNhYWZlNDE3ZjM5MGIwYzkwMzYzYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/d4532179a60372011ec12246baa4c9bf28e65b89","sha":"d4532179a60372011ec12246baa4c9bf28e65b89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/d4532179a60372011ec12246baa4c9bf28e65b89"}],"sha":"ddc840f12992a9c756caafe417f390b0c90363bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/ddc840f12992a9c756caafe417f390b0c90363bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/d4532179a60372011ec12246baa4c9bf28e65b89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T22:34:24Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T22:36:53Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Fix two cloud-adapter defects the cascade was hiding\n\nTwo defects that only became VISIBLE once the undeclared client libraries were declared.\n\nThis is the cascade effect working in reverse. One `google.cloud` sub-package missing from the\nlock makes mypy synthesise the whole namespace, and every correctly installed sibling then\nreports `has no attribute` — noise that buries anything real underneath it. With the\ndeclarations fixed fleet-wide, the checker could finally resolve these modules and immediately\nreported two things nothing had ever been able to see:\n\n- **continuous-controls-monitoring** bound `SecurityCenterClient` and `AssetServiceClient` to one\n  variable name across two branches. The first assignment fixed the type, so the second was a\n  type error. Harmless at runtime because the first branch returns, and wrong to leave: they are\n  different clients. They have different names now.\n\n- **disputes-chargebacks-manager called a method that does not exist.**\n  `SessionsClient.get_session_entity_type` is not on that client — it lives on\n  `SessionEntityTypesClient`, and a session entity type is a slot-value override rather than a\n  transcript, so even the right client would not have returned conversation turns. The port\n  would have raised `AttributeError` on its first live call. Nothing caught it: the SDK import is\n  lazy and the whole method is excluded from coverage, so it imported clean and was never run.\n\n  It now REFUSES explicitly rather than being replaced with a guess. Dialogflow CX serves\n  transcripts through Conversational Insights, not the Sessions API, and writing that against no\n  live CCAI to test it would be inventing an implementation and calling it a fix. This is the\n  shape the fleet already uses for a port that is named but not yet wired.\n\n  The behavioural-parity contract now declares BOTH refusals, because both are true: with no SDK\n  installed the lazy import raises first (what it pinned before), and with the SDK present it\n  raises `NotImplementedError`. The lazy import is deliberately left ahead of the raise so the\n  offline behaviour this contract pins is unchanged.\n\nGates: each repository''s own CI-declared target passes.","tree":{"sha":"d542e299465f31d71f9ea09c73f97e78087f0545","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/d542e299465f31d71f9ea09c73f97e78087f0545"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/d4532179a60372011ec12246baa4c9bf28e65b89","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/d4532179a60372011ec12246baa4c9bf28e65b89","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiBcdoAKGQ0NTMyMTc5YTYwMzcyMDExZWMxMjI0NmJhYTRjOWJmMjhlNjViODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/18b9f115def050657d993b6bcea744320f37529a","sha":"18b9f115def050657d993b6bcea744320f37529a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/18b9f115def050657d993b6bcea744320f37529a"}],"sha":"d4532179a60372011ec12246baa4c9bf28e65b89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/d4532179a60372011ec12246baa4c9bf28e65b89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/18b9f115def050657d993b6bcea744320f37529a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T22:17:14Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T22:20:24Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Declare the client libraries the bound cloud adapters import\n\nThe `lint-gcp` job was widened from its four pilot trees to every tree carrying a\n`requirements-gcp.lock`, and run locally against each. This repository was one of **thirty of\nfifty-three** where it found the same defect: a Google Cloud client library that a bound adapter\nimports and that is declared **nowhere** — not in the `gcp` extra, not in the lock.\n\nNothing noticed because the imports are lazy. The module imports clean and the port fails only on\nuse, so the adapter is DEAD on the managed profile while every gate stays green. That is precisely\nthe blindness this job exists to remove: `make lint` installs the dev lock alone, so mypy resolves\n`google.cloud.*` to `Any` and reports nothing about the code that talks to the cloud.\n\nThe fix is a declaration, not a suppression. Each distribution is added to the `gcp` extra with a\nfloor equal to the major that actually resolved — written after resolving rather than guessed\nbefore it, because a floor invented in advance either guesses or permits a resolution predating\neverything the adapter was written against.\n\n**The lock change is purely additive: zero existing pins changed**, checked across all thirty\ntrees. `requirements-dev.lock` is untouched, so the offline gate installs exactly what it did.\n\nVerified by re-running the job against a runtime venv built from the new lock: the findings this\ncloses are gone. What remains fleet-wide is upstream untypedness in `google-cloud-logging` and\n`google.auth` (`Call to untyped function`), which is a property of those libraries rather than of\nthis tree, and is why the job stays non-blocking for now.\n\nGate: this repository''s own CI-declared target passes.","tree":{"sha":"8dc675331dff9e33e7fffaed4c45c826a88bbf25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/8dc675331dff9e33e7fffaed4c45c826a88bbf25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/18b9f115def050657d993b6bcea744320f37529a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/18b9f115def050657d993b6bcea744320f37529a","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiBcdoAKDE4YjlmMTE1ZGVmMDUwNjU3ZDk5M2I2YmNlYTc0NDMyMGYzNzUyOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/0e77f746e140607ac40727109b6dd5325ecc18d3","sha":"0e77f746e140607ac40727109b6dd5325ecc18d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/0e77f746e140607ac40727109b6dd5325ecc18d3"}],"sha":"18b9f115def050657d993b6bcea744320f37529a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/18b9f115def050657d993b6bcea744320f37529a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/0e77f746e140607ac40727109b6dd5325ecc18d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:17:42Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:36:56Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Adopt hex-service-kit v0.0.6\n\nThe 0.0.6 identity knobs -- machine_tenants, subject_from, refuse_unmapped_tenant and a\nhuman-subject allowlist -- have been released and unadopted since 2026-08-28. Every one\ndefaults to what this repository already does, so this bump is the version move and\nnothing else: no behaviour changes until an adopter says so.\n\nThe lockfiles pin the 40-character commit the tag resolved to, not the tag, so what\ninstalls cannot change without a diff.","tree":{"sha":"cc6329718117cc3ef4a0f9be0fa3e99566a07cc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/cc6329718117cc3ef4a0f9be0fa3e99566a07cc8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/0e77f746e140607ac40727109b6dd5325ecc18d3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/0e77f746e140607ac40727109b6dd5325ecc18d3","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiBcdoAKDBlNzdmNzQ2ZTE0MDYwN2FjNDA3MjcxMDliNmRkNTMyNWVjYzE4ZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/b7a91b510287a70f421243eda0a3c0ca46ae10ea","sha":"b7a91b510287a70f421243eda0a3c0ca46ae10ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/b7a91b510287a70f421243eda0a3c0ca46ae10ea"}],"sha":"0e77f746e140607ac40727109b6dd5325ecc18d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/0e77f746e140607ac40727109b6dd5325ecc18d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/b7a91b510287a70f421243eda0a3c0ca46ae10ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T08:56:02Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T09:29:20Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the platform environment variables for what they are\n\nThe HRZ_ prefix is a retired catalog code. It named nothing an operator could look up:\nHRZ_HUMAN_REVIEW_URL, HRZ7_S2S_TOKEN and HRZ_REGISTRY_* say which internal identifier a\nservice used to carry, not which service they address. The names now say that directly --\nHUMAN_REVIEW_URL, HUMAN_REVIEW_S2S_TOKEN, AGENT_REGISTRY_*, KNOWLEDGE_BASE_URL,\nGUARDRAIL_GATEWAY_URL, QUALITY_GATE_URL, OBSERVABILITY_URL, AUDIT_URL -- so a\n`.env` file can be read without the catalog open beside it.\n\nNothing about the wire contract changes; these are the names of the values, not the\nvalues. Two repositories that had gone their own way (a repo-scoped review-console URL,\na second spelling of the knowledge-base URL) join the fleet-standard names rather than\nkeeping a private variant with the code stripped out.\n\nThe review-kit call site now names the credential environment variables EXPLICITLY\ninstead of inheriting the kit''s defaults. review-kit is a commit-pinned git dependency,\nso its defaults are frozen at the pinned version: leaving them implicit would mean this\nrepository could not rename its own environment variables without a coordinated release\nof the kit and a pin bump here. Renaming the variables while relying on those defaults\nwould have failed closed at run time -- the operator sets the new name, the pinned kit\nreads the old one, and the submission goes out unauthenticated or is refused.","tree":{"sha":"46f0373f9878774df89cf3517d223cd7498c4093","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/46f0373f9878774df89cf3517d223cd7498c4093"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/b7a91b510287a70f421243eda0a3c0ca46ae10ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/b7a91b510287a70f421243eda0a3c0ca46ae10ea","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiBcdoAKGI3YTkxYjUxMDI4N2E3MGY0MjEyNDNlZGEwYTNjMGNhNDZhZTEwZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/ef3ace84efd77f3eaabaf1c25e87ea993ed7a5b2","sha":"ef3ace84efd77f3eaabaf1c25e87ea993ed7a5b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/ef3ace84efd77f3eaabaf1c25e87ea993ed7a5b2"}],"sha":"b7a91b510287a70f421243eda0a3c0ca46ae10ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/b7a91b510287a70f421243eda0a3c0ca46ae10ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/ef3ace84efd77f3eaabaf1c25e87ea993ed7a5b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:53:21Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:59:54Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: hex-service-kit v0.0.5","tree":{"sha":"e00aaa84620610699b5d0ea9214bda3b9d42dd83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/e00aaa84620610699b5d0ea9214bda3b9d42dd83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/ef3ace84efd77f3eaabaf1c25e87ea993ed7a5b2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/ef3ace84efd77f3eaabaf1c25e87ea993ed7a5b2","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiBcdoAKGVmM2FjZTg0ZWZkNzdmM2VhYWJhZjFjMjVlODdlYTk5M2VkN2E1YjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/6ac7c5cbbf0beed28e51fbea14f6d464d421cc13","sha":"6ac7c5cbbf0beed28e51fbea14f6d464d421cc13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/6ac7c5cbbf0beed28e51fbea14f6d464d421cc13"}],"sha":"ef3ace84efd77f3eaabaf1c25e87ea993ed7a5b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/ef3ace84efd77f3eaabaf1c25e87ea993ed7a5b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/6ac7c5cbbf0beed28e51fbea14f6d464d421cc13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:10:13Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:10:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Adopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#10)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d728f93c307ab56080296d9b71d75b82882d6cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/9d728f93c307ab56080296d9b71d75b82882d6cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/6ac7c5cbbf0beed28e51fbea14f6d464d421cc13","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d728f93c307ab56080296d9b71d75b82882d6cd\nparent b63425fcfd145bebf90f47d91ef5e61698c67542\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787706613 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787706613 +0800\n\nAdopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#10)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjjz1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvRkQAJ2An8ouGd1oUra2Je4zUAFF\nCAINC7LQQd4i9Z+ddO88RVyl8FFNZNbIANxK8E60fPY6WLcQ5UvDbh7bQbySfhuA\n1IaXXG6OYkp5ApXUmpFZii5UNIq74rCXlGDH+UdHCSbDV1F5GKROmQOuqb6rUAKw\nDRzuuR8knK3wUVMDs2HMauDv7SQxZhfm8rFuzyJzx/YrkKG38M7U/qDKr7wa7l/x\nAelA2sfW2CFF/G8g0d2ySB7Ry5rWEi8q86xiDSBKp4YT17p+Ch0rgpqNgxUrVMCV\nDHLJf6iUhtXM4WUUX6ybdIgMpaYYvbuaUVt1j6LswP5VAgmvh5cx+L3uKSsR3IOO\nkgUjWveSaJ2NRKOPsX+igCgXWQpjTyTcwiDTy2/PD9ZjLDy+2T33zpXoK8KVAr6r\nnP1Djt6GWbsWG3STvPfr056yQGIDNScjGwptWT2pw2EAGImqD8jFyufEyvA6jh5Q\noOzzKacGZ1oupukqQfUGB9ZPBwiN4q03AhJ94+lReAJwBPJ4BpsqUPBgEm7//jKH\nO36eL0hfruJ3lRv+BGlfL+NYDtBo9mTCwBU1WlO+KRSGwFNwWjltkxTLtf0+AuVx\nnROsI2PX20Zp1Qz1H+FRy6wiv1tdEJ44IYUOmZhoj8+RN7CpeqQUL9deBNhup/nS\nPUnN+4Wr2OgrCfsiAv97\n=1dKq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T01:10:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/6ac7c5cbbf0beed28e51fbea14f6d464d421cc13","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiBcdoAKDZhYzdjNWNiYmYwYmVlZDI4ZTUxZmJlYTE0ZjZkNDY0ZDQyMWNjMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/b63425fcfd145bebf90f47d91ef5e61698c67542","sha":"b63425fcfd145bebf90f47d91ef5e61698c67542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/b63425fcfd145bebf90f47d91ef5e61698c67542"}],"sha":"6ac7c5cbbf0beed28e51fbea14f6d464d421cc13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/6ac7c5cbbf0beed28e51fbea14f6d464d421cc13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/b63425fcfd145bebf90f47d91ef5e61698c67542/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:59:49Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:59:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#9)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"eba5dd5c4455382946c329b97e8b81ccae4d659b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/eba5dd5c4455382946c329b97e8b81ccae4d659b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/b63425fcfd145bebf90f47d91ef5e61698c67542","verification":{"payload":"tree eba5dd5c4455382946c329b97e8b81ccae4d659b\nparent e9725a0ef1938fef4067eb781df1ae766e81b07f\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787673589 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787673589 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#9)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbv1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARsUQAGavXw7G3VK6TAHSQP1ObLSi\nM54ch2n3uWo9G6pZt8l4Y1uD6X1TWbouF6ya09ljMaKpzqE0Esn4HJWS659lyrvi\njcFVvynyiVquI2D8Vv0cRIO5cqkgK3ZVGnpBSWjFgjgKq/WdHFeB/bIBtPj6ijIR\nzTtg9imWw94dKu/HN7g3ZYICnjmgBGbMIWn9y19qNBe1VHxWrF17BKcmHn6u25Gy\nQX0TzlFg4YbzgKh67fq5oN3mUZV7qagWbPuyUGufz70l60Xl3SBwvtHDe1XmVf4L\nveSjOkXiLdS1U585xJcn04QaHU8A25IHs2SjVrpCrAagPymocjaiu5SSsDsajHTN\nPB96JulfiZBjxa3trC5aTv+K6WniuHroCbcOyRnYtgCIBOAsaAtDHTgs5XiE+Ecd\nBVt7N1kgR73Oyqq9RyH0fsFlQJVsLww+azAlNFsEsXhsD7K8Fd3G+O07UFV6YfVS\nWjIcfXVOihED4GHCQj01+G/LYMd47z3IV/tE9dSJ6x6d7e71PvCW9QOFevnzCoJw\nLk53XcmAZyWEEYWxF036QRy435ykx8VcKiX/nWBOwCnixHnEUQxQcatCpJDGpmsN\nzcfbi4ZQ2/7fDkXOzgc3Hen2kggJbDJsljLteJxc7+tNuh/mi0PtJtaBQVwcqWXs\ndGsZe9sQpU9QM093jgwY\n=aOjC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:59:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/b63425fcfd145bebf90f47d91ef5e61698c67542","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiBcdoAKGI2MzQyNWZjZmQxNDViZWJmOTBmNDdkOTFlZjVlNjE2OThjNjc1NDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commit/e9725a0ef1938fef4067eb781df1ae766e81b07f","sha":"e9725a0ef1938fef4067eb781df1ae766e81b07f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/e9725a0ef1938fef4067eb781df1ae766e81b07f"}],"sha":"b63425fcfd145bebf90f47d91ef5e61698c67542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/b63425fcfd145bebf90f47d91ef5e61698c67542"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/commits/e9725a0ef1938fef4067eb781df1ae766e81b07f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:12:38Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:12:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#8)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 493 passed 11 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","tree":{"sha":"f18957771fca90f48518eb65f4fa312b4b39905c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/trees/f18957771fca90f48518eb65f4fa312b4b39905c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/continuous-controls-monitoring/git/commits/e9725a0ef1938fef4067eb781df1ae766e81b07f","verification":{"payload":"tree f18957771fca90f48518eb65f4fa312b4b39905c\nparent 9e79c43ea7ce3699ef1e124f1bd03c08d9e8d16b\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787670758 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787670758 +0800\n\nBind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#8)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 493 passed 11 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbDmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2RMQAAMQTzG2+Nz3cEUxfNHPYNXR\nedQwdrmvEcx9lE0P5acSSb6ULO3JEz6pWvlFYymvhCFjKtmqgsl28Ep7Lmge7srx\nakQvxTGRFp8KSrm2CkKSefq0QL8Ke7BjqIHvhZieuJAQ8EKrZK5bKAa2Lu05UH83\nLb8g7t/pdg7brtTWH7RLUgG/iYHHp7Q8mQtZyJcD9XN9EsgV/d4T/Zm4eDFB0rmF\ns8BA51CSTsxLq71F6FlWWQE+TH3c5o/rtPuv84qmSfv6d3zdb4n6YtmKoCIPecPt\nxlWtCREPPgLsW0tG8ogZyHbdVrzbTHcDif64mrjny+wcSGol3pYek2NhOCl6Hkjk\nFwCaGaWKYyD7pY0oF71iyCRvbqqtxrXd5CTJ3HqRDflEOVae10m55OCpKx5KA1PX\ngW3sjNwbT6ImfB6wafLs+HsvmaB2Pio1dbPH5XV7i1Mwb31WbakgYRdrtvG4qTmn\n4/1dXG1/rbA8lOZ6XU6LI9Nt