subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/internal-audit-lifecycle/commits/11b3cf32ff6cc32f38bf3d9b591e1eecc6037eab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:41:19Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:54:04Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump hex-service-kit to v0.0.11: trace only through the collector\n\nDecision D1: build_tracer refuses an unset OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT instead of\nexporting straight to Cloud Trace around the collector''s GenAI-content redaction, and\ntakes no project argument any more.\n\n- pyproject.toml and the locks: hex-service-kit v0.0.11 (ec2d724). The only other lock\n  movement is opentelemetry-exporter-gcp-trace and its dependencies leaving with the\n  kit''s otel extra, where this repo resolved it.\n- adapters/gcp/tracer.py: build_tracer(service=...) only.\n- tests/contract: the managed tracer''s documented refusal is now\n  CollectorEndpointRequiredError; on-prem keys off a new onprem_refuses field; a new\n  test keeps the old guarantee that with a collector configured and no SDK a span\n  degrades to a no-op.\n- settings, config, Terraform variable and adoption notes stop describing a direct\n  Cloud Trace path that no longer exists.\n\nRelocked without --upgrade: fleet-deps bump-commons'' --upgrade relock moved 0\nunrelated pins here, and those were reverted.","tree":{"sha":"5885d64f1603e2ab2277f6262dc0e75a4c265ee4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/internal-audit-lifecycle/git/trees/5885d64f1603e2ab2277f6262dc0e75a4c265ee4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/internal-audit-lifecycle/git/commits/11b3cf32ff6cc32f38bf3d9b591e1eecc6037eab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/internal-audit-lifecycle/commit/11b3cf32ff6cc32f38bf3d9b591e1eecc6037eab","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCHdoAKDExYjNjZjMyZmY2Y2MzMmYzOGJmM2Q5YjU5MWUxZWVjYzYwMzdlYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/internal-audit-lifecycle/commit/5c661a87b5ca548265647eac1d5a46f881d43316","sha":"5c661a87b5ca548265647eac1d5a46f881d43316","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/internal-audit-lifecycle/commits/5c661a87b5ca548265647eac1d5a46f881d43316"}],"sha":"11b3cf32ff6cc32f38bf3d9b591e1eecc6037eab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/internal-audit-lifecycle/commits/11b3cf32ff6cc32f38bf3d9b591e1eecc6037eab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/internal-audit-lifecycle/commits/5c661a87b5ca548265647eac1d5a46f881d43316/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T04:35:39Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T04:38:50Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Screen both model calls through a fail-closed guardrail port, audited BLOCKED (rule R1)\n\nPhase P3 of the guardrail/registry/observability plan, adopting the fixed design from\nhex-service-template: a GuardrailPort with local (heuristic), gcp (Model Armor) and onprem\n(refusing) bindings, the AUDIT_GUARDRAIL switch, and model_armor.tf.\n\n- domain/screening.py: ScreenedGeneration wraps each generation call. The prompt as sent\n  (plan scope, audit area, every retrieved passage) is screened INPUT before the call, the\n  raw response OUTPUT before it is parsed or grounded, and the screened text is used exactly\n  as given. A refusal, or a guardrail that raises (backend error, deadline, onprem), is\n  audited Decision.BLOCKED with action, direction and reason, never the refused text, and\n  the caller uses its deterministic fallback: narration is optional by design here, so a\n  block never returns a partial or unscreened answer. An audit sink that refuses the record\n  propagates.\n- domain/narration.py, domain/fieldwork.py: both services take the guardrail and audit\n  sink and the verified actor; api/app.py, agent/tools.py and scripts/demo.py pass them.\n- domain/kernel.py: Decision.BLOCKED; GuardrailVerdict refuses allowed-without-text and\n  blocked-with-text; AuditEvent.severity is optional for an unscored working-paper draft.\n- adapters/gcp/guardrail.py: the template''s fixed adapter. The copied one tested a\n  substring of str() over a proto-plus IntEnum (its number on 3.11+) and allowed every\n  prompt; this one allows only NO_MATCH_FOUND with invocation_result SUCCESS, by .name,\n  with model_armor.timeout_seconds on every call. local/onprem adapters match the template.\n- pyproject.toml, requirements-gcp.lock: google-cloud-modelarmor 0.7.1 in the gcp extra.\n- infra/terraform: model_armor.tf gated on model_armor_full_capabilities with\n  template_metadata and ignore_partial_invocation_failures = false, roles/modelarmor.user,\n  the API and perimeter entry, the google-beta provider with its lock entry, the\n  AUDIT_GUARDRAIL env on the service, and tftest runs for both capability settings.\n- scripts/demo.py: a guardrail row in EXIT_CALLS, so the portability tour proves onprem\n  refuses it.\n- tests: the switch''s three states and boot refusal, heuristic block/allow tables, both\n  services'' screening order, injected scope/area/passage refused before the model, output\n  refusals, sanitized text honoured, fail-closed on a raising guardrail, the routes, the\n  SDK-free verdict mirror and the real-enum mapping test.\n- Docs: COMPLIANCE R1, runbook, SPEC, ADOPTING, model card, practices audit, FAQs.","tree":{"sha":"d58daba7b069c2f6ed65e640e3262c5bdd78f117","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/internal-audit-lifecycle/git/trees/d58daba7b069c2f6ed65e640e3262c5bdd78f117"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/internal-audit-lifecycle/g