shawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commit/888c4e34e945c0a0b067e5da421020f9f52ff412","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCc9oAKDg4OGM0ZTM0ZTk0NWMwYTBiMDY3ZTVkYTQyMTAyMGY5ZjUyZmY0MTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commit/e9ecf73ed96a92d801c18e07ebd0e428600c4f88","sha":"e9ecf73ed96a92d801c18e07ebd0e428600c4f88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commits/e9ecf73ed96a92d801c18e07ebd0e428600c4f88"}],"sha":"888c4e34e945c0a0b067e5da421020f9f52ff412","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commits/888c4e34e945c0a0b067e5da421020f9f52ff412"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commits/e9ecf73ed96a92d801c18e07ebd0e428600c4f88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:41:53Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:48:46Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Create the issue landing tables, qualify the query, and serve one book on both sides\n\nThe managed intake could not have run, for two independent reasons.\n\nNothing in infra/terraform/ created any of the five landing tables, no API was\nenabled, no IAM role named BigQuery and no CMEK bound a dataset. And the statement was\nSELECT * FROM `aud1_findings`: an UNQUALIFIED table name against a client built with no\nproject and no default dataset, which BigQuery rejects before it ever looks for the\ntable. So even a hand-created dataset would not have helped. The dataset is\nconfiguration now, three-state, every statement names it, and an empty one makes the\nadapter refuse rather than return an empty tuple, because an empty intake reads as an\ninstitution with no open issues.\n\nA warehouse row has NULLs, never absent keys. The offline fixture omitted a field to\nmake a record schema-invalid, which is a shape BigQuery cannot produce.\ndomain/capa.py::_require reads raw.get(key), so None and missing reach the same refusal\nand the drop-not-default rule holds either way, but only if the book carries the column\nand nulls it. Otherwise the laptop and the deployment drop different sets of records and\nnothing says so. Every shipped row now carries every column, and the book refuses one\nthat omits a key.\n\nThe rows move from a Python dict to src/issue_remediation_capa/data/demo_book/, five\nfiles in the landing tables'' own column order, read by the DuckDB store the offline\nprofiles serve, the loader that fills the dataset, and the tests. Everything is STRING,\nincluding gross_loss: a landing table holds what the feed published and the normalizer\nis what parses it, so a typed column would make the warehouse convert what the laptop\ndoes not.\n\ndemo_book.INVALID_RECORDS names the two records that must stay broken. The\ndrop-not-default rule is the one an offline gate is most likely to prove vacuously:\nwith no invalid record in the book, a normalizer that admitted everything would pass\nevery test. Deleting one now fails the build.\n\nThe book imports nothing from the domain, and is keyed by source VALUE for that reason:\nreaching into domain.capa reaches through ports/__init__ and back, which the loader\nscript hits as a circular import because it imports the book before anything else. A\ntest holds the map against the enum.\n\nThe managed refusal moves from ImportError to RuntimeError: the configuration check runs\nbefore the lazy SDK import. There was nothing to be missing before.\n\nGate green: 509 tests, eval 1.000 on all seven metrics, terraform validate and 14\nterraform tests, docs, demo self-test 8 steps. The qualification guard was watched\nfailing against the shipped statement.","tree":{"sha":"901fe4ab1d80916b243775135d628ef6e268cde9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/git/trees/901fe4ab1d80916b243775135d628ef6e268cde9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/git/commits/e9ecf73ed96a92d801c18e07ebd0e428600c4f88","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commit/e9ecf73ed96a92d801c18e07ebd0e428600c4f88","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCc9oAKGU5ZWNmNzNlZDk2YTkyZDgwMWMxOGUwN2ViZDBlNDI4NjAwYzRmODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commit/1b3bffe77885e13bf5cd90d51808304df9a68569","sha":"1b3bffe77885e13bf5cd90d51808304df9a68569","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commits/1b3bffe77885e13bf5cd90d51808304df9a68569"}],"sha":"e9ecf73ed96a92d801c18e07ebd0e428600c4f88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commits/e9ecf73ed96a92d801c18e07ebd0e428600c4f88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commits/1b3bffe77885e13bf5cd90d51808304df9a68569/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T10:01:16Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:44:21Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the systems this repo depends on, instead of their catalog ids\n\nRepository names are unique across the organization, so a reader no longer has\nto resolve a code through a table to learn which system is meant. The catalog\ndropped its ID column, and this repository follows.\n\nBeyond prose, four identifier changes:\n\n- The review payload''s source_key prefix is the repository name. It is a dedup\n  key -- human-review-console queries on it and the local store makes it a\n  PRIMARY KEY -- so producers and the console have to agree, and the branch\n  carries the migration for rows written under the old prefix.\n- Terraform''s local.render_catalog_id becomes local.render_repository. It feeds\n  display names and descriptions, which update in place.\n- scripts/demo.py''s catalog id is deleted rather than renamed: a REPOSITORY\n  constant and a \"repository\" state key were already there beside it.\n- scripts/rename_fork.py loses --catalog-id, which had nothing left to rewrite.\n\nLines that outgrew the 100-column limit because a name is longer than an id are\nrewrapped rather than shortened by dropping the name. `ruff check`,\n`ruff format --check` and the offline tests are clean.\n\nDeployed resource identifiers are deliberately NOT changed: the Terraform\nname_prefix stems and the Secret Manager secret ids still carry the old\nlowercase id. Those name resources that exist in the deployment, and renaming a\nname_prefix destroys and recreates them, so they are an infrastructure\nmigration rather than a rename.","tree":{"sha":"389d78973cdedd33f0f476fa88503348f236382d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/git/trees/389d78973cdedd33f0f476fa88503348f236382d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/git/commits/1b3bffe77885e13bf5cd90d51808304df9a68569","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commit/1b3bffe77885e13bf5cd90d51808304df9a68569","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCc9oAKDFiM2JmZmU3Nzg4NWUxM2JmNWNkOTBkNTE4MDgzMDRkZjlhNjg1Njk","parents":[{"html_url":"https: