":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/commits/d5325807e9779284631bd4c60ec1316155528d7e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:51:19Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:51:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"e7782219d1aa5775039cd7d03104f5ccae5aaada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/git/trees/e7782219d1aa5775039cd7d03104f5ccae5aaada"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/issue-remediation-capa/git/commits/d5325807e9779284631bd4c60ec1316155528d7e","verification":{"payload":"tree e7782219d1aa5775039cd7d03104f5ccae5aaada\nparent 9a0ef7c6d539c4a5b2c4b1ba1edfc24089dc7e5f\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787673079 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787673079 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbn3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABtgQAJCBbB7bTRJKD/nIpzjFNiI4\nCcnRXwuiNg7E0MrZqxa6vWE4hMFjf1Wg6Xln6OEureO1Adjw+u1uH2VhH5MkHf3e\npK0OoH6EwexqekjlISv7GrEnM9LooxK2LaNNVHuCH6zGwHNM0aVA7r9eFwrcl90N\nYVkXihjvkyP7P+VVg0so7hD+KTvf/3gEiFclm52F4Pd//LN/g8QIZWctRucvD7D9\nDp44HMv+IaS3tU89TRBD7dJgrwh6gX+d6zuixBRz6ZxS90ICR904UhtBbp4wZ7SE\nxk35Sl+UQFQpHvSrksghD8d7qLyuTx4hKNK+ujDv5d9vD