adaa242de072aa995a40f0d133/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:46:32Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:02:07Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump the npm-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 3 updates\n\nBumps the npm-minor-patch group with 3 updates in the /ui directory: [next](https://github.com/vercel/next.js), [@types/node](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/node) and [@types/react-dom](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react-dom).\n\n\nUpdates `next` from 16.3.1 to 16.3.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/compare/v16.3.1...v16.3.3)\n\nUpdates `@types/node` from 26.2.0 to 26.4.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/node)\n\nUpdates `@types/react-dom` from 19.2.4 to 19.2.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react-dom)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@types/node\"\n  dependency-version: 26.3.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react-dom\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.5\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: next\n  dependency-version: 16.3.2\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","tree":{"sha":"aec37ad143ad2b214dbc8024b310a1e219f558a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/trees/aec37ad143ad2b214dbc8024b310a1e219f558a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/commits/cd5ea818d8ed11adaa242de072aa995a40f0d133","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/cd5ea818d8ed11adaa242de072aa995a40f0d133","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCxtoAKGNkNWVhODE4ZDhlZDExYWRhYTI0MmRlMDcyYWE5OTVhNDBmMGQxMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/904ac036a56d85763205e0fb49a23f026ba57e10","sha":"904ac036a56d85763205e0fb49a23f026ba57e10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/904ac036a56d85763205e0fb49a23f026ba57e10"}],"sha":"cd5ea818d8ed11adaa242de072aa995a40f0d133","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/cd5ea818d8ed11adaa242de072aa995a40f0d133"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/904ac036a56d85763205e0fb49a23f026ba57e10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:17:09Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:17:18Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Stop next dev writing a second working agreement into ui/\n\n`next dev` generates `ui/AGENTS.md` and `ui/CLAUDE.md` and leaves them behind.\nThe catalog''s convention is that AGENTS.md is the working agreement and it is\nthe ONLY one, with no tool-specific alias, and this repo already carries its own\nat the root: the generated pair is a second agreement plus exactly the alias\nthe convention forbids. The generated prose also contains an em-dash, which\n`make docs-check` fails on.\n\nNeither file had reached this tree yet, so this shuts the door first.\nDeleting them by hand does not hold either, because the next `next dev` writes\nthem again. This is a template defect, not a per-repo one.\n\n`agentRules` is a top-level NextConfig option in the pinned next 16.3.x, not an\nexperimental one (config-shared.d.ts, default true; the writer is\nserver/lib/generate-agent-files.js, called behind an isDev check, which is why\nthe CI production build never surfaced it). Setting it false in\nui/next.config.mjs turns the generation off at the source.\n\nThe guard lives in\n`tests/unit/test_ui_surface.py`\nand has two halves. Asserting the flag catches its removal; asserting both\nfiles are ABSENT catches a framework bump that renames or drops the option,\nwhich the flag assertion alone would sail straight through.\n\nSame change as hex-service-template PR 15, which carries the proof: a repo\nrendered, installed and started on the same next version with agent detection\non, before and after. Before, both files and the generation line in the log;\nafter, neither. Verified here by this repo''s own offline gate.","tree":{"sha":"cc3b19dbac4cdc6768d60777f93157a983ed64e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/trees/cc3b19dbac4cdc6768d60777f93157a983ed64e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/commits/904ac036a56d85763205e0fb49a23f026ba57e10","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/904ac036a56d85763205e0fb49a23f026ba57e10","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCxtoAKDkwNGFjMDM2YTU2ZDg1NzYzMjA1ZTBmYjQ5YTIzZjAyNmJhNTdlMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/c5d647722c945b7cae120b48b707732fac36faf4","sha":"c5d647722c945b7cae120b48b707732fac36faf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/c5d647722c945b7cae120b48b707732fac36faf4"}],"sha":"904ac036a56d85763205e0fb49a23f026ba57e10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/904ac036a56d85763205e0fb49a23f026ba57e10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/c5d647722c945b7cae120b48b707732fac36faf4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:44:20Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:51:05Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Let mypy see the Google SDKs it had been resolving to nothing\n\nThe hosted `lint_gcp` job type-checks this tree against its RUNTIME lock, which is the only\ncheck in the fleet that can see the cloud adapters at all: the offline gate installs the dev\nlock, which carries no Google Cloud SDK, so mypy resolved `google.*` to nothing and reported\nnothing about the code that talks to the cloud. That job has been **non-blocking** since\n2026-08-30 while its findings were worked through. It is blocking now, and this is the\nrepository half of that promotion.\n\n**What was left before this could happen was upstream typing, and the answer is MORE type\nchecking rather than a suppression.** Two settings, in this repository''s own `pyproject.toml`\nrather than in the CI runner:\n\n* **`follow_untyped_imports = true`, scoped to `google.*`.** mypy now ANALYSES a dependency\n  that ships no `py.typed` instead of skipping it. Measured rather than argued: a bogus method\n  planted on a `google.cloud.storage` client is reported by **nothing** under the old\n  configuration and is an `attr-defined` error under this one -- the same defect class that\n  turned out to be real in `disputes-chargebacks-manager`, which called a `SessionsClient`\n  method that does not exist.\n* **`untyped_calls_exclude = [\"google\"]`.** This drops one complaint -- *\"this callee has no\n  annotations\"* -- and nothing else. `disallow_untyped_calls` exists to stop typed code calling\n  OUR untyped code; aimed at a third-party release it is a demand no work in this repository can\n  satisfy, and proto-plus generates every message `__init__` without annotations. Falsified\n  before it was trusted: with the exclusion in place, a planted nonexistent method still reports\n  `attr-defined` and a planted wrong argument type still reports `arg-type` naming the real\n  expected type.\n\n**They live here and not in the runner on purpose.** Two checks reading different configuration\nis what produced the one-line contradiction that blocked this promotion for a day: in\n`human-review-console` a `# type: ignore` was REQUIRED by the offline gate and reported UNUSED by\nlint-gcp. The offline gate and the hosted job now read the same `[tool.mypy]` and differ only in\nwhich packages are installed, which is the property the SDK declaration in this file already\nexisted to hold.\n\n**The scope on `follow_untyped_imports` is not tidiness.** Set globally it also follows the 3.14\nstandard library, where mypy 2.3.1 cannot parse CPython''s own `annotationlib.py`: `agent-registry`\nreported `Invalid syntax` in a standard-library file and **checked nothing at all**. That was\nfound by running all fifty-two trees rather than the three the shape had been validated on.\n`google.protobuf.*` is then excluded from following INSIDE that scope, because a generated `_pb2`\nmodule builds its classes at import time through a descriptor builder, so mypy reading the source\nreports `Module has no attribute \"Timestamp\"` for a class that plainly exists.\n\n**The mypy floor was legacy and is raised to `>=2.3.1`.** `>=1.10` was not neutral: both settings\nabove arrived in mypy 1.14, so the floor permitted a resolution that would not understand the\nfile configuring it. The lock already pins `mypy==2.3.1`, so this was latent rather than live.\n\nWhat this tree reports now, both checks, cold cache:\n\n| check | environment | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lint_gcp` | runtime lock (`requirements-gcp.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 56 source files` |\n| offline gate | dev lock (`requirements-dev.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 56 source files` |\n\nGate:  474 passed, 1 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"1f7d401cbdcf91d5e4d2679a3a48fd3fae855307","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/trees/1f7d401cbdcf91d5e4d2679a3a48fd3fae855307"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/commits/c5d647722c945b7cae120b48b707732fac36faf4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/c5d647722c945b7cae120b48b707732fac36faf4","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCxtoAKGM1ZDY0NzcyMmM5NDViN2NhZTEyMGI0OGI3MDc3MzJmYWMzNmZhZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/b1cfdd6471dc251a17f4dc859a5c724c780f9c00","sha":"b1cfdd6471dc251a17f4dc859a5c724c780f9c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/b1cfdd6471dc251a17f4dc859a5c724c780f9c00"}],"sha":"c5d647722c945b7cae120b48b707732fac36faf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/c5d647722c945b7cae120b48b707732fac36faf4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/b1cfdd6471dc251a17f4dc859a5c724c780f9c00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T03:55:39Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:04:59Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Read the managed model id from where each service actually keeps it\n\nThe provenance banner resolved the managed model id from a constant declared on the\nbound adapter, and **twenty-five of thirty-eight trees answered `managed-model-unnamed`**.\n\nReading them showed the resolver was looking in the wrong place rather than the trees being\nsilent. Most of the fleet pins the id in SETTINGS, under a name chosen per repository:\n`models.reasoning`, `narrator_model`, `generation_model`, `narration_model`, `drafting_model`.\nOne kept it as a literal inside the model call. Twelve bind a managed adapter that is a\ndeployment-wired placeholder and raises rather than generating, so there is no model to name.\n\n`_GENERATOR_MODEL_ATTR` now names that settings path once per tree, beside `_GENERATOR_PORT`,\nand the resolver reads it before falling back to an adapter constant. The banner reads the same\nvalue the adapter passes to the model call rather than a second copy that drifts.\n\nThis tree keeps no settings field for it, so the adapter constant and the placeholder branch decide the answer.\n\nWhat this tree now reports:\n\n| profile | `runtime` | `generator_model` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `local` | `local` | `no-model` |\n| `gcp` | `gcp` | `no-model` |\n| `onprem` | `local` | `no-model` |\n\n**Two answers replace the placeholder, because they say different things.**\n`managed-not-implemented` means the managed path refuses rather than generating.\n`managed-model-unset` means the settings field exists and this deployment has not pinned a\nmodel — actionable, and different from a repository that names none. `managed-model-unnamed`\nsurvives only as a defensive fallback and **no tree reaches it any more.**\n\n**`managed-not-implemented` is the only answer that is INFERRED rather than read, so it\nis the only one that can be wrong**, and it now has a guard: a tree claiming it must not call a\nmodel API. That guard took three attempts, and each failure was found by falsifying rather than\nby reading:\n\n1. Asserting the adapter \"raises\" passed a deliberately broken `soc-fraud-fusion`, which\n   generates and also raises on bad input. Too weak.\n2. It had already let a real mis-classification through. **`conversation-qa-scorecard` calls\n   `generate_content`** and raises only when its model is unconfigured; it had been grouped with\n   the placeholders on the strength of that raise. Its model is named now, and its banner reports\n   `gemini-3.5-flash` instead of claiming the path is unimplemented.\n3. The check read the DEFAULT profile, where the answer is the offline stub, so it returned\n   before checking anything and passed the broken tree again. It reads the managed profile now.\n\nFalsified in both directions at the end: clearing `soc-fraud-fusion`''s settings path makes it\nfail with *\"reports managed-not-implemented but calls ''generate_content''\"*, and restoring it\nclears it.\n\nGate: 474 passed, 1 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"f06b1680f5ef287528f6fc00d8bf377b9117a621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/trees/f06b1680f5ef287528f6fc00d8bf377b9117a621"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/commits/b1cfdd6471dc251a17f4dc859a5c724c780f9c00","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/b1cfdd6471dc251a17f4dc859a5c724c780f9c00","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCxtoAKGIxY2ZkZDY0NzFkYzI1MWExN2Y0ZGM4NTlhNWM3MjRjNzgwZjljMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/180b29ae49d317e8613ccba57d7b1fa5fd95ac22","sha":"180b29ae49d317e8613ccba57d7b1fa5fd95ac22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/180b29ae49d317e8613ccba57d7b1fa5fd95ac22"}],"sha":"b1cfdd6471dc251a17f4dc859a5c724c780f9c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/b1cfdd6471dc251a17f4dc859a5c724c780f9c00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/180b29ae49d317e8613ccba57d7b1fa5fd95ac22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T02:28:26Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T02:35:01Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"State where this console runs and which model answers, on every page\n\nEvery served console now names, at the top of every page, WHERE it is running and\nWHICH model answers. That is the org decision of 2026-08-30, and this tree is one of the\nthirty-eight that had not adopted it.\n\n**Not cosmetic.** These systems are demonstrated on a laptop and on a deployment, sometimes\nin the same hour, and a screenshot of one is indistinguishable from the other. A viewer who\ncannot tell which they are looking at cannot tell whether what they are reading came from a\nmanaged model or from a deterministic offline stub, and that is exactly the confusion an\naudit-first pitch cannot afford. The page says it, always, instead of the presenter saying\nit sometimes.\n\n**Both halves come from the service, on `/healthz`.** Nothing in the browser infers either.\nA console that read its own runtime from `window.location` would be right until the day the\ndeployment served through a proxy, and wrong silently after that.\n\nWhat this tree now reports:\n\n| profile | `runtime` | `generator_model` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `local` | `local` | `no-model` |\n| `gcp` | `gcp` | `no-model` |\n| `onprem` | `local` | `no-model` |\n\n**`generator_model` is read off the BINDING, not kept as a second settings string.** A\nsettings field would be a claim ABOUT the binding, and the two drift the first time somebody\nrebinds a profile without remembering the second field. `_GENERATOR_PORT` names the port\nwhose active binding decides the answer, so rebinding it changes the banner in the same edit.\n\nThis service binds no generative port at all, so every profile answers `no-model` -- which is\ndeliberately NOT `deterministic-offline-stub`. The stub string claims a model-shaped port\nbound to a stub; this service has no such port.\n\n**The vocabulary distinguishes four things that are genuinely different**, because a reviewer\napproving an escalation is entitled to know which one they are reading:\n`deterministic-offline-stub` (a model-shaped port bound to a stub), `no-model` (no such port\nexists at all), `onprem-not-implemented` (the port exists and refuses), and a real model id.\n`runtime` states where the PROCESS runs, so `onprem` reads `local` -- a managed model call\ndoes not make a process cloud-hosted.\n\n`tests/unit/test_provenance_banner_contract.py` asserts agreement with the profile rather\nthan mere presence, because a banner that is present and wrong is worse than none: it turns\n\"the viewer does not know\" into \"the viewer has been told the wrong thing\". Falsified rather\nthan assumed -- making an offline profile report a Gemini id fails it with *\"the ''local''\nprofile reports ''gemini-3.5-flash'', which reads as a managed model answering a request that\nnever left the machine\"*, and reverting clears it.\n\nThe component and the `.provenance-banner` style are copied from the render-verified\n`hex-service-template`, and it is mounted in the LAYOUT rather than in a page: \"at the top of\nevery page\" is a property of the console, and a page that forgot it would be the one a\nscreenshot came from.\n\nGate: 472 passed, 1 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"1b8dc49463e9e0019bae1355ccbbc2651dc09e4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/trees/1b8dc49463e9e0019bae1355ccbbc2651dc09e4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/commits/180b29ae49d317e8613ccba57d7b1fa5fd95ac22","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/180b29ae49d317e8613ccba57d7b1fa5fd95ac22","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCxtoAKDE4MGIyOWFlNDlkMzE3ZTg2MTNjY2JhNTdkN2IxZmE1ZmQ5NWFjMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/414919a0e80de1b2e6a15179b4ca5ab7301a1805","sha":"414919a0e80de1b2e6a15179b4ca5ab7301a1805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/414919a0e80de1b2e6a15179b4ca5ab7301a1805"}],"sha":"180b29ae49d317e8613ccba57d7b1fa5fd95ac22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/180b29ae49d317e8613ccba57d7b1fa5fd95ac22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/414919a0e80de1b2e6a15179b4ca5ab7301a1805/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:17:42Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:38:41Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Adopt hex-service-kit v0.0.6\n\nThe 0.0.6 identity knobs -- machine_tenants, subject_from, refuse_unmapped_tenant and a\nhuman-subject allowlist -- have been released and unadopted since 2026-08-28. Every one\ndefaults to what this repository already does, so this bump is the version move and\nnothing else: no behaviour changes until an adopter says so.\n\nThe lockfiles pin the 40-character commit the tag resolved to, not the tag, so what\ninstalls cannot change without a diff.","tree":{"sha":"e2477b881de23fe2f0b09af6255b5db52db12fc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/trees/e2477b881de23fe2f0b09af6255b5db52db12fc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/commits/414919a0e80de1b2e6a15179b4ca5ab7301a1805","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/414919a0e80de1b2e6a15179b4ca5ab7301a1805","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCxtoAKDQxNDkxOWEwZTgwZGUxYjJlNmExNTE3OWI0Y2E1YWI3MzAxYTE4MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/a5556bfaae22bfff30287972171c0d856153b5b7","sha":"a5556bfaae22bfff30287972171c0d856153b5b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/a5556bfaae22bfff30287972171c0d856153b5b7"}],"sha":"414919a0e80de1b2e6a15179b4ca5ab7301a1805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/414919a0e80de1b2e6a15179b4ca5ab7301a1805"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/a5556bfaae22bfff30287972171c0d856153b5b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T08:56:39Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T09:30:44Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the platform environment variables for what they are\n\nThe HRZ_ prefix is a retired catalog code. It named nothing an operator could look up:\nHRZ_HUMAN_REVIEW_URL, HRZ7_S2S_TOKEN and HRZ_REGISTRY_* say which internal identifier a\nservice used to carry, not which service they address. The names now say that directly --\nHUMAN_REVIEW_URL, HUMAN_REVIEW_S2S_TOKEN, AGENT_REGISTRY_*, KNOWLEDGE_BASE_URL,\nGUARDRAIL_GATEWAY_URL, QUALITY_GATE_URL, OBSERVABILITY_URL, AUDIT_URL -- so a\n`.env` file can be read without the catalog open beside it.\n\nNothing about the wire contract changes; these are the names of the values, not the\nvalues. Two repositories that had gone their own way (a repo-scoped review-console URL,\na second spelling of the knowledge-base URL) join the fleet-standard names rather than\nkeeping a private variant with the code stripped out.\n\nThe review-kit call site now names the credential environment variables EXPLICITLY\ninstead of inheriting the kit''s defaults. review-kit is a commit-pinned git dependency,\nso its defaults are frozen at the pinned version: leaving them implicit would mean this\nrepository could not rename its own environment variables without a coordinated release\nof the kit and a pin bump here. Renaming the variables while relying on those defaults\nwould have failed closed at run time -- the operator sets the new name, the pinned kit\nreads the old one, and the submission goes out unauthenticated or is refused.","tree":{"sha":"b5fb9f133e23ed7db85ea34277772ef76f8dcd13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/trees/b5fb9f133e23ed7db85ea34277772ef76f8dcd13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/commits/a5556bfaae22bfff30287972171c0d856153b5b7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/a5556bfaae22bfff30287972171c0d856153b5b7","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCxtoAKGE1NTU2YmZhYWUyMmJmZmYzMDI4Nzk3MjE3MWMwZDg1NjE1M2I1Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/2a8200f9bdce9dd00bf3af187f694e4c28f7d3eb","sha":"2a8200f9bdce9dd00bf3af187f694e4c28f7d3eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/2a8200f9bdce9dd00bf3af187f694e4c28f7d3eb"}],"sha":"a5556bfaae22bfff30287972171c0d856153b5b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/a5556bfaae22bfff30287972171c0d856153b5b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/2a8200f9bdce9dd00bf3af187f694e4c28f7d3eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:54:23Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:59:53Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: hex-service-kit v0.0.5","tree":{"sha":"8235dc6fd294ec8b3510c0e0a14d5351953c9ca7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/trees/8235dc6fd294ec8b3510c0e0a14d5351953c9ca7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/commits/2a8200f9bdce9dd00bf3af187f694e4c28f7d3eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/2a8200f9bdce9dd00bf3af187f694e4c28f7d3eb","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCxtoAKDJhODIwMGY5YmRjZTlkZDAwYmYzYWYxODdmNjk0ZTRjMjhmN2QzZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/386a687d4e4899368c2bb9439e2835202bb84dd0","sha":"386a687d4e4899368c2bb9439e2835202bb84dd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/386a687d4e4899368c2bb9439e2835202bb84dd0"}],"sha":"2a8200f9bdce9dd00bf3af187f694e4c28f7d3eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/2a8200f9bdce9dd00bf3af187f694e4c28f7d3eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/386a687d4e4899368c2bb9439e2835202bb84dd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:11:26Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:11:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Adopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#14)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a638be810735f58d8c232ade668e0641f8e8070","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/trees/7a638be810735f58d8c232ade668e0641f8e8070"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/commits/386a687d4e4899368c2bb9439e2835202bb84dd0","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a638be810735f58d8c232ade668e0641f8e8070\nparent eaeea09fef34d2799a830231a1946e1052c108dd\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787706686 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787706686 +0800\n\nAdopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#14)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjj0+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACOAQAD5k3mKf1YPKQbw72aSbk+vI\nqzxMmh9l5nkd2Ekbjei0dHrE3naQdrauiM+MV2CS67tmIyWJ3p3EhV6efT/4bEq3\njqGZ3xlZViFbw2lY3Z7cZR/jdXt4gKzmIpA2ha7+NOrxhynD8IEtDOZm3wfn8coC\nleVGZnktW7QPANJZb0a5aOp2VZRm3ZCW2PM3u3sr4MbPdbPxzJYgJCIgoFRjXEFk\nbu2N03jBeiyuK8G3iVzTWeXMOe3IfnKt3lW7SGG6nG/3SMJnu0hUgqJ0pgV4w0yA\nEoxdF975LKdB5ccwd4Rnstq0Rs7JUquFSaZY5vlqbic1Bi2A8j6oBDOOBgLA4E+P\nExuPZtnSKfXJg3E0CIlah+4YKBtTNtNTFDfNwg9RHc8FnHpTEookvKtwwWoUNEFK\nPLez9dp4mh+wKer6BiYvt/cUz+JJJH5LQGwoc3DaGOuwJOnyewGSKOSBXm3+1Ciq\n4aMjL4V7/FSkD+VhSyh+qaamCiGpCyV1r5PXNbVtSTeRWXBSqXF28zTsQoaBMu10\n8e9f9WQcMjv/sg3lmA8qC8+KCls8TV8K3G0Ndd5HqCJgxVg9dCLZObXNkMdFrv16\nF9OYfz+i4gBmedvp9AfhCT+2yxRmVieKVckYNLalKXIhP3ezhxopVBfa2MhZxYz3\n++sH2uSKr+m7Liwn1H9H\n=zbBN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T01:11:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/386a687d4e4899368c2bb9439e2835202bb84dd0","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiCxtoAKDM4NmE2ODdkNGU0ODk5MzY4YzJiYjk0MzllMjgzNTIwMmJiODRkZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commit/eaeea09fef34d2799a830231a1946e1052c108dd","sha":"eaeea09fef34d2799a830231a1946e1052c108dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/eaeea09fef34d2799a830231a1946e1052c108dd"}],"sha":"386a687d4e4899368c2bb9439e2835202bb84dd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/386a687d4e4899368c2bb9439e2835202bb84dd0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/commits/eaeea09fef34d2799a830231a1946e1052c108dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:47:15Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:47:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"782a2445de0e68798845d4066baed82f0dd815ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/trees/782a2445de0e68798845d4066baed82f0dd815ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/model-risk-validation/git/commits/eaeea09fef34d2799a830231a1946e1052c108dd","verification":{"payload":"tree 782a2445de0e68798845d4066baed82f0dd815ba\nparent c5ec38fabf447a8d65fe18825b97ac460d05e51c\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672835 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672835 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbkDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcbkQAEbDzLMsgNp1qEuuIO8LefCl\nX/WpMyA9nQcE/0VTzbkKvQbbm1oNOq+InxyLmn/5Ycdsx2dXWmk0y1JrnadDnITA\n7uNgd0QEy5EwHYjs1NkN0fGPLxQf6w6ZhgFQDUffKvXASciS6HkrIhlm477c8Voq\nXGSttUzRygMTcAVR2svad4OmmZ0X4fyf02iTjURyRRAfMU92evzIsoX4NzemJHm3\nu8N1I7qZwDwYxZ1Np+XgI+e1evThrgz1bOc+Z3J68HRmV08ThImWqD99xWiDVUe4\n20LHidHWKZ8zW2xoM6HCL0+ILMmPyXboNB/kF1T7xLSnYt/8WFufoWuES1VpgZnT\nYuAB4ay9pC5BahyxjRgIZ1gbgv2vMJp1YBpZDfKRss8teQXIA3VT11gzuPzxyJ9/\nVwfDNYRhj01EG4PBq+ezgLDXleSQEIE2Tg1KcoMpu3ve8l5GwUqc4s1iX+Ler+lR\nAyQgTnm9/Adcdr5oWcKY75nLI67r7To3NK7EfTizSi9FlHQg8CuSJoTl8etnTsIw\npGpHQEhmRNISzAljhZqGIzXTc98YCfwcFf9TlGa1Xyr7djHEZh0bIrTnwpM3c17N\n9e3nSsu5kuznr+mVkPhp0SD/KVumY6DKV+FubvTgHedoeUVI79D7hI5mqnICt7Zq\nP8lth/LOmzr286eeibyd\n=uGDz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:47:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","o