s://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/9ea29b41178f521304f263962d5726fe9de29e86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:29:40Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T21:53:52Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Drop the dark-scheme pill override: this console stays light\n\n- The template''s prefers-color-scheme block inverts the pills for a dark\n  page, but this console''s page never goes dark. Under a dark OS scheme it\n  showed the configured pill solid and the answered one faint on the light\n  page, reversing what the two styles mean (measured in a browser on\n  sanctions-screening). The .model-pills comment now says why there is no\n  override.","tree":{"sha":"933852d5be40444eaf5b01e57f19fb43ae89336a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/trees/933852d5be40444eaf5b01e57f19fb43ae89336a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/commits/9ea29b41178f521304f263962d5726fe9de29e86","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/9ea29b41178f521304f263962d5726fe9de29e86","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiDctoAKDllYTI5YjQxMTc4ZjUyMTMwNGYyNjM5NjJkNTcyNmZlOWRlMjllODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/5802500106d5f2b847a4fa4b20a55d19b6f95fc8","sha":"5802500106d5f2b847a4fa4b20a55d19b6f95fc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/5802500106d5f2b847a4fa4b20a55d19b6f95fc8"}],"sha":"9ea29b41178f521304f263962d5726fe9de29e86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/9ea29b41178f521304f263962d5726fe9de29e86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/5802500106d5f2b847a4fa4b20a55d19b6f95fc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:26:53Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T21:53:52Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Show the model that answered as two pills, not a banner, on hex-service-kit v0.0.10\n\nOwner decision 2026-09-23: every console shows two small pills at the top\nright, the model that ANSWERED and Search when an online search tool was\nused, in place of the full-width provenance banner that named what\nconfiguration would call.\n\n- pyproject: hex-service-kit v0.0.10 (0e71fc7), both lockfiles relocked; no\n  other pin moved.\n- api/app.py installs install_answer_provenance(app), so X-Answered-By and\n  X-Search-Used carry whatever the model adapters note.\n- The local generation stub notes config.OFFLINE_STUB_MODEL\n  (\"deterministic-offline-stub\"), the one spelling generator_model, the\n  /healthz default and the stub''s GenerationResponse.model now share (the\n  response said \"local-stub\" before). POST /v1/tolerance, which narrates the\n  proposal''s justification, therefore answers X-Answered-By offline. The\n  managed Gemini adapter is a deploy-time placeholder that raises before any\n  model answers, so it notes nothing; Document AI extraction is not a model\n  and notes nothing either.\n- Sampling: the one generation call site narrates, so it stays free. The\n  request type has no temperature field and none is added, because no real\n  adapter sends one.\n- config.py: the hard-reasoning branch is deleted from the model resolver.\n  generator_model names the setting the managed adapter reads, never a\n  model a flag swaps in while the adapter calls another.\n- ui/app/ModelPills.tsx replaces ProvenanceBanner.tsx in layout.tsx: the\n  configured generator_model from /healthz, dimmed, until an answer names\n  the model that answered; Search only while that answer searched. One\n  window.fetch wrapper (lib/answer-provenance.mjs, node-tested) reads both\n  headers; the proxy route now forwards them. The banner CSS is deleted.\n- CONTRIBUTING row 5c: a new model port notes its model and any search it\n  attached, and makes temperature optional, pinned only for extraction,\n  classification and scoring, omitted (not 1.0) elsewhere.\n- tests: test_answer_provenance.py (the stub names itself on the real\n  route and matches /healthz; a noting fake yields both headers and does\n  not leak into the next request; narration sends no temperature; no flag\n  moves generator_model), the pills contract in test_ui_surface.py, and the\n  banner contract renamed to test_model_pills_contract.py.","tree":{"sha":"6c12c95ec50fecd66d59bcedb509f3907116bc70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/trees/6c12c95ec50fecd66d59bcedb509f3907116bc70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/commits/5802500106d5f2b847a4fa4b20a55d19b6f95fc8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"http