"date":"2026-09-25T03:47:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Correct docs that say the review router refuses at request time\n\nThe service now refuses to boot under the managed profile when review\nrouting is on and HUMAN_REVIEW_URL is unset, RESILIENCE_REVIEW_ROUTING switches\nrouting, and a hand-off that fails at request time is reported as\nreview_routing \"failed\" and logged. Some documents still said the\nmanaged router refuses the escalation at request time rather than\nswallowing it, and .env.example named no switch. Routing off needs no console.\nDocumentation only; no practices-audit verdict changed.","tree":{"sha":"5572ead5c4fda458b2ca72d3a43bae7bd100eb10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/trees/5572ead5c4fda458b2ca72d3a43bae7bd100eb10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/commits/20281c9e0884333c033aa4fbddefc42065cdc28b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/20281c9e0884333c033aa4fbddefc42065cdc28b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiDctoAKDIwMjgxYzllMDg4NDMzM2MwMzNhYTRmYmRkZWZjNDIwNjVjZGMyOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/3c4bf1d48388f80f1372d0f88bc9b0a1e53627d6","sha":"3c4bf1d48388f80f1372d0f88bc9b0a1e53627d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/3c4bf1d48388f80f1372d0f88bc9b0a1e53627d6"}],"sha":"20281c9e0884333c033aa4fbddefc42065cdc28b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/20281c9e0884333c033aa4fbddefc42065cdc28b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/3c4bf1d48388f80f1372d0f88bc9b0a1e53627d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:26:46Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:29:21Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Correct the review-routing comments to the boot refusal\n\nThe variables.tf header and the review_url comment in settings.yaml still\nsaid the managed review router refuses to swallow an escalation when\nHUMAN_REVIEW_URL is empty. Since the runtime control switches landed that\nis false: the service refuses at BOOT when review routing is on and no console\nis named, and RESILIENCE_REVIEW_ROUTING=false switches routing off, so\nhuman_review_url is only required with review_routing_enabled on.\n\nComment-only; no behaviour changes.","tree":{"sha":"aebfc9e020bd866d3e271364175795dbddd1484e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/trees/aebfc9e020bd866d3e271364175795dbddd1484e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/commits/3c4bf1d48388f80f1372d0f88bc9b0a1e53627d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/3c4bf1d48388f80f1372d0f88bc9b0a1e53627d6","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiDctoAKDNjNGJmMWQ0ODM4OGY4MGYxMzcyZDBmODhiYzliMGExZTUzNjI3ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/98c55a15b2a1f5a84bbbe24609122f4fa0936409","sha":"98c55a15b2a1f5a84bbbe24609122f4fa0936409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/98c55a15b2a1f5a84bbbe24609122f4fa0936409"}],"sha":"3c4bf1d48388f80f1372d0f88bc9b0a1e53627d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/3c4bf1d48388f80f1372d0f88bc9b0a1e53627d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/98c55a15b2a1f5a84bbbe24609122f4fa0936409/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:06:56Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:19:33Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Wire the console to the real tolerance call\n\nThe console posted {subject, text} to POST /v1/triage, which this service does not serve: its\none consequential route is POST /v1/tolerance taking ToleranceRequest {scope, service_id,\nservice_name, regulator, document_ids}. Every submit was a 404 and the console could never\nproduce a resilience map or an impact-tolerance proposal.\n\nIt now posts that request, prefilled with the fictional important business service the local\nprofile maps (ibs-retail-payments, \"Retail Payments (FICTIONAL)\", scope projects/fictional,\ndocument doc-settlement-runbook), with the regulator offered as a select of the three values\nthe Regulator enum accepts (APRA_CPS230, DORA, UK_OPRES) rather than free text the service\nwould refuse with a 422. The default submission returns 200 with four tolerances, routed to\nthe review console.\n\ntests/unit/test_console_matches_api.py reads every fetch(API + ...) in ui/app/ and holds it\nagainst the live route table: path and method served, every required field sent, no field\nthe model silently drops. It failed against the old console (POST /v1/triage is not served)\nand passes against this one.","tree":{"sha":"93bac8097a8627c5f9801c3ab34dbeec23818359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/trees/93bac8097a8627c5f9801c3ab34dbeec23818359"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/commits/98c55a15b2a1f5a84bbbe24609122f4fa0936409","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/98c55a15b2a1f5a84bbbe24609122f4fa0936409","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiDctoAKDk4YzU1YTE1YjJhMWY1YTg0YmJiZTI0NjA5MTIyZjRmYTA5MzY0MDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/adced3b859abb95908a372dcd7d96ef42e67e9aa","sha":"adced3b859abb95908a372dcd7d96ef42e67e9aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/adced3b859abb95908a372dcd7d96ef42e67e9aa"}],"sha":"98c55a15b2a1f5a84bbbe24609122f4fa0936409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/98c55a15b2a1f5a84bbbe24609122f4fa0936409"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/adced3b859abb95908a372dcd7d96ef42e67e9aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:26:44Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:29:05Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Switch review routing, refuse at boot without a console, and report every hand-off\n\nThe fleet''s runtime-control contract, template shape (as aml-alert-triage). Review routing is\nthe one cheap runtime control this service has, so it is the one switch.\n\n- RESILIENCE_REVIEW_ROUTING is read once at settings load in three states: unset is on, a\n  boolean wins, emptied or unrecognised refuses at boot. Off binds a disabled router and logs\n  one warning per process, however many containers the agent tools build.\n- Under gcp, routing on with no HUMAN_REVIEW_URL refuses at boot. It used to surface as a 500\n  on the first tolerance proposal, after the proposal had already been audited.\n- The studio routes inside the domain, so build_studio takes an optional recording router,\n  and every caller that proposes tolerances (the tolerance route, the assess_resilience tool\n  and the tolerance CLI command) passes one. A failed hand-off no longer fails the request:\n  the result carries review_routing (routed, failed, off, not_required) and an empty\n  review_ref, and the failure is logged. The domain is unchanged.\n- Terraform gains review_routing_enabled, sets the service''s switch from it, and relaxes the\n  edge''s console requirement only when routing is stated off; a new plan test holds that.\n- The docs that said the managed router refuses at request time now say the service refuses\n  at boot and reports the hand-off.\n- pii-kit masking here protects the audit trail, tool results and the review payload rather\n  than a user''s free-text question, so it is not the redaction control the contract\n  switches, and it gains no switch.","tree":{"sha":"7f7dc5778ceb33438c07cbdb81266ed77b61274c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/trees/7f7dc5778ceb33438c07cbdb81266ed77b61274c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/commits/adced3b859abb95908a372dcd7d96ef42e67e9aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/adced3b859abb95908a372dcd7d96ef42e67e9aa","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiDctoAKGFkY2VkM2I4NTlhYmI5NTkwOGEzNzJkY2Q3ZDk2ZWY0MmU2N2U5YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/ead9a18baf3a7e1338356c35f10f657f13152185","sha":"ead9a18baf3a7e1338356c35f10f657f13152185","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/ead9a18baf3a7e1338356c35f10f657f13152185"}],"sha":"adced3b859abb95908a372dcd7d96ef42e67e9aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/adced3b859abb95908a372dcd7d96ef42e67e9aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/ead9a18baf3a7e1338356c35f10f657f13152185/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T03:50:59Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T04:08:10Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Take the default off the audit bucket lock\n\nworm_locked defaulted to true, so the first apply of this stack in any\nproject locked its audit bucket irreversibly for the whole retention window,\nwith nothing in that deployment''s own tfvars saying so. The fleet decided on\n2026-09-12 that an irreversible control takes no default; this stack was one\nof 33 that sweep never reached.\n\nA plan now refuses until the deployment states the lock. The Terraform tests\nstate it once per file in the production form, still assert that a stated\nlock sits on the six-month floor, and gain a run proving the unlocked posture\ncreates an unlocked bucket. That run fails if the lock is ever hard-coded\nback into the bucket, which every other run would miss.","tree":{"sha":"23ef2a8d47c61856b64a4952e4999e744c262aa2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/trees/23ef2a8d47c61856b64a4952e4999e744c262aa2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/git/commits/ead9a18baf3a7e1338356c35f10f657f13152185","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/ead9a18baf3a7e1338356c35f10f657f13152185","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiDctoAKGVhZDlhMThiYWYzYTdlMTMzODM1NmMzNWYxMGY2NTdmMTMxNTIxODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commit/6f26fa7e6c36f84944ecd89f295bfcc3fcae11bb","sha":"6f26fa7e6c36f84944ecd89f295bfcc3fcae11bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/6f26fa7e6c36f84944ecd89f295bfcc3fcae11bb"}],"sha":"ead9a18baf3a7e1338356c35f10f657f13152185","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/ead9a18baf3a7e1338356c35f10f657f13152185"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/operational-resilience-mapping/commits/6f26fa7e6c36f84944ecd89f295bfcc3fcae11bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:15:45Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:29:42Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump the npm-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 6 updates\n\nBumps the npm-minor-patch group with 6 updates in the /ui directory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [next](https://github.com/vercel/next.js) | `16.3.4` | `16.3.5` |\n| [react](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react) | `19.2.8` | `19.3.0` |\n| [@types/react](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react) | `19.2.18` | `19.3.0` |\n| [react-dom](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom) | `19.2.8` | `19.3.0` |\n| [@types/react-dom](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react-dom) | `19.2.5` | `19.3.0` |\n| [@types/node](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/node) | `26.4.0` | `26.5.1` |\n\n\n\nUpdates `next` from 16.3.4 to 16.3.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/compare/v16.3.4...v16.3.5)\n\nUpdates `react` from 19.2.8 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/react/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/react/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/react/react/commits/v19.3.0/packages/react)\n\nUpdates `@types/react` from 19.2.18 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react)\n\nUpdates `react-dom` from 19.2.8 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/react/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/react/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/react/react/commits/v19.3.0/packages/react-dom)\n\nUpdates `@types/react-dom` from 19.2.5 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react-dom)\n\nUpdates `@types/node` from 26.4.0 to 26.5.1\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/node)\n\nUpdates `@types/react` from 19.2.18 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react)\n\nUpdates `@types/react-dom` from 19.2.5 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react-dom)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: next\n  dependency-version: 16.3.5\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: react\n  dependency-version: 19.3.0\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react\"\n  dependency-version: 19.3.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: react-dom\n  dependency-version: 19.3.0\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react-dom\"\n  dependency-version: 19.3.0\n  dependency-type: direct:developmen