ollowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/trade-comms-surveillance/commits/425467f3968f5cce2bf1920d75cfcd41d2f95c11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:51:22Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:51:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"d955cec6246477fa170bf8464e78ec3b7c400892","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/trade-comms-surveillance/git/trees/d955cec6246477fa170bf8464e78ec3b7c400892"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/trade-comms-surveillance/git/commits/425467f3968f5cce2bf1920d75cfcd41d2f95c11","verification":{"payload":"tree d955cec6246477fa170bf8464e78ec3b7c400892\nparent bf075509d6358ca6e7d268ad607a28b834ac3d48\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787673082 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787673082 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbn6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8ZcQAJ2skh1rcEp7UazqZpIuNIJg\nqHLHp7Tga+5TI+imR1xEdo9VMTo+9Wjsu0bCTxmfvOxKwFWvaiH4FW5mS5Z5qAAA\no8PF1Lgls73D6p/n56plb5mvyBzkJBLkvIV+CRfmKH5qFA/mrbdIBDomQBvxbwtV\naMNOf4JhvkbLPlGAw5oKoDWAy5W/XrQIirEVGF3EuF7pSXPxAXOIZJ8L5/4QSUAv\nHFfyUdp8eLMtvGHbVPv1W5VKpcOIQ5jEPC1WdzLU2atperXDTkpO+N69tewhE0TT\no6HKaxsMvu7zZz0tP8xP2zUTm8j1iknGsqhPG3nu7VVSBEBOaNb4ufuBfcUsM5LR\nsHSE05bBPIjWQ51AwGIUfx3TjQwD/FZ77T4431LVSEM9Q6l0jVg0wMQzhW82DJYZ\n8cXn5MzuMOfqCcr2R3UPPzwyoGoD5rMmSVIwjjI4u03Ec92My+43MwJPqQkTqfGr\n/cJu0F4ZgQrdG+axw7NuGY6jLHMWH5ZHLcOvKCHXtgBQxQPclLjBvOKgynu2kCTg\nhr1yQYlBm50yPvOH3M/MAAPuBTyFbTErtTVfMznV/1FqrgcLWO