","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/fe272c3a7d3b5aef95d3af9bbaba2d9128a109be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:31:11Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:38:05Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Every bar this corpus cannot express is 1.0 now, and says so\n\nA threshold t tolerates a single failure only over at least 1/(1-t) scored\ndecisions. Every bar raised here is scored 0/1 once per case over a corpus far\nshort of that, so each one already required a perfect run while reading as though\nit priced one failure in. 0.99 was not a looser bar than 1.00 over these corpora.\nIt was the same bar with a friendlier face, which is worse than either: a\nreviewer reads it as headroom that does not exist.\n\nEach rubric now carries the arithmetic beside the number: how many decisions the\nmetric scores, what a single failure would give, and how many cases it would take\nbefore a bar below 1.0 meant anything. The last line is the useful one, because\nit says the number to move first is the corpus and not the bar.\n\nFor the safety family it is also what the property means. A leak gate that is\nright 99% of the time is a gate with a hole in it, and there is no acceptable\nlevel of one unredacted identifier reaching an audit record.\n\nFound by org-metadata''s new eval-governance check, which reads every launch-set\nrepository''s rubrics against the promotion authority and could see what no single\nrepository can see about itself.","tree":{"sha":"d53a717cf26249716f842805f102bae1e777c784","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/git/trees/d53a717cf26249716f842805f102bae1e777c784"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/git/commits/fe272c3a7d3b5aef95d3af9bbaba2d9128a109be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commit/fe272c3a7d3b5aef95d3af9bbaba2d9128a109be","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiF4toAKGZlMjcyYzNhN2QzYjVhZWY5NWQzYWY5YmJhYmEyZDkxMjhhMTA5YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commit/e975086f545efe0281bce03fc75582fe95bff967","sha":"e975086f545efe0281bce03fc75582fe95bff967","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/e975086f545efe0281bce03fc75582fe95bff967"}],"sha":"fe272c3a7d3b5aef95d3af9bbaba2d9128a109be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/fe272c3a7d3b5aef95d3af9bbaba2d9128a109be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/e975086f545efe0281bce03fc75582fe95bff967/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:15:04Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:18:35Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Put a real model in the path, and find out what the metrics were measuring\n\n`eval/datasets/gemini_replay.jsonl` holds 32 replies recorded from\ngemini-3.5-flash over these scenarios. `eval/run_eval.py --drafter\nreplay-gemini` scores the same rubrics and the same hand-written labels against\nthem, offline, with the replay adapter raising on a missing key rather than\nfalling back. It runs in `make gate`.\n\nTwo things came out of it and the second is the one this repository''s model card\nhas been claiming in prose since it was written.\n\n**The managed drafter was dead, and nothing here could have told you.** The\nfirst recording produced 32 rows of `\"response\": null`.\n`VertexGenerationAdapter` capped output at 512 tokens, the configured model\nspends output tokens reasoning before it answers, so the JSON was truncated on\nevery single request, `response.parsed` came back None, and `draft` returned\nNone. The kernel treats any generation failure as silence, deliberately, because\nfor the product a model outage must degrade to \"no suggestion\" rather than to an\nunvalidated fallback. So on the managed profile this service would have produced\nno suggestion for any contact, in any market, and said nothing about why. Fixed\nwith a zero thinking budget; the 512-token bound stays, because the drafter''s job\nis one short grounded sentence and a drafter that needs to reason at length about\nwhich passage to quote is answering a different question.\n\n**The grounding metrics were measuring the validator.** Same corpus, same labels,\nonly the drafter changed:\n\n    groundedness       1.000 -> 0.500\n    citation_accuracy  1.000 -> 0.833\n\nTwo causes, different in kind, and neither repaired here because a bar tuned\nuntil the number looks acceptable measures nothing. The model returns an empty\ndraft on some turns where the template always produced one, which is a real\ncapability gap and the one that matters most in this product. And the fact check\nrequires the canonical phrasing: the label says \"Calls are recorded for quality\nand training\", the model wrote \"we record our calls for quality and training\npurposes\", same fact, scored zero. Against a template that emits the corpus\nsentence verbatim that check could never fail; against a model it is a PHRASING\ncheck wearing a groundedness name. Loosening it would replace a measurement with\na judgement, and this repository already has a place for judgements.\n\n`eval/rubrics/replay/` holds the bars for that run, as a REGRESSION FLOOR under a\nmeasured baseline and not a quality target. Two metrics take them and only two,\nbecause only two of these metrics measure the drafter at all: moving the others\nwould be excusing a real regression under cover of the model swap.\n\nThe recorder needed a change to work at all, and the change is the point of it.\nIt built the full MANAGED container, which reaches a Firestore database before it\nreaches a model, and which would have captured managed-retrieval prompts whose\nkeys the replay can never produce, so every draft would have missed and the run\nwould have failed naming a stale recording that was in fact a recording of\nsomething else. It builds the EVAL''s container now, with only the generation call\nmanaged: the same inputs the replay will present, a real model''s words for the\nanswer.\n\n`tests/unit/test_replay_drafter.py` asserted the shipped state was no recording\nand named its own obsolescence. It now asserts the recording is real: that more\nthan half the rows carry a response, because a recording of nulls satisfies every\nstructural check and scores nothing, and that the model named is the one the\nsettings default to, because a recording of some other model produces keys the\neval cannot build.","tree":{"sha":"600dac55108add165bf58da1226ea272de4e6ae9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/git/trees/600dac55108add165bf58da1226ea272de4e6ae9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/git/commits/e975086f545efe0281bce03fc75582fe95bff967","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"