r}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/2f05ff8c699f56bae6e7fb1306c318e19d87ab64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:28:45Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:34:49Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: agent-eval-kit v0.0.3","tree":{"sha":"81681b75b58d2c1ff3d95d34fd668bed321107b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/git/trees/81681b75b58d2c1ff3d95d34fd668bed321107b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/git/commits/2f05ff8c699f56bae6e7fb1306c318e19d87ab64","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commit/2f05ff8c699f56bae6e7fb1306c318e19d87ab64","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiF4toAKDJmMDVmZjhjNjk5ZjU2YmFlNmU3ZmIxMzA2YzMxOGUxOWQ4N2FiNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commit/c754bf9275607adc9d9251e9e1ad0b1c4ac518c0","sha":"c754bf9275607adc9d9251e9e1ad0b1c4ac518c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/c754bf9275607adc9d9251e9e1ad0b1c4ac518c0"}],"sha":"2f05ff8c699f56bae6e7fb1306c318e19d87ab64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/2f05ff8c699f56bae6e7fb1306c318e19d87ab64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/c754bf9275607adc9d9251e9e1ad0b1c4ac518c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:14:10Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:34:49Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Two markets whose PII rows were live and tested by nothing\n\n`adapters/_review_payload.py` scrubs against EVERY jurisdiction''s rows on every\ncontact, and the pack ships four. The scenarios covered two. So the HKID and TFN\npatterns were live in every SG and JP contact and exercised by nothing, and\n`customer_pii_safety` was scoring two markets'' patterns while reporting a number\nthat read as though it covered four.\n\n`ss-hk-pii-in-turn` and `ss-au-pii-in-turn` are the cases that change that, each\nplanting its own market''s identifier mid sentence, which is how a customer\nactually volunteers one. The AU case plants a checksum-valid TFN, because the\nrow validates the checksum and the planted literal is what protects that\nprecision: a row narrowed until it stops matching would make the pack scan agree\nthat nothing leaked.\n\nThree things the two markets settled that a copy of SG''s fixtures would not.\n\n**A market''s allowlist is a decision, and HK''s is narrower.** HK ships no\nchargeback intent, so a disputed transaction there is refused by the allowlist\nand handed to a person, while the same words in AU are handled and routed for\nmaker-checker. Two files, one difference, and it is the argument for per-market\npacks rather than a global one with exceptions.\n\n**A cue pack is policy and it is not translatable.** `cues-hk.yaml` carries\nCantonese vulnerability phrases because an HK centre serves customers who switch\nlanguage mid sentence. `cues-au.yaml` carries hardship phrases because in that\nmarket those words start a defined process with an obligation attached. Neither\nlist derives from the other, and neither is something a model should infer.\n`procedure-au-card-dispute.yaml` carries the `hardship_raised` entry the AU\ndisclosure pack opens a 30-second referral window off, and the pack library''s\ncross-reference check is what makes a window that could never open a build\nfailure rather than a dead row.\n\n**A finding, recorded rather than fixed here.** `ss-au-hardship` is the first\nscenario anywhere in this corpus pairing a vulnerability cue WITH an allowlisted\naction in the same turn. The service raises the vulnerability handoff and\nexecutes the balance read: the handoff and the gate are computed independently\nand the gate''s reason list does not mention the cue. Every existing vulnerability\nscenario pairs the cue with no requested action, so the combination had never\nbeen scored. The scenario is labelled with what the service does, not with what\nanyone had decided it should do, and the conduct question is stated in the\nscenario note and in docs/evals.md rather than answered by whoever wrote a label.\n\nTwo smaller things on the way.\n\n`_MARKET_LOCALE` in `eval/eval_schema.py` was a hard-coded `{\"SG\", \"JP\"}`. The\ncost was not the duplication: adding a market meant editing a table in the eval\nas well as shipping the packs, and doing the second without the first failed with\n\"market has no packs\" against a directory full of them. It is derived from the\nshipped allowlist packs now, keyed on the allowlist because that is what makes a\nmarket servable at all, and it refuses a market served under two locales.\n\n`pii` is a scenario family of its own rather than folded into `benign`, because\nthe report groups by family and these are the only scenarios exercising the\nnational-id rows: folded in, a market losing its only PII case would leave the\ngroup''s size unchanged.\n\nThe recording half of this repo''s owed work is untouched and still open.\n`eval/datasets/gemini_replay.jsonl` needs a real managed-model call from\n`scripts/record_gemini_fixtures.py`, which is an authoring step with credentials\nthat nothing in a gate should be doing. docs/evals.md now says so under \"what is\nnot measured\" rather than leaving it to be discovered.","tree":{"sha":"845a34ced989dbf32e7d9d03dcb8ea45b6207542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/git/trees/845a34ced989dbf32e7d9d03dcb8ea45b6207542"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/git/commits/c754bf9275607adc9d9251e9e1ad0b1c4ac518c0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commit/c754bf9275607adc9d9251e9e1ad0b1c4ac518c0","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiF4toAKGM3NTRiZjkyNzU2MDdhZGM5ZDkyNTFlOWUxYWQwYjFjNGFjNTE4YzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commit/500aaf427cd8b20d261a8390e5bd3a423f002a27","sha":"500aaf427cd8b20d261a8390e5bd3a423f002a27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/500aaf427cd8b20d261a8390e5bd3a423f002a27"}],"sha":"c754bf9275607adc9d9251e9e1ad0b1c4ac518c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/c754bf9275607adc9d9251e9e1ad0b1c4ac518c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/commits/500aaf427cd8b20d261a8390e5bd3a423f002a27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:32:15Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:44:05Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Ask the promotion authority for a mode-scoped bundle, not a bare repo name\n\nThe managed evaluation port sent `bundle=\"contact-centre-conversations\"`. The\nauthority does not register that name: it registers the two mode-scoped bundles\nand no blended third, because one bundle would let a strong agent-assist result\ncarry a weak customer-facing one over the line, which is the whole reason those\nmodes are gated apart. Every promotion request from this port would have failed\nclosed on UnknownMetricError, and nothing reported it because the offline smoke\ngate never reaches this path.\n\nThe bundle is no longer a constant in the adapter at all. Each mode''s bundle is\nalready resolved into its own ModeGate.promotion_bundle from the settings block,\nand that is the one home for it; a constant here would be a second, and the two\nwould diverge the first time a deployment renamed a bundle.\n\nA deployment with BOTH modes on has two promotions and this port carries one\nbundle, so it refuses by name and points at `eval/run_eval.py --mode gate`, which\nalready asks per rubric. No mode enabled, and an enabled mode with no bundle, are\nrefusals for the same reason: a verdict over nothing certifies nothing.\n\ntests/unit/test_eval_gate_mode.py covers all four states.","tree":{"sha":"1c4673cd79a991bf0b34778b6255eb5847231a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/git/trees/1c4673cd79a991bf0b34778b6255eb5847231a38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/contact-centre-conversations/git/commits/500aaf427cd8b20d261a8390e5bd3a423f002a27","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com