:{"date":"2026-09-27T09:53:35Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump hex-service-kit to v0.0.11: trace only through the collector\n\nDecision D1: build_tracer refuses an unset OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT instead of\nexporting straight to Cloud Trace around the collector''s GenAI-content redaction, and\ntakes no project argument any more.\n\n- pyproject.toml and the locks: hex-service-kit v0.0.11 (ec2d724). The only other lock\n  movement is opentelemetry-exporter-gcp-trace and its dependencies leaving with the\n  kit''s otel extra, where this repo resolved it.\n- adapters/gcp/tracer.py: build_tracer(service=...) only.\n- tests/contract: the managed tracer''s documented refusal is now\n  CollectorEndpointRequiredError; on-prem keys off a new onprem_refuses field; a new\n  test keeps the old guarantee that with a collector configured and no SDK a span\n  degrades to a no-op.\n- settings, config, Terraform variable and adoption notes stop describing a direct\n  Cloud Trace path that no longer exists.\n\nRelocked without --upgrade: fleet-deps bump-commons'' --upgrade relock moved 0\nunrelated pins here, and those were reverted.","tree":{"sha":"5ae5545a69d23378523de187ee2e6e3abab6a673","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/git/trees/5ae5545a69d23378523de187ee2e6e3abab6a673"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/git/commits/f08b34e9265d1b457ae9e7027069d0b0c71fc7cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commit/f08b34e9265d1b457ae9e7027069d0b0c71fc7cd","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiGM9oAKGYwOGIzNGU5MjY1ZDFiNDU3YWU5ZTcwMjcwNjlkMGIwYzcxZmM3Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commit/b1f002eb848a8a790e086aa78d88bb1004d6f91b","sha":"b1f002eb848a8a790e086aa78d88bb1004d6f91b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/b1f002eb848a8a790e086aa78d88bb1004d6f91b"}],"sha":"f08b34e9265d1b457ae9e7027069d0b0c71fc7cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/f08b34e9265d1b457ae9e7027069d0b0c71fc7cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/b1f002eb848a8a790e086aa78d88bb1004d6f91b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T04:33:57Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T04:36:42Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Adopt the fixed guardrail: fail-closed Model Armor, prompts screened as sent, blocks audited\n\nThe Model Armor adapter read str(filter_match_state), which is the enum''s number on 3.11+, so it\nallowed everything. Take the template''s fixed adapter: allowed only on NO_MATCH_FOUND with\ninvocation_result SUCCESS, an explicit per-call deadline, API errors propagate. The local\nheuristic no longer blocks a customer called Dan or \"the system prompted me\".\n\nScreen the prompt each generation call actually sends (narration_prompt / signal_prompt, now\nshared with the managed adapters), use the screened output text as given, and audit every\nrefusal, a raising guardrail included, as Decision.BLOCKED before falling back to the\ndeterministic summary or no advisory note. The guardrail is now a required argument.\n\nDeclare google-cloud-modelarmor in the gcp extra and lock it (lint-gcp), add the guardrail exit\ncall to scripts/demo.py (portability), set ignore_partial_invocation_failures on the template,\nand add the SDK-free enum-mirror test and the real-enum mapping test.","tree":{"sha":"671707c678718ebc6eba85a6950d52c701db4457","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/git/trees/671707c678718ebc6eba85a6950d52c701db4457"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/git/commits/b1f002eb848a8a790e086aa78d88bb1004d6f91b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commit/b1f002eb848a8a790e086aa78d88bb1004d6f91b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiGM9oAKGIxZjAwMmViODQ4YThhNzkwZTA4NmFhNzhkODhiYjEwMDRkNmY5MWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commit/0e8245e669d675d51873209c0064f22391f68cbf","sha":"0e8245e669d675d51873209c0064f22391f68cbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/0e8245e669d675d51873209c0064f22391f68cbf"}],"sha":"b1f002eb848a8a790e086aa78d88bb1004d6f91b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/b1f002eb848a8a790e086aa78d88bb1004d6f91b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/0e8245e669d675d51873209c0064f22391f68cbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T05:27:54Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T04:36:42Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Wire the guardrail into narration and signals (rule R1)\n\nAdopts the merged hex-service-template guardrail design\n(org-metadata/docs/plans/guardrail-registry-observability.md, P3 sweep) for this\nrepository: this repo shipped no guardrail port, so it declared\nagent-guardrail-gateway as a mandatory dependency while\nadapters/gcp/narration.py and adapters/gcp/signals.py called Gemini with\nnothing screening either direction.\n\n- ports/guardrail.py: the GuardrailPort protocol (screen one direction of one\n  generation call).\n- domain/kernel.py: Direction, GuardrailCategory, GuardrailFinding and\n  GuardrailVerdict, the vertical-neutral safety types.\n- domain/scorecard_service.py: `_narrate` and `_advisory` now screen INPUT\n  before the narrator/classifier runs and OUTPUT before a draft or advisory\n  note is attached to the scorecard. Neither call is consequential (the\n  engine decides before either runs), so a block degrades exactly the way an\n  unreachable model already does: the narrator falls back to\n  deterministic_narration and the classifier contributes no advisory colour,\n  logged, never raised -- the scorecard''s consequential fields are\n  untouched.\n- domain/narration.py: guardrail_input_text(), a stable text rendering of a\n  NarrationBrief for the INPUT screen.\n- adapters/{local,gcp,onprem}/guardrail.py: a deterministic heuristic\n  stand-in, ModelArmorGuardrailAdapter against a regional Model Armor\n  template (reusing cio-advisory''s adapter and regional-host shape), and a\n  fail-fast placeholder.\n- adapters/controls.py, config.py: the CONVQA_GUARDRAIL switch beside\n  CONVQA_REVIEW_ROUTING (same three states), ModelArmorSettings with a\n  non-empty default template_id so the shipped settings never boot\n  unconfigured, and a boot refusal when the guardrail is on with the Model\n  Armor adapter bound and no template named.\n- config/settings.yaml: the guardrail adapter binding and the model_armor\n  block.\n- infra/terraform/model_armor.tf: the template, gated on\n  var.model_armor_full_capabilities (asia-southeast1 refuses the\n  malicious-URI filter otherwise), roles/modelarmor.user on the runtime\n  account (iam.tf), the API (apis.tf), the VPC-SC perimeter entry\n  (vpc_sc.tf), and the google-beta provider this resource needs\n  (providers.tf), mocked in production_edge.tftest.hcl.\n- ports/__init__.py, service.py, tests/contract/canonical.py,\n  tests/unit/test_iap_identity.py: the guardrail''s five required homes (port\n  map, binding table, settings file, container accessor, canonical-call\n  table) plus the hand-written settings fixture that test file carries.\n- tests/unit/test_guardrail_screening.py: the switch''s three states, the\n  boot refusal, the disabled pass-through, and the domain proof that INPUT\n  and OUTPUT are each screened before anything downstream sees the text,\n  with the fallback behaviour proved for both the narrator and the\n  classifier.\n- COMPLIANCE.md, docs/runbook.md, docs/onprem-migration.md,\n  docs/practices-audit.md: rule R1 moves from Partial to Covered.\n\nmake gate (lint, format, mypy, pytest -m ''not integration'', eval) and\n`terraform test` under infra/terraform both green.","tree":{"sha":"30482e7552e28d5b5f83d64cf236710c51321076","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/git/trees/30482e7552e28d5b5f83d64cf236710c51321076"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/git/commits/0e8245e669d675d51873209c0064f22391f68cbf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commit/0e8245e669d675d51873209c0064f22391f68cbf","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiGM9oAKDBlODI0NWU2NjlkNjc1ZDUxODczMjA5YzAwNjRmMjIzOTFmNjhjYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commit/81d42c5cb08a74e0af50992bd4363851efdf1d72","sha":"81d42c5cb08a74e0af50992bd4363851efdf1d72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/81d42c5cb08a74e0af50992bd4363851efdf1d72"}],"sha":"0e8245e669d675d51873209c0064f22391f68cbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/0e8245e669d675d51873209c0064f22391f68cbf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/81d42c5cb08a74e0af50992bd4363851efdf1d72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T22:20:29Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T22:30:01Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Sync the canonical skills: model pills and the live profile","tree":{"sha":"d2c416520d34a0fc72273424c89f2db05b814433","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/git/trees/d2c416520d34a0fc72273424c89f2db05b814433"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/git/commits/81d42c5cb08a74e0af50992bd4363851efdf1d72","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commit/81d42c5cb08a74e0af50992bd4363851efdf1d72","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiGM9oAKDgxZDQyYzVjYjA4YTc0ZTBhZjUwOTkyYmQ0MzYzODUxZWZkZjFkNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commit/d812a91305a2682a4ce021f28fb5c1b5452985d0","sha":"d812a91305a2682a4ce021f28fb5c1b5452985d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/d812a91305a2682a4ce021f28fb5c1b5452985d0"}],"sha":"81d42c5cb08a74e0af50992bd4363851efdf1d72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/81d42c5cb08a74e0af50992bd4363851efdf1d72"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/commits/d812a91305a2682a4ce021f28fb5c1b5452985d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T22:00:24Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T22:03:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Show the model that answered as two pills, not a banner, on hex-service-kit v0.0.10\n\nBump hex-service-kit to v0.0.10 (only the kit pin moved in the locks) and call\ninstall_answer_provenance(app), so every response names the model that answered\n(X-Answered-By) and whether it searched (X-Search-Used).\n\nThe Gemini narrator and advisory classifier note the model they called after a\nusable answer; neither attaches a search tool, so neither notes a search. The\nlocal fakes note deterministic-offline-stub, the same string generator_model\nreports under local. Both managed calls now sample free (temperature omitted):\nnarration restates decided figures, and the classifier writes one advisory\nsentence whose kind and confidence are fixed in code. No managed call is left\npinned, because no model output here is scored, labelled or compared.\n\nThe console''s full-width provenance banner becomes a ModelPills component at the\ntop right, fed by one window.fetch wrapper; the proxy forwards both headers. The\nhard-reasoning branch in the generator_model resolver is gone.","tree":{"sha":"8b621cfb0b7632588f9cca525a3ebc87c33a4b3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/git/trees/8b621cfb0b7632588f9cca525a3ebc87c33a4b3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/conversation-qa-scorecard/git/commits/d812a91305a2682a4ce021f28fb5c1b5452985d0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/user