sthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/d7985adfbf4e19c6bb994ad9ce329a3dbdc90ecd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:28:25Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T21:53:59Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Keep the model pills light: no dark-scheme override on a light-only page\n\n- globals.css: drop the template''s prefers-color-scheme pill block. This\n  console''s page has no dark theme, so under a dark OS scheme that block\n  showed the configured pill solid and the answered pill faint on a light\n  page, reversing what the two styles mean. The .model-pills comment says so.","tree":{"sha":"0057071b527c99cfe24f1ec8d2141f163477aeff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/trees/0057071b527c99cfe24f1ec8d2141f163477aeff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/commits/d7985adfbf4e19c6bb994ad9ce329a3dbdc90ecd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a