{"sha":"7132e998d8baba3d28671fe528d6c488fc9142cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/trees/7132e998d8baba3d28671fe528d6c488fc9142cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/commits/3a82aeba72a50c49cc4cf8cc72c39f6c187ba6a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commit/3a82aeba72a50c49cc4cf8cc72c39f6c187ba6a8","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiGh9oAKDNhODJhZWJhNzJhNTBjNDljYzRjZjhjYzcyYzM5ZjZjMTg3YmE2YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commit/633071068e20050bbe7a32d413c2bc0e730a5a3a","sha":"633071068e20050bbe7a32d413c2bc0e730a5a3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/633071068e20050bbe7a32d413c2bc0e730a5a3a"}],"sha":"3a82aeba72a50c49cc4cf8cc72c39f6c187ba6a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/3a82aeba72a50c49cc4cf8cc72c39f6c187ba6a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/633071068e20050bbe7a32d413c2bc0e730a5a3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:11:52Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:11:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Adopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#15)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4bcb7413a9c3cea5b99b95c7ea1ce2bdec9cc141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/trees/4bcb7413a9c3cea5b99b95c7ea1ce2bdec9cc141"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/commits/633071068e20050bbe7a32d413c2bc0e730a5a3a","verification":{"payload":"tree 4bcb7413a9c3cea5b99b95c7ea1ce2bdec9cc141\nparent 757b3f2c087255684ba1b81b4517f55006426378\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787706712 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787706712 +0800\n\nAdopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#15)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjj1YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtbAQAHYPIq/bNJGkybjtPRgsEkGT\nWCEBZOPOmaSsCc96hyNnH+mnnK39/E1eZMLVWnoXmn6LXFTDJ18dwK5nVMQbdg38\nXog6gJN8N46nTcnh2CNIP+4hS4Rd89W6GZWg3iLPYBRUKp921aAe6X276pP2UnxU\nMmzP4zrjFfPZBk1OuhC0xA31eKI8qvvN2CW0mfFht7PrasvayWX0eYkSWY0ynEbK\nUdcURf1tqbl5+NYRVm5DWIEGbc64jXg9KOsL5y2yDxZGCzKT1a1q+WcHrd5hKFEs\n80RCbsrCK4dZsDYC4wZdH9PyIfXD9z9G1szMkxb+t5iiyPjPt7qIOZP8Sy8ZR1lp\nVMPwXegXRHOzaQEYc9+0YqrRyI7stbteOtPqmHqsQK+WsIuE6zLt8qtJqp4fxSfA\nUCunScdjhjKEmR5MphYSFfj53ywkE24eGYY9L94b4+qpC5La0TcFhhmGh5hIBPcD\n8zmcG78yYua3vtAOxF5IYp4NYATKd86/lc0bRvKocO/9bCGYKjUfvfAnwegwJgLd\nDcdznKD4isr7GtMBU4EMn+AriSrpb8LUouqcirdAgoaQIDtqg2Zsmbzx0xos1NkM\nsyLGmaHoBBZtCJHqaIv2D5uWFsuOm6yI7rfDdIykHJtj27zKhV2RTxqLrC4psnAA\nD1BPmf8ahTlztHL04BbC\n=ttSc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T01:11:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commit/633071068e20050bbe7a32d413c2bc0e730a5a3a","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiGh9oAKDYzMzA3MTA2OGUyMDA1MGJiZTdhMzJkNDEzYzJiYzBlNzMwYTVhM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commit/757b3f2c087255684ba1b81b4517f55006426378","sha":"757b3f2c087255684ba1b81b4517f55006426378","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/757b3f2c087255684ba1b81b4517f55006426378"}],"sha":"633071068e20050bbe7a32d413c2bc0e730a5a3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/633071068e20050bbe7a32d413c2bc0e730a5a3a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/757b3f2c087255684ba1b81b4517f55006426378/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:49:50Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:49:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#14)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"04f7a752a835b1872cf1dc661f4c9d87dc3cdf4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/trees/04f7a752a835b1872cf1dc661f4c9d87dc3cdf4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/commits/757b3f2c087255684ba1b81b4517f55006426378","verification":{"payload":"tree 04f7a752a835b1872cf1dc661f4c9d87dc3cdf4c\nparent e1239a26e7bf7cfd24606571d4c4dfa60334b1d4\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672990 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672990 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#14)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbmeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA78YQAJxyWqUzGh4zx2HN3heJukk3\nGILkzWTlYqhIoJi6fvF66XMU7cdq8HonrREXB+UVAYZIC+YI+dnx72Aa6XXib6yS\nwSOtLmWwua13SRq1j5RiDA6RtyDq1JUIRAY6GvWMth2Fb+T7xQRMczJZrTsea1Gh\n8hW9osxCRW+unsGouAO8fXB+ZdmnnfmhKTXv4ZrVM4nbC5yeWV8/VrXJ9qRRVq78\ntZ9Nyotdsu0589D6KhMvegVbQ/+iOZl6twXaW8wpPb+j0DjjwmWSRnYaHizLe6pz\n+W4b3UK2AeGv6yYaKnK5t7AJqbiDGQE69ucApeGbzTJzo/Hriui+CSokNsH94KL5\nAr84IbheF9w+Qyua7F4wTnmJbW1WkrD5dM6cYDQVq41oYOmAwzBiMnYA0IxegL+6\n38q4oyTGL5kI9vhBUmeUit2+DYF54ZbzJ9vT8PQcAHPiUoaxjpks0M6fvt5sc8Ru\n4u/9OZNxbkBSN4qcQo2fJ/Q7checqwN3JeSGnkZbWysK1eEJJrWhrQI7IW57kTnU\nXornIaJtDzX/GTLfC4tnpaGPw7Gbehmesi4PhoGERYYgQoxNzESG6ySihGEA7byl\n6a3njiVe6/wgpxsaZb4WUlQFZOhfg9vWXSIkam4UjY+N/9xTx6Hco8hCUhNltJlo\n+aU8rHO8fm6h9JQnOjdG\n=UYHV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:49:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commit/757b3f2c087255684ba1b81b4517f55006426378","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiGh9oAKDc1N2IzZjJjMDg3MjU1Njg0YmExYjgxYjQ1MTdmNTUwMDY0MjYzNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commit/e1239a26e7bf7cfd24606571d4c4dfa60334b1d4","sha":"e1239a26e7bf7cfd24606571d4c4dfa60334b1d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/e1239a26e7bf7cfd24606571d4c4dfa60334b1d4"}],"sha":"757b3f2c087255684ba1b81b4517f55006426378","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/757b3f2c087255684ba1b81b4517f55006426378"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/e1239a26e7bf7cfd24606571d4c4dfa60334b1d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:14:57Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:14:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#13)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 522 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","tree":{"sha":"e69ebd471809dcca8a76420503f120aadeb67fd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/trees/e69ebd471809dcca8a76420503f120aadeb67fd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/commits/e1239a26e7bf7cfd24606571d4c4dfa60334b1d4","verification":{"payload":"tree e69ebd471809dcca8a76420503f120aadeb67fd5\nparent b03dfbe3114fa2f7465ea27332367b1e4ed008e9\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787670897 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787670897 +0800\n\nBind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#13)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 522 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbFxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3pQQABusYF1JU3H8/KTXf0bDaIG5\nOZqNXNTgQulNXuKeMpkUghgDu/iJN2BTc0xSvUYkdEnauU9TYSy6JUnUYUljoq5w\nGygI1w/FjNiJSzfx4l1kiEd0vdXJmeVohK9fLg4EmL/E+MtZSZYpdgeLnF+h+Rv8\nRX482wPLXEcsWTcZQA+is3VBwZ2Te63xPH+TsDzZUBgnf/NQBD8pFu4XUHTH4zp3\n7FynIOIvpTczRc41tTWPappstrN3KjCqJApVWOQuSnALl8H0qLzn6MFeCrhi+iKe\nhT4ycLawgnyRkHeh9TJaLbXhX3xg6VVuTrXYw7r6kzQ61wP4EGYB9IX8m2hZUQNE\ncaQP8RCZVZLK7KVnBsEdAteQ/EtPMTAhef1R+IrPC2gxTHGFk4OfZ/iDlLfh+4lN\nJ3jthHOf7MN2142hcPgJdzXiwoehREIQSNimAkTt6si3U/tk0jqAQ/+mrHobsK+X\nrQVcFuG4s7ULYGWkvMFlCy7U4KCj9nOo59iZnthmu9QT+W1UOwaAtbdowjtcZdkE\ntnlg5RiH8aVNXxXcOiSFL108aVN8qB8NJuRwTt5oUI0JVlY9vTNthxyPE2ajdqKG\nmYywuOAqN9P0d2rSngHEdDK5e0FVvgJ7xUpOlh5L41WKA6TcP6CLPhB4ITESEX8+\ncgXqo59WTnQ4xYz67TGZ\n=XTDM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:14:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commit/e1239a26e7bf7cfd24606571d4c4dfa60334b1d4","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiGh9oAKGUxMjM5YTI2ZTdiZjdjZmQyNDYwNjU3MWQ0YzRkZmE2MDMzNGIxZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commit/b03dfbe3114fa2f7465ea27332367b1e4ed008e9","sha":"b03dfbe3114fa2f7465ea27332367b1e4ed008e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/b03dfbe3114fa2f7465ea27332367b1e4ed008e9"}],"sha":"e1239a26e7bf7cfd24606571d4c4dfa60334b1d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/e1239a26e7bf7cfd24606571d4c4dfa60334b1d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/commits/b03dfbe3114fa2f7465ea27332367b1e4ed008e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:58:57Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:58:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Re-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#12)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"86fd4dd2315e64c9676adbc2504ec4bbde03ffc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/trees/86fd4dd2315e64c9676adbc2504ec4bbde03ffc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/proactive-service-outreach/git/commits/b03dfbe3114fa2f7465ea27332367b1e4ed008e9","verification":{"payload":"tree 86fd4dd2315e64c9676adbc2504ec4bbde03ffc7\nparent 31a76bdafc9cc97479f149cb62ecb1f5086561af\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787644737 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787644737 +0800\n\nRe-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#12)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjUtBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPc4QADpXJGdEuZACwSnP/4+mdMOq\nD+QDh/mnEcZfmDr2cow+3clKt2+x1VCXq2IcbIYIVji/U+kMrVv9N9ux/lDNddsD\nmKbGn7l9pX8b6nYFA82bQgUTbCemQvcual/WJu5Jjqajz6At+9oIAsHg33QpTVtF\nYetrsAOZV5THi7EYAsH5kMM8vgi58pul972QI8