ed{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/commits/f3a856df1941a61e8225f4c7b7fc3726aeb76295/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T03:50:40Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T03:59:43Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Take the default off the audit bucket lock\n\nworm_locked defaulted to true, so the first apply of this stack in any\nproject locked its audit bucket irreversibly for the whole retention window,\nwith nothing in that deployment''s own tfvars saying so. The fleet decided on\n2026-09-12 that an irreversible control takes no default; this stack was one\nof 33 that sweep never reached.\n\nA plan now refuses until the deployment states the lock. The Terraform tests\nstate it once per file in the production form, still assert that a stated\nlock sits on the six-month floor, and gain a run proving the unlocked posture\ncreates an unlocked bucket. That run fails if the lock is ever hard-coded\nback into the bucket, which every other run would miss.","tree":{"sha":"269f85e7ede4a690d99874ac0ee90ed2b84501b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/git/trees/269f85e7ede4a690d99874ac0ee90ed2b84501b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/git/commits/f3a856df1941a61e8225f4c7b7fc3726aeb76295","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"