ents_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/commits/4d6041c1e090d5698a8e7c78b2cee53988afb012/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:53:41Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:59:53Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: hex-service-kit v0.0.5","tree":{"sha":"03b7bcfdad5f4ee37b089241ce86cbbd657cfee2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/git/trees/03b7bcfdad5f4ee37b089241ce86cbbd657cfee2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/git/commits/4d6041c1e090d5698a8e7c78b2cee53988afb012","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/commit/4d6041c1e090d5698a8e7c78b2cee53988afb012","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiHQtoAKDRkNjA0MWMxZTA5MGQ1Njk4YThlN2M3OGIyY2VlNTM5ODhhZmIwMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/commit/d2af38eab26b88f0e0f396d364fd34775078e052","sha":"d2af38eab26b88f0e0f396d364fd34775078e052","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/commits/d2af38eab26b88f0e0f396d364fd34775078e052"}],"sha":"4d6041c1e090d5698a8e7c78b2cee53988afb012","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/commits/4d6041c1e090d5698a8e7c78b2cee53988afb012"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/commits/d2af38eab26b88f0e0f396d364fd34775078e052/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:10:40Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:10:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Adopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#14)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"966a23c27e12b1c4f6b6b5ff900db579c67be75a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/git/trees/966a23c27e12b1c4f6b6b5ff900db579c67be75a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/git/commits/d2af38eab26b88f0e0f396d364fd34775078e052","verification":{"payload":"tree 966a23c27e12b1c4f6b6b5ff900db579c67be75a\nparent 953ac7e84b4a90df83602a8c1fd920d21d9ac8fe\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787706640 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787706640 +0800\n\nAdopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#14)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjj0QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQzIQAHMd5vb3QKK32yssWd6ER8vU\n3WSsYYj9/TQ3EKFl/MM7VCNW7qpf6iDMuQdLzLOAnP1exBmVsDr/7Jh3JnldSRWi\nSIMkeHuXIVpG7gW+OAigkAzRKYohk8cpGH5Z2jFQcxFIujrw4cr4B9NEg922LS8P\nPpbLOL1of+zz5RA3VXBjlx6bohKCWpaTM3z5rilOgzkItyiu