.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/commits/40428fb4b26dcdb4efa47d6a74e05ee5c4d3d411/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:20:05Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:20:05Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"message":"Close the bare-invocation gap in the fork rename\n\nThe shell-invocation rule keys on a following subcommand or flag, so a Dockerfile\nexec form (ENTRYPOINT [\"cmd\"], CMD [\"cmd\", ...]) and the command alone on a usage\nline fell through to the bare package rule and were rewritten to the package name: a\nfork''s image would exec a command that no longer exists. Two exec-form anchors and a\nwhole-line anchor now catch those shapes, and the new test was observed red against\nthe unfixed rules before being trusted green.","tree":{"sha":"8a9000f898ee8a02d3b11e924ca7d9ba58b0c41e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/git/trees/8a9000f898ee8a02d3b11e924ca7d9ba58b0c41e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/data-quality-governance/git/commits/40428fb4b26dcdb4efa47d6a74e05ee5c4d3d411","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","