om/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/9ddc23c5a6e14a2655d9ca667f74f68b8ca6d298/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:41:16Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:45:10Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Correct docs that say the review router refuses at request time\n\nThe service now refuses to boot under the managed profile when review\nrouting is on and HUMAN_REVIEW_URL is unset, MEETCAP_REVIEW_ROUTING switches\nrouting, and a hand-off that fails at request time is reported as\nreview_routing \"failed\" and logged. Some documents still said the\nmanaged router refuses the escalation at request time rather than\nswallowing it, and .env.example named no switch. Routing off needs no console.\nDocumentation only; no practices-audit verdict changed.","tree":{"sha":"0f468da8f253087f83f5805aff8a0fb240d7f2b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/git/trees/0f468da8f253087f83f5805aff8a0fb240d7f2b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/git/commits/9ddc23c5a6e14a2655d9ca667f74f68b8ca6d298","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commit/9ddc23c5a6e14a2655d9ca667f74f68b8ca6d298","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiH3doAKDlkZGMyM2M1YTZlMTRhMjY1NWQ5Y2E2NjdmNzRmNjhiOGNhNmQyOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commit/14cd49d23e4052ca6b6e0ad1c51da98cfef40f6f","sha":"14cd49d23e4052ca6b6e0ad1c51da98cfef40f6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/14cd49d23e4052ca6b6e0ad1c51da98cfef40f6f"}],"sha":"9ddc23c5a6e14a2655d9ca667f74f68b8ca6d298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/9ddc23c5a6e14a2655d9ca667f74f68b8ca6d298"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/14cd49d23e4052ca6b6e0ad1c51da98cfef40f6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:10:38Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:13:17Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Correct the review-routing comments to the boot refusal\n\nThe variables.tf header and the review_url comment in settings.yaml still\nsaid the managed review router refuses to swallow an escalation when\nHUMAN_REVIEW_URL is empty. Since the runtime control switches landed that\nis false twice over: the service refuses at BOOT when review routing is on\nand no console is named, and MEETCAP_REVIEW_ROUTING=false switches routing\noff, so human_review_url is only required with review_routing_enabled on.\n\nComment-only; no behaviour changes.","tree":{"sha":"c0777a16748d3b4e2960dd70e854afc782abb2c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/git/trees/c0777a16748d3b4e2960dd70e854afc782abb2c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/git/commits/14cd49d23e4052ca6b6e0ad1c51da98cfef40f6f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commit/14cd49d23e4052ca6b6e0ad1c51da98cfef40f6f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiH3doAKDE0Y2Q0OWQyM2U0MDUyY2E2YjZlMGFkMWM1MWRhOThjZmVmNDBmNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commit/367c78ac4135855e5e351c5cc2aa3098e0ba0741","sha":"367c78ac4135855e5e351c5cc2aa3098e0ba0741","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/367c78ac4135855e5e351c5cc2aa3098e0ba0741"}],"sha":"14cd49d23e4052ca6b6e0ad1c51da98cfef40f6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/14cd49d23e4052ca6b6e0ad1c51da98cfef40f6f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/367c78ac4135855e5e351c5cc2aa3098e0ba0741/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:13:40Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:16:31Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Switch review routing, refuse at boot without a console, and report every hand-off\n\nThe fleet''s runtime-control contract, template shape (as aml-alert-triage). Review routing is\nthe one cheap runtime control this service has, so it is the one switch.\n\n- MEETCAP_REVIEW_ROUTING is read once at settings load in three states: unset is on, a\n  boolean wins, emptied or unrecognised refuses at boot. Off binds a disabled router and logs\n  one warning per process, however many containers the agent tools build.\n- Under gcp, routing on with no HUMAN_REVIEW_URL refuses at boot. It used to surface on the\n  first escalation: a 500 from triage, and a 422 blaming the caller from capture.\n- Every caller that hands off goes through a recording wrapper: the triage route, tool and\n  CLI command directly, and the capture route, tool and CLI command by handing the wrapper to\n  the capture service, which routes each consequential entry. A failed hand-off no longer\n  fails the request: the result carries review_routing (routed, failed, off, not_required),\n  the entry''s review_ref stays empty (so it still cannot dispatch), and the failure is\n  logged. The console states the triage outcome in plain words.\n- Terraform gains review_routing_enabled, sets the service''s switch from it, and relaxes the\n  edge''s console requirement only when routing is stated off; a new plan test holds that.\n- The docs that said the managed router refuses at request time now say the service refuses\n  at boot and reports the hand-off.\n- pii-kit masking here protects the transcript, audit trail, tool results and the review\n  payload inside the domain rather than being a redaction port on the request path, so it is\n  not the control the contract switches, and it gains no switch.","tree":{"sha":"db79a9158a118022cb7b4627f94b1814ea5a91d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/git/trees/db79a9158a118022cb7b4627f94b1814ea5a91d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/git/commits/367c78ac4135855e5e351c5cc2aa3098e0ba0741","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commit/367c78ac4135855e5e351c5cc2aa3098e0ba0741","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiH3doAKDM2N2M3OGFjNDEzNTg1NWU1ZTM1MWM1Y2MyYWEzMDk4ZTBiYTA3NDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commit/2336ebe1644daf7123c7065d585707628a363998","sha":"2336ebe1644daf7123c7065d585707628a363998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/2336ebe1644daf7123c7065d585707628a363998"}],"sha":"367c78ac4135855e5e351c5cc2aa3098e0ba0741","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/367c78ac4135855e5e351c5cc2aa3098e0ba0741"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/2336ebe1644daf7123c7065d585707628a363998/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T03:50:54Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T04:04:20Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Take the default off the audit bucket lock\n\nworm_locked defaulted to true, so the first apply of this stack in any\nproject locked its audit bucket irreversibly for the whole retention window,\nwith nothing in that deployment''s own tfvars saying so. The fleet decided on\n2026-09-12 that an irreversible control takes no default; this stack was one\nof 33 that sweep never reached.\n\nA plan now refuses until the deployment states the lock. The Terraform tests\nstate it once per file in the production form, still assert that a stated\nlock sits on the six-month floor, and gain a run proving the unlocked posture\ncreates an unlocked bucket. That run fails if the lock is ever hard-coded\nback into the bucket, which every other run would miss.","tree":{"sha":"ddeef03ece255b8b1294f231f67d69fa7efb2ed1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/git/trees/ddeef03ece255b8b1294f231f67d69fa7efb2ed1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/git/commits/2336ebe1644daf7123c7065d585707628a363998","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commit/2336ebe1644daf7123c7065d585707628a363998","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiH3doAKDIzMzZlYmUxNjQ0ZGFmNzEyM2M3MDY1ZDU4NTcwNzYyOGEzNjM5OTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commit/c21383d79cba0ef2fd66589a00f8ebc8294ef767","sha":"c21383d79cba0ef2fd66589a00f8ebc8294ef767","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/c21383d79cba0ef2fd66589a00f8ebc8294ef767"}],"sha":"2336ebe1644daf7123c7065d585707628a363998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/2336ebe1644daf7123c7065d585707628a363998"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/meeting-knowledge-capture/commits/c21383d79cba0ef2fd66589a00f8ebc8294ef767/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T11:06:35Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:27:18Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump the npm-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 6 updates\n\nBumps the npm-minor-patch group with 6 updates in the /ui directory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [next](https://github.com/vercel/next.js) | `16.3.4` | `16.3.5` |\n| [react](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react) | `19.2.8` | `19.3.0` |\n| [@types/react](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react) | `19.2.18` | `19.3.0` |\n| [react-dom](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom) | `19.2.8` | `19.3.0` |\n| [@types/react-dom](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react-dom) | `19.2.5` | `19.3.0` |\n| [@types/node](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/node) | `26.4.0` | `26.5.1` |\n\n\n\nUpdates `next` from 16.3.4 to 16.3.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/compare/v16.3.4...v16.3.5)\n\nUpdates `react` from 19.2.8 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/react/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/react/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/react/react/commits/v19.3.0/packages/react)\n\nUpdates `@types/react` from 19.2.18 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react)\n\nUpdates `react-dom` from 19.2.8 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/react/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/react/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/react/react/commits/v19.3.0/packages/react-dom)\n\nUpdates `@types/react-dom` from 19.