te_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/nl2sql-analytics/commits/05f540100b013a7fdb804ac5cfc0d3f8c39aa974/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:47:32Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:47:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"1aa3160e1443b1c573db6333504920ef7e598d53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/nl2sql-analytics/git/trees/1aa3160e1443b1c573db6333504920ef7e598d53"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/nl2sql-analytics/git/commits/05f540100b013a7fdb804ac5cfc0d3f8c39aa974","verification":{"payload":"tree 1aa3160e1443b1c573db6333504920ef7e598d53\nparent bb7782fdf27eb569230c1dd08ead032945fd9329\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672852 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672852 +0800\n\nPin 