W_ROUTING switches\nrouting, and a hand-off that fails at request time is reported as\nreview_routing \"failed\" and logged. Some documents still said the\nmanaged router refuses the escalation at request time rather than\nswallowing it, and .env.example named no switch. Routing off needs no console.\nDocumentation only; no practices-audit verdict changed.","tree":{"sha":"c5e792a308894d265cc2eb99edbe9c6dd30b0d24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/trees/c5e792a308894d265cc2eb99edbe9c6dd30b0d24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/commits/05ca0c9c76f18370f17ca75db180de256cd73d81","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commit/05ca0c9c76f18370f17ca75db180de256cd73d81","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiIiNoAKDA1Y2EwYzljNzZmMTgzNzBmMTdjYTc1ZGIxODBkZTI1NmNkNzNkODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commit/d1cd58b44c5c841853c4f5c6cb9bae0e46bdeabd","sha":"d1cd58b44c5c841853c4f5c6cb9bae0e46bdeabd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/d1cd58b44c5c841853c4f5c6cb9bae0e46bdeabd"}],"sha":"05ca0c9c76f18370f17ca75db180de256cd73d81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/05ca0c9c76f18370f17ca75db180de256cd73d81"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/d1cd58b44c5c841853c4f5c6cb9bae0e46bdeabd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:10:03Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:13:16Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Correct the review-routing comments to the boot refusal\n\nThe variables.tf header and the review_url comment in settings.yaml still\nsaid the managed review router refuses to swallow an escalation when\nHUMAN_REVIEW_URL is empty. Since the runtime control switches landed that\nis false twice over: the service refuses at BOOT when review routing is on\nand no console is named, and POLICYHR_REVIEW_ROUTING=false switches routing\noff, so human_review_url is only required with review_routing_enabled on.\n\nComment-only; no behaviour changes.","tree":{"sha":"8be670f62a7c2cf764808fb88be23f85bf23b0d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/trees/8be670f62a7c2cf764808fb88be23f85bf23b0d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/commits/d1cd58b44c5c841853c4f5c6cb9bae0e46bdeabd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commit/d1cd58b44c5c841853c4f5c6cb9bae0e46bdeabd","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiIiNoAKGQxY2Q1OGI0NGM1Yzg0MTg1M2M0ZjVjNmNiOWJhZTBlNDZiZGVhYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commit/f7e762f775429f3c165df8cb58aba87633f6073f","sha":"f7e762f775429f3c165df8cb58aba87633f6073f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/f7e762f775429f3c165df8cb58aba87633f6073f"}],"sha":"d1cd58b44c5c841853c4f5c6cb9bae0e46bdeabd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/d1cd58b44c5c841853c4f5c6cb9bae0e46bdeabd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/f7e762f775429f3c165df8cb58aba87633f6073f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:38:07Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:40:28Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Switch review routing, refuse at boot without a console, report hand-offs\n\nApplies the fleet''s runtime-control contract (template shape, after aml-alert-triage). Review\nrouting is the one cheap runtime control this service has, so it is the one switch.\n\n- POLICYHR_REVIEW_ROUTING is read once at settings load in three states: unset is on, a\n  boolean wins, emptied or unrecognised refuses at boot. Off binds a disabled router and logs\n  one warning per process, however many containers the agent tools build.\n- Under gcp, routing on with no HUMAN_REVIEW_URL refuses at boot. It used to surface as a 500\n  on the first escalated triage or entitlement, after the result had already been audited.\n- The triage and entitlement routes, both agent tools and both CLI commands hand off through a\n  recording wrapper that carries the console action label through, so a hand-off that fails\n  no longer fails the request: the result carries review_routing (routed, failed, off,\n  not_required) and an empty review_ref, and the failure is logged. The console states the\n  outcome in plain words.\n- Terraform gains review_routing_enabled, sets the service''s switch from it, and relaxes the\n  edge''s console requirement only when routing is stated off; a new plan test holds that.\n- pii-kit masking here is minimisation, not a redaction port, so it gains no switch.\n- SPEC, COMPLIANCE, ADOPTING, the runbook and the security FAQ no longer say the router refuses\n  at request time.","tree":{"sha":"9cf814869bcde70ac69a51b197c2eadadb6e15c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/trees/9cf814869bcde70ac69a51b197c2eadadb6e15c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/commits/f7e762f775429f3c165df8cb58aba87633f6073f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commit/f7e762f775429f3c165df8cb58aba87633f6073f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiIiNoAKGY3ZTc2MmY3NzU0MjlmM2MxNjVkZjhjYjU4YWJhODc2MzNmNjA3M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commit/5914df9fddadad8e8926450614dd0496a407b6a4","sha":"5914df9fddadad8e8926450614dd0496a407b6a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/5914df9fddadad8e8926450614dd0496a407b6a4"}],"sha":"f7e762f775429f3c165df8cb58aba87633f6073f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/f7e762f775429f3c165df8cb58aba87633f6073f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/5914df9fddadad8e8926450614dd0496a407b6a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T03:50:45Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T04:03:57Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Take the default off the audit bucket lock\n\nworm_locked defaulted to true, so the first apply of this stack in any\nproject locked its audit bucket irreversibly for the whole retention window,\nwith nothing in that deployment''s own tfvars saying so. The fleet decided on\n2026-09-12 that an irreversible control takes no default; this stack was one\nof 33 that sweep never reached.\n\nA plan now refuses until the deployment states the lock. The Terraform tests\nstate it once per file in the production form, still assert that a stated\nlock sits on the six-month floor, and gain a run proving the unlocked posture\ncreates an unlocked bucket. That run fails if the lock is ever hard-coded\nback into the bucket, which every other run would miss.","tree":{"sha":"963cb88f3aef1addc83c1fffc44f7c871773da3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/trees/963cb88f3aef1addc83c1fffc44f7c871773da3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/commits/5914df9fddadad8e8926450614dd0496a407b6a4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commit/5914df9fddadad8e8926450614dd0496a407b6a4","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiIiNoAKDU5MTRkZjlmZGRhZGFkOGU4OTI2NDUwNjE0ZGQwNDk2YTQwN2I2YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commit/0698b501fa2e12b138feeacbe6daf541431b3355","sha":"0698b501fa2e12b138feeacbe6daf541431b3355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/0698b501fa2e12b138feeacbe6daf541431b3355"}],"sha":"5914df9fddadad8e8926450614dd0496a407b6a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/5914df9fddadad8e8926450614dd0496a407b6a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://gi