mmit/dc46a5737b657df091c5e99197d0471f6a67f406","sha":"dc46a5737b657df091c5e99197d0471f6a67f406","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/dc46a5737b657df091c5e99197d0471f6a67f406"}],"sha":"de3104107b5fa96c3712b5583df36fbe775ad846","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/de3104107b5fa96c3712b5583df36fbe775ad846"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/dc46a5737b657df091c5e99197d0471f6a67f406/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:13:29Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:13:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#12)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 449 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","tree":{"sha":"956855430f58f75fb3b4727f90893c12a141e5f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/trees/956855430f58f75fb3b4727f90893c12a141e5f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/commits/dc46a5737b657df091c5e99197d0471f6a67f406","verification":{"payload":"tree 956855430f58f75fb3b4727f90893c12a141e5f2\nparent 37036cb9004e7b6baafac1be59e4eec05e954b33\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787670809 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787670809 +0800\n\nBind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#12)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 449 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbEZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAussQAI1yOesdpvWbfR/LefG2NINu\nuB2lssP5tghPW/LUo1LKtw/MKWtRmDJx3hh89nTLwpMdCMB2PI63PB/QakHouLjT\n6qHrKfOS74n/U2yUjkFo8mqWeh/vAvKnOlsWAQyDa6prMoFe4UF/VVOa0C7jJ5G9\nh176dGoUr95/1Ty51OEXPsjhC67C/EXf4YiDt6rH1FD0MQA7w96mxJxvW0ihSd8w\nsEGc+1Hrhub922cSbcpFcR2/P83sQaxR5hmA4laV30B4Z/NihSgM5yQvWhDZJ5/W\nt4FrHMh09FVJY3t6LP8juipR85PyLbH136RWI2I68jx1H7dGfwxTzZPB/3aXyRtF\n/YvYGdrElvld8wiUkrV+2YGiw+GgVnDZHpIuOb6a/fRAtUtxpSJe5JxlnBq3vcsW\nf3DC+ukALGgx7loZZCMFN2txKsNi0268gUvVSpM94zPAOEtytGcS7JYqdU5sTAv7\nz7Nh+dgwx+JU21zsbomiz4VeRVRw7NUQxwcG1VcqzR+ff9nYD3M4hDQvGvHt10g9\neLipj8XS7nG5XdFZVI7B2WBzwwl4fMY5P931SBC62TKPEeCin0QAf2gOLIqQIdRS\nKyvpmhpRw3V40wUyCWM0xHB1PmbQa3ZWBwS8HXBR22FuuGPwSX37FAFIRg57f5Op\nnIlmsAVxn+bx37BcPvId\n=5H2A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:13:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commit/dc46a5737b657df091c5e99197d0471f6a67f406","node_id":"C_kwDOUAiIiNoAKGRjNDZhNTczN2I2NTdkZjA5MWM1ZTk5MTk3ZDA0NzFmNmE2N2Y0MDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commit/37036cb9004e7b6baafac1be59e4eec05e954b33","sha":"37036cb9004e7b6baafac1be59e4eec05e954b33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/37036cb9004e7b6baafac1be59e4eec05e954b33"}],"sha":"dc46a5737b657df091c5e99197d0471f6a67f406","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/dc46a5737b657df091c5e99197d0471f6a67f406"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/commits/37036cb9004e7b6baafac1be59e4eec05e954b33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:57:56Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:57:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Re-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#11)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3011355b6c9df5b50ee52c9cdf9c0149019ae08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/trees/e3011355b6c9df5b50ee52c9cdf9c0149019ae08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/hr-policy-answers/git/commits/37036cb9004e7b6baafac1be59e4eec05e954b33","verification":{"payload":"tree e3011355b6c9df5b50ee52c9cdf9c0149019ae08\nparent e7c6b434f3c863994b7ad4e6e250f056f01e5dfc\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787644676 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787644676 +0800\n\nRe-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#11)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjUsECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXBIQAJo6TV/LGVnp/fZh815LyTiW\nITpcq7Q1gj7Uxom/oK/iZNSuSW8m+T7NONRgAWWxhCtti2rnAnH/YAvSWNCJ/71A\nU4amPndvcimvpoDflXpESJkqlJq+zWesiEYgPQpakpL+rv9DTkBrF6FcAho2246X\nN+hrArDO0e5VD9/W1EQIkElo4QMgH+M7h0jYic3nujaDgKrRWJiXJbfh2GlWEBCc\nPYIlKfw2vMgQzxmHsgyMd3Qr+a29z207M/vWGsys72a18krVfckbT3gM+HnnmcNE\neArWOz53645W1YaEV3NYc5upzlU5BtTEONyumlZuMRbCKUiQUOJbthZBdM6+FOUE\nvsh/6gF5EX3CjIcDR/uQ4pdwPe29AjyEO/L4HjwcTtgJ2lFFgc/cl2WpTAmtG4pl\nb68qmIYPl+urvVw5Yu9BHrAW/L6noEKb2lrv8m76kfFFDhF4+V1ZdbOb+76ctdMA\nfi/IWh/ywm4TttDug0aT1ogoiokAB46bmlWBgD9EVg2tuHQpBXfb22ws6cOoOuCY\ng5XvR6FgJTfSB4kbUf3Pfgze3UuGRPyTon2AJWZ/7128WR06J48tER7a+BdSt2j3\nMLd37mK8pKqhxiYUwqWOSvENqGSs1oMZMdVf44w4zmGpJANcS4kwjPFFo4jE/W/i\nXiCWjTNJQu4vw6dcv+Gy\n=nJFj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T07:57:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos