//api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/c61a710722ac83ff4415a38be906f0b0938bf59e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:20:28Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:20:28Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"message":"feat(cmd): PRODUCT_CLASSIFICATION_MODE=kafka|permissive; remove the inventory-storage HTTP client (ADR-0035)\n\ncmd/wes: mode kafka wires the Postgres copy (in-memory without\nDATABASE_URL) as the lookup and starts the ProductClassified consumer under\nPRODUCT_CLASSIFICATION_CONSUMER_GROUP; it is stopped and drained during\ngraceful shutdown right after the integration consumer. Missing group or\nKAFKA_BROKERS is a boot error. permissive is unchanged.\n\ncmd/mcp: never starts a consumer; mode kafka reads the same copy table\nread-only when DATABASE_URL is set, permissive otherwise.\n\nBoth: http (and any other value) is rejected at boot with an error naming\nthe replacement (productclassificationcopy.ParseMode).\n\nRemoved internal/adapters/outbound/productclassification (HTTP client,\ncircuit breaker + retry, tests) and every INVENTORY_STORAGE_BASE_URL read\n(classification was its only use). Comments that described the live lookup\nare updated.\n\nTests: boot config (http/unknown rejected, kafka without group/brokers\nrejected), consumer start/stop and shutdown order, MCP mode selection;\nintegration (testcontainers Kafka + Postgres): ProductClassified on Kafka ->\nconsumer -> copy -> ReleaseNextWork''s WorkReleased carries hazmat/fragile,\nstale version ignored, unknown SKU gets no hints; MCP release reads the copy.","tree":{"sha":"8f19f06e744d6387fbdd4c5fcded06a7763466f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/8f19f06e744d6387fbdd4c5fcded06a7763466f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/gi