:"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3","sha":"31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3"}],"sha":"818b4e44b8b521863376737a1f3acf9b60e0bb1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/818b4e44b8b521863376737a1f3acf9b60e0bb1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/eb085d184e4fb561c1fc78ef7202f90a86f93ed7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:38:14Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:38:14Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"message":"docs(executive): add executive briefing deck\n\nAdds `executive/index.html`: a self-contained reveal.js executive deck covering strategy, architecture, observability, competitive position and next steps for this repo. Open it in a browser (loads reveal.js 6.0.0 from jsDelivr, pinned with an SRI hash; no vendored library code in this repo); no build step. Full source text is in the speaker notes (press S).\n\nNo code, config, workflow or chart changes; the folder is outside `.github/`, `charts/` and the docs site, so `repo_lint` and the docs build are unaffected. Fleet-wide gap analysis lives in `warehouse-docs/executive/competitive-gaps.html`.","tree":{"sha":"33e1578e88cf1bf54dacf269adc7f8d76afbbede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/33e1578e88cf1bf54dacf269adc7f8d76afbbede"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/eb085d184e4fb561c1fc78ef7202f90a86f93ed7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/eb085d184e4fb561c1fc78ef7202f90a86f93ed7","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBRNoAKGViMDg1ZDE4NGU0ZmI1NjFjMWZjNzhlZjcyMDJmOTBhODZmOTNlZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3","sha":"31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3"}],"sha":"eb085d184e4fb561c1fc78ef7202f90a86f93ed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/eb085d184e4fb561c1fc78ef7202f90a86f93ed7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:20:52Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:20:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: configurable pools, reserved RateDeviationDetected, ADR syntax fix (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#152)\n\n* feat(release): ConfigurePool domain rule and use case (ADR-0033)\n\nWorkPool.Configure sets mode + WIP limit (positive integer, known mode),\nnever evicts work, reports whether anything changed. The ConfigurePool use\ncase creates the pool when absent, is idempotent (no write on an identical\nrepeat) and runs under the pool optimistic-concurrency retry.\n\n* feat(http): PUT /paths/{pathId}/pool configures a pool (ADR-0033)\n\nConfigurePool REST endpoint: sets mode (ReleaseFed|FlowFed) and WIP limit,\ncreating the pool when absent. 400 invalid-wip-limit / unknown-feed-mode,\nidempotent, optimistic concurrency via the existing retry. OpenAPI updated;\nPostgres testcontainers integration tests prove create/update/idempotency,\nlowering below WIP without eviction, and a configure-vs-enqueue race.\n\n* docs: record audit decisions 10a/10c/8, ADR syntax fix, ConfigurePool docs pack\n\n- AsyncAPI: RateDeviationDetected (integration + analytics message) marked\n  \"Reserved: declared for a future detection rule (ADR 0020 defers it); not\n  emitted today.\"\n- DDD pack: RateDeviationDetected -> Decided: kept reserved;\n  UsableInventoryObserved -> Decided: read-only context by design (ADR-0006);\n  `events` table -> Decided: legacy, unused, retained, additive migrations only;\n  \"no code path creates a flow-fed pool\" -> Resolved (ADR-0033). Event storming\n  process 3, aggregate canvas (W9 + ConfigurePool command), sequence diagram 10,\n  class diagram, bounded-context canvas, ER table, api index/events pages.\n- ADR 0004 and 0021: `:::warning Title` -> `:::warning[Title]` (syntax only, no\n  wording change). ADR 0004 also had `:::caution Recorded honestly`, same defect,\n  fixed the same way.\n\n* fix: stop tracking apis/tooling/node_modules (accidentally committed)\n\nThe branch had committed ~9,200 vendored files from `npm ci` in apis/tooling. Remove them from the index (files stay on disk) and ignore the directory so it cannot be re-added.","tree":{"sha":"e67060d6855cdac8a9d95fe0784578c3c93e4fc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/e67060d6855cdac8a9d95fe0784578c3c93e4fc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3","verification":{"payload":"tree e67060d6855cdac8a9d95fe0784578c3c93e4fc1\nparent 6c986a545acada839e6cb684034fc2b0151e9ee4\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791328852 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791328852 -0300\n\nfeat: configurable pools, reserved RateDeviationDetected, ADR syntax fix (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#152)\n\n* feat(release): ConfigurePool domain rule and use case (ADR-0033)\n\nWorkPool.Configure sets mode + WIP limit (positive integer, known mode),\nnever evicts work, reports whether anything changed. The ConfigurePool use\ncase creates the pool when absent, is idempotent (no write on an identical\nrepeat) and runs under the pool optimistic-concurrency retry.\n\n* feat(http): PUT /paths/{pathId}/pool configures a pool (ADR-0033)\n\nConfigurePool REST endpoint: sets mode (ReleaseFed|FlowFed) and WIP limit,\ncreating the pool when absent. 400 invalid-wip-limit / unknown-feed-mode,\nidempotent, optimistic concurrency via the existing retry. OpenAPI updated;\nPostgres testcontainers integration tests prove create/update/idempotency,\nlowering below WIP without eviction, and a configure-vs-enqueue race.\n\n* docs: record audit decisions 10a/10c/8, ADR syntax fix, ConfigurePool docs pack\n\n- AsyncAPI: RateDeviationDetected (integration + analytics message) marked\n  \"Reserved: declared for a future detection rule (ADR 0020 defers it); not\n  emitted today.\"\n- DDD pack: RateDeviationDetected -> Decided: kept reserved;\n  UsableInventoryObserved -> Decided: read-only context by design (ADR-0006);\n  `events` table -> Decided: legacy, unused, retained, additive migrations only;\n  \"no code path creates a flow-fed pool\" -> Resolved (ADR-0033). Event storming\n  process 3, aggregate canvas (W9 + ConfigurePool command), sequence diagram 10,\n  class diagram, bounded-context canvas, ER table, api index/events pages.\n- ADR 0004 and 0021: `:::warning Title` -> `:::warning[Title]` (syntax only, no\n  wording change). ADR 0004 also had `:::caution Recorded honestly`, same defect,\n  fixed the same way.\n\n* fix: stop tracking apis/tooling/node_modules (accidentally committed)\n\nThe branch had committed ~9,200 vendored files from `npm ci` in apis/tooling. Remove them from the index (files stay on disk) and ignore the directory so it cannot be re-added.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxYJUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFP0QAFYjtqSy54DGUyBrzCqQ+fPq\n9fMrhWTunoWRr5km0cdqrOUcSsUdc+MqwO/yTXpw+orl/LpT14+J3fij7j+pKu20\nYNghkKHbxPQ0XqRLLaXmicCEUPw4/FinVGYifxW3j+d3yHmLqw1hk2179bj4Kk2u\ncPVtrw2X9kDU/hycMrYf5NOa6CZJcoiMxRoX24LIWNQcqvK/PYkfWgeK4mIebyf9\niuUexXqcNmS0Cnwm9hm0UD1EGbVlrSbyC61kbZGgRkG5Dr4aTrj3d1N3CSD2eF7x\nBeBdHKuttWu80bG95ojDkLC7jQSNLIAddUjArZ8hO4ay/WUEplOPOSCPUq7K7wQZ\nTc7LWLgTryMR6gnNVogidIJHd0CJorBLlgwgWBmRHXTGcYW1ORR89I2nfRJ1F7cv\nVqW4z8UR+ny1glaEeUoxwzvjWtHC71E8jDqdR9YNtTirJLNYY4U1RgNKO41BSZ1z\ntJa++lH0FLm/3bnkvOmrcH208eV4dl2uwlglBhBbTh0Xuww1EiwHMDhbbjAyP21V\nhjNpVNJu4ZgDpBJ5iP01H0DyBaX3InpckdKbRp9bnQeRT8gGCtOSTnuUy49ptxNi\nzohBOph45dP2GB974rY3kZWn/N697m1yn+HPC1EJSOOGBtfPJ+s88XiRw4vrJMJF\nt4N+1QxLDwv40X5tLghM\n=P1UI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T23:20:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBRNoAKDMxZjcyMWM3ZTYwZTQ3ZTQ0NmVjMWRhZjUwMWZkYWY2MTNhYTE3ZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/6c986a545acada839e6cb684034fc2b0151e9ee4","sha":"6c986a545acada839e6cb684034fc2b0151e9ee4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/6c986a545acada839e6cb684034fc2b0151e9ee4"}],"sha":"31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/31f721c7e60e47e446ec1daf501fdaf613aa17f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/6c986a545acada839e6cb684034fc2b0151e9ee4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T22:40:14Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T22:40:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: consume NIP WorkDemandReleased into transfer-referenced work units (#150)\n\n* feat: consume NIP WorkDemandReleased into transfer-referenced work units\n\nnetwork-inventory-planning releases inter-site transfer legs as\nWorkDemandReleased on warehouse.network-inventory-planning.events;\nApplyWorkDemandReleased enqueues one WorkUnit per demand through the\nexisting EnqueueWorkUnit under the deterministic id demand_id (reference\n= demand_id), with the processed-event mark + enqueue atomic\n(onceAtomically, ADR-0028), path_id validated via the PathCatalogue and\nwork_kind against the declared enum before any write; duplicate CE id or\ndifferent-CE-same-demand is a benign no-op exactly like\nApplyOrderAllocated (ADR-0033).\n\nTransfer metadata (transfer_ref, work_kind, site_id, quantity) is\nadditive on WorkUnit (SetSKU-style setters), threaded through\nEnqueueWorkUnitRequest, persisted by migration 0011 (NOT NULL safe\ndefaults), and rehydrated by the postgres/memory repos (work_kind\nvalidated on read like state).\n\nworkReleasedData gains OPTIONAL transfer_ref/work_kind/site_id/quantity\non the SAME v1 type/dataschema, present only on transfer-referenced\nunits — non-transfer payloads stay byte-identical (pinned by a legacy-\nshape golden byte-compat test). AsyncAPI documents the consumed message\nand the optional fields; ADR-0033 records the decision; the inbound\nintegration tests create the fifth topic so the consumer group\nstabilizes.\n\n* fix(api): allow consumed events to carry producer urns\n\nCloudEventBase''s dataschema pattern and source enum only admitted this\nrepo''s own identifiers; a consumed message (NIP WorkDemandReleased)\ncarries the PRODUCER''s urn and source by fleet contract. Widen both to\nthe fleet-wide shapes: any /warehouse/<repo> source, any\nurn:warehouse:<repo>:<events|analytics>:<Event>:v<N> dataschema.\nPublished messages are unchanged and still constrained.\n\n* fix: adapt scan-test to widened scanWorkUnit signature post-rebase","tree":{"sha":"b5ecfba6c2257633a3492c8df5b99de6fc556820","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/b5ecfba6c2257633a3492c8df5b99de6fc556820"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/6c986a545acada839e6cb684034fc2b0151e9ee4","verification":{"payload":"tree b5ecfba6c2257633a3492c8df5b99de6fc556820\nparent d2e80c459b2019cc9ec99566bf7fb69e29c1f35b\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791326414 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791326414 -0300\n\nfeat: consume NIP WorkDemandReleased into transfer-referenced work units (#150)\n\n* feat: consume NIP WorkDemandReleased into transfer-referenced work units\n\nnetwork-inventory-planning releases inter-site transfer legs as\nWorkDemandReleased on warehouse.network-inventory-planning.events;\nApplyWorkDemandReleased enqueues one WorkUnit per demand through the\nexisting EnqueueWorkUnit under the deterministic id demand_id (reference\n= demand_id), with the processed-event mark + enqueue atomic\n(onceAtomically, ADR-0028), path_id validated via the PathCatalogue and\nwork_kind against the declared enum before any write; duplicate CE id or\ndifferent-CE-same-demand is a benign no-op exactly like\nApplyOrderAllocated (ADR-0033).\n\nTransfer metadata (transfer_ref, work_kind, site_id, quantity) is\nadditive on WorkUnit (SetSKU-style setters), threaded through\nEnqueueWorkUnitRequest, persisted by migration 0011 (NOT NULL safe\ndefaults), and rehydrated by the postgres/memory repos (work_kind\nvalidated on read like state).\n\nworkReleasedData gains OPTIONAL transfer_ref/work_kind/site_id/quantity\non the SAME v1 type/dataschema, present only on transfer-referenced\nunits — non-transfer payloads stay byte-identical (pinned by a legacy-\nshape golden byte-compat test). AsyncAPI documents the consumed message\nand the optional fields; ADR-0033 records the decision; the inbound\nintegration tests create the fifth topic so the consumer group\nstabilizes.\n\n* fix(api): allow consumed events to carry producer urns\n\nCloudEventBase''s dataschema pattern and source enum only admitted this\nrepo''s own identifiers; a consumed message (NIP WorkDemandReleased)\ncarries the PRODUCER''s urn and source by fleet contract. Widen both to\nthe fleet-wide shapes: any /warehouse/<repo> source, any\nurn:warehouse:<repo>:<events|analytics>:<Event>:v<N> dataschema.\nPublished messages are unchanged and still constrained.\n\n* fix: adapt scan-test to widened scanWorkUnit signature post-rebase","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxXjOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlzkQABoVDszwPBF6OjE+4CCDZQOn\nLczckHteaTWflGaa+pPSepwk1CJbnwpX2upUG3sCYl3iZ0F17XEeX3DDrI15/TVO\nk+e89Hh2CfitJ8H+ypzt7UaczDhDfZoqGxyaqDs3ynrsP/GXsGCAGnXU1/0p4Dux\nN5Dh3LJcWsyQK6AUsI36Vtpjsw0Bl1XdbD2XWbApk74s8GgKbrLNP43PjA7saUIX\nx5DfSgBygFjF6SIUwIqJFbrUX917gBlnDzZM+aylo7UdgMN0u7gi6mPI4iuOMbz6\n26zu7YXQ5OehJQwgpTZQf3tzdI64I8OB8fhtvT9ChpOOMV9tOb8BUjDO5KlnX7WO\njF/FpJUPMBmYOLjc/fxqXwUccKRU2x2SEu749Mt3sMU0vTof4nXPcqvR/xzh+iPR\n73Wv7tZqPkOWAJrwL128ogmgSD42RXqBo8n5r25WzKFH88HN6yC0Q6b/zuqMtn5L\nxheMGbF6LCObsnf1K5o8RhxozzhlnGGHDRJEufjg6zFx7gwc6aNAEPIDJRbvgcni\nGCwPlaU7FTk3T21NXLl3nBC3xFlt8OARNZzf3fQ1A0Hjr4mcX6Dt7JxqlTjs34G6\n8fPgyQYCJIAN4fiAQAcLdRtu/nqS+c1NusYPAMR+hL/feot3DQB2Nz3ivFuaNchk\nHsigl2h5uTDuZ5U53JLe\n=yTLH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T22:40:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gi