gin":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/9ce3e575b40aa3416fe543d1baac52bf48dbf989","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBRNoAKDljZTNlNTc1YjQwYWEzNDE2ZmU1NDNkMWJhYWM1MmJmNDhkYmY5ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/fd75d6eca027edcbb4ebcaaec960bd270ec8b532","sha":"fd75d6eca027edcbb4ebcaaec960bd270ec8b532","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/fd75d6eca027edcbb4ebcaaec960bd270ec8b532"}],"sha":"9ce3e575b40aa3416fe543d1baac52bf48dbf989","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/9ce3e575b40aa3416fe543d1baac52bf48dbf989"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/fd75d6eca027edcbb4ebcaaec960bd270ec8b532/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:22:31Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:22:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: ADR conformance fixes (2026-10 audit) — all items except ADR-0019 (#136)\n\n* fix(postgres): persist work_units.gift_wrap so WorkReleased and GET /work-units carry it (ADR-0010)\n\n* fix(mcp): publish MCP-raised events through the outbox, add otelchi to the MCP router (ADR-0008, ADR-0014, ADR-0013)\n\n* fix(release): clamp RemainingCapacity to max(0, wipLimit-WIP) (ADR-0018)\n\n* docs(ecosystem): name GET /reports/throughput as the FlowFed observed-throughput signal (ADR-0020)\n\n* fix(kafka): key integration-topic events by aggregate id, not event id (ADR-0024)\n\n* fix(kafka): log DLQ hand-off at ERROR; wait for consumer.Run before shutdown teardown; fix stale ADR-0023 text (ADR-0023)\n\n* fix(http): document Idempotency-Key and its 400/422 problems, route them through the problem catalogue, allow the header in CORS (ADR-0005, ADR-0022)\n\n* fix(telemetry): otelchi RED metrics on the reports router; move wes.work_units.released behind ports.ReleaseMetrics, key path.id (ADR-0013)\n\n* docs(adr): fix drift in 0001/0004/0007/0008/0012, add ADR-0030 (Kafka path catalogue, bootretry) and ADR-0031 (OrderAllocated choreography), index template link\n\n* feat(outbox): add wes.outbox.lag_seconds gauge behind the OutboxRelay (ADR-0014 follow-up)\n\n* feat(housekeeping): sweep expired idempotency_keys (24h) and long-published outbox_events (7d), env-configurable (ADR-0032)\n\n* fix: align capacity integration test with aggregate key; declare Idempotency-Key optional in schema (in-memory contract config does not enforce it)","tree":{"sha":"c22b799088d0a8e5d7dc6842e1b2926b5f2144cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/c22b799088d0a8e5d7dc6842e1b2926b5f2144cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/fd75d6eca027edcbb4ebcaaec960bd270ec8b532","verification":{"payload":"tree c22b799088d0a8e5d7dc6842e1b2926b5f2144cd\nparent 07aa7ba8de77000bb86929588709e5e914fc35e5\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791156151 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791156151 -0300\n\nfix: ADR conformance fixes (2026-10 audit) — all items except ADR-0019 (#136)\n\n* fix(postgres): persist work_units.gift_wrap so WorkReleased and GET /work-units carry it (ADR-0010)\n\n* fix(mcp): publish MCP-raised events through the outbox, add otelchi to the MCP router (ADR-0008, ADR-0014, ADR-0013)\n\n* fix(release): clamp RemainingCapacity to max(0, wipLimit-WIP) (ADR-0018)\n\n* docs(ecosystem): name GET /reports/throughput as the FlowFed observed-throughput signal (ADR-0020)\n\n* fix(kafka): key integration-topic events by aggregate id, not event id (ADR-0024)\n\n* fix(kafka): log DLQ hand-off at ERROR; wait for consumer.Run before shutdown teardown; fix stale ADR-0023 text (ADR-0023)\n\n* fix(http): document Idempotency-Key and its 400/422 problems, route them through the problem catalogue, allow the header in CORS (ADR-0005, ADR-0022)\n\n* fix(telemetry): otelchi RED metrics on the reports router; move wes.work_units.released behind ports.ReleaseMetrics, key path.id (ADR-0013)\n\n* docs(adr): fix drift in 0001/0004/0007/0008/0012, add ADR-0030 (Kafka path catalogue, bootretry) and ADR-0031 (OrderAllocated choreography), index template link\n\n* feat(outbox): add wes.outbox.lag_seconds gauge behind the OutboxRelay (ADR-0014 follow-up)\n\n* feat(housekeeping): sweep expired idempotency_keys (24h) and long-published outbox_events (7d), env-configurable (ADR-0032)\n\n* fix: align capacity integration test with aggregate key; d