ite_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/a54eec62a2f24d0dd347ff865b3a7842fb9802f7","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBRNoAKGE1NGVlYzYyYTJmMjRkMGRkMzQ3ZmY4NjViM2E3ODQyZmI5ODAyZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/f8be60aba090088c5bcef246eaa8cd743b23cd25","sha":"f8be60aba090088c5bcef246eaa8cd743b23cd25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/f8be60aba090088c5bcef246eaa8cd743b23cd25"}],"sha":"a54eec62a2f24d0dd347ff865b3a7842fb9802f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/a54eec62a2f24d0dd347ff865b3a7842fb9802f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/f8be60aba090088c5bcef246eaa8cd743b23cd25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T22:42:54Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T22:42:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(kafka): commit the processed-event mark atomically with handling so a retried failure is never swallowed (#121)\n\nEvery inbound consumer path marked the CloudEvents id in processed_events\nFIRST, as its own committed write, and only then ran the effect. A failure\nafter the mark made handleWithRetry''s next attempt see \"already processed\"\nand return nil, so the DLQ was never reached, the offset was committed and\nthe event was silently lost. For TaskCompleted that left the WorkUnit\nReleased and its WIP slot taken (the soak-run WIP ratchet, now reachable\nfrom any transient error); for OrderAllocated the order lines were never\nenqueued. ObserveLaborPlan/ObserveInventoryChange had the same shape.\n\n- usecases.onceAtomically: TryMarkProcessed + effect in ONE UnitOfWork\n  scope (mark rolls back with the effect); without a UnitOfWork the\n  in-memory mark is undone via the optional ports.ProcessedEventReleaser.\n- New ApplyTaskCompleted / ApplyOrderAllocated use cases own the\n  idempotency that used to live in the Kafka adapter; ObserveLaborPlan /\n  ObserveInventoryChange gain WithUnitOfWork and use the same primitive.\n  cmd/wes wires all four with repos.uow.\n- TaskCompleted for an unknown work unit (ErrNotFound, e.g. a PACK task\n  keyed by order id) is an INFO-logged, processed skip: no retry, no DLQ.\n  task_type is read from the payload for that log. Every other error\n  propagates, is retried, and is dead-lettered.\n- Consumer dispatch extracted from handleMessage behind a dlqWriter\n  interface so the retry->DLQ path is unit-tested with a fake writer.\n- ADR-0028; AsyncAPI consumer-semantics prose and event docs updated\n  (no contract change).\n- Tests: use-case atomicity under both wirings, consumer retry/DLQ/skip,\n  and a Postgres+Kafka testcontainers integration test. Reverting to the\n  old mark-first shape fails 12 unit tests and the integration test.","tree":{"sha":"e7527a7ee81138186ccb1b4ca43645f892246088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/e7527a7ee81138186ccb1b4ca43645f892246088"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/f8be60aba090088c5bcef246eaa8cd743b23cd25","verification":{"payload":"tree e7527a7ee81138186ccb1b4ca43645f892246088\nparent 5be0524d6a1793c38d6253bc301230a55e505831\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790894574 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790894574 -0300\n\nfix(kafka): commit the processed-event mark atomically with handling so a retried failure is never swallowed (#121)\n\nEvery inbound consumer path marked the CloudEvents id in processed_events\nFIRST, as its own committed write, and only then ran the effect. A failure\nafter the mark made handleWithRetry''s next attempt see \"already processed\"\nand return nil, so the DLQ was never reached, the offset was committed and\nthe event was silently lost. For TaskCompleted that left the WorkUnit\nReleased and its WIP slot taken (the soak-run WIP ratchet, now reachable\nfrom any transient error); for OrderAllocated the order lines were never\nenqueued. ObserveLaborPlan/ObserveInventoryChange had the same shape.\n\n- usecases.onceAtomically: TryMarkProcessed + effect in ONE UnitOfWork\n  scope (mark rolls back with the effect); without a UnitOfWork the\n  in-memory mark is undone via the optional ports.ProcessedEventReleaser.\n- New ApplyTaskCompleted / ApplyOrderAllocated use cases own the\n  idempotency that used to live in the Kafka adapter; ObserveLaborPlan /\n  ObserveInventoryChange gain WithUnitOfWork and use the same primitive.\n  cmd/wes wires all four with repos.uow.\n- TaskCompleted for an unknown work unit (ErrNotFound, e.g. a PACK task\n  keyed by order id) is an INFO-logged, processed skip: no retry, no DLQ.\n  task_type is read from the payload for that log. Every other error\n  propagates, is retried, and is dead-lettered.\n- Consumer dispatch extracted from handleMessage behind a dlqWriter\n  interface so the retry->DLQ path is unit-tested with a fake writer.\n- ADR-0028; AsyncAPI consumer-semantics prose and event docs updated\n  (no contract change).\n- Tests: use-case atomicity under both wirings, consumer retry/DLQ/skip,\n  and a Postgres+Kafka testcontainers integration test. Reverting to the\n  old mark-first shape fails 12 unit tests and the integration test.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvuHuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4VAQADOfbK/igjYPg/cMjMHTd3EY\nZ7OZ91UvNxuIvPQ1dFYw6e3QPFDUsQazLUhT7bB2hJl5LySXlzMUQX7Xa+BJuUiV\nN+efU7F8aBswHBak5/gnvWiWsdyKs0oYwKAYM8bl/1Z8xqTtaGyrH07GgWRQMRli\nouHcjTpjkDTIMBmQ1yqvEHSEl4FHJe50TYODKZyPuZGQxf3ovrYE3dFiSbzn+KRZ\np7sGq2ImfSkAKsuH3DS43HuTE/bUhBUCJkMj8Fdc+S+SE/wEo785C2SVxMJ0hABQ\n74zhUCn6Q2Uy/Ux+zEpXA0hyIIykIwdh9nYBVF3+/x4NXv+a0JG7CRdF4t+uXRhj\nP9xPu/HKXWuX80pejQSR+qRkUNdqYGVkBPaxKkbdfGsluNb4Y9hHErgoHDc9U2NG\n8i/rMXxOyoZO6t2OPgw6hXQLYxvLrVkL5v/RYsSnWnuIg/5kQMXZv6j7Mfmmb+Bm\ni/Q2VfW19ALodIjVxkurSpvUQmND3fxS0XaipMnoXYWf3f6EZPrWszTSEfAl5qM8\nINf2Syb+3wZVS7AcPKiwPZ3TDOIAk6IvbtoGgqcj5OwKHZ7bGlk3p+/D4siGfGfy\nzRnrWPoYtUAUS1hUi1yvoEzO53FR0QVa6iFHa5ErFPm2P3rf0aWA7N5JOWLhfio7\nwXdN7rhECfDhyczByKKC\n=A5Z5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T22:42:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com