UAjBRNoAKGEzYTUwZDYxZWZiNjY1NmZhOTU3NjM5YTZkNzM0NjA3ZTM3ZDZhNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/f7f0704b856eb9a0d216dd4e34c484fd6de705c2","sha":"f7f0704b856eb9a0d216dd4e34c484fd6de705c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/f7f0704b856eb9a0d216dd4e34c484fd6de705c2"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/d1ae280852832f186b4ec56569e01e45a32888fe","sha":"d1ae280852832f186b4ec56569e01e45a32888fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/d1ae280852832f186b4ec56569e01e45a32888fe"}],"sha":"a3a50d61efb6656fa957639a6d734607e37d6a49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/a3a50d61efb6656fa957639a6d734607e37d6a49"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/f7f0704b856eb9a0d216dd4e34c484fd6de705c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:21:50Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:21:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#113)\n\nFleet-wide bug fix, ported from order-management PR #115 (ADR-0029).\ngolang-migrate''s postgres driver takes a session-scoped pg_advisory_lock\nto serialize concurrent migration runs at boot, but DATABASE_URL\n(warehouse-infra PR #43, PgBouncer rollout) points this service at\nPgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode, which does not preserve session\nstate across statements. Two or more wes-work-planning api replicas\nstarting concurrently (an HPA scale-out per ADR-0025, or an ordinary\nrolling deploy with replicas>1) would crash-loop with pq: unnamed\nprepared statement does not exist / pq: canceling statement due to\nstatement timeout for ~1-2 minutes until one wins the advisory-lock\nrace.\n\ncmd/wes/main.go''s wireRepositories (the only migration-running call site\nin this repo -- cmd/mcp opens the pgxpool but never runs migrations\nitself; cmd/wes-projector/cmd/wes-reports already migrate the analytics\nstore via ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL, which was never routed through\nPgBouncer) now reads a new MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env var for the\nmigration step only, falling back to DATABASE_URL when unset:\n\n    migrationsDatabaseURL := getenv(\"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\", databaseURL)\n\nThe pgxpool built right after migrations complete still uses databaseURL\nunchanged -- every request this service serves keeps going through\nPgBouncer exactly as before. The fallback keeps local dev, CI\nintegration tests, and any environment that doesn''t provision the split\nworking byte-identically to before this change.\n\ncharts/wes-work-planning: new database.migrationsExistingSecretKey value\n(default \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders the env var in the api\nDeployment only, sourced from the same existingSecret, with\noptional: true on the secretKeyRef so a secret that predates this key\nstill starts the pod. The mcp Deployment''s template is deliberately left\nuntouched (cmd/mcp has no migration step to redirect).\n\nwarehouse-infra PR #44 (already merged) provisions MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\nas a direct, non-pooled DSN for all 9 OLTP services, wes-work-planning\nincluded -- confirmed live in terraform.tfstate. No warehouse-infra work\nneeded for this PR.\n\nAdds:\n- TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback: proves the getenv fallback in both\n  directions.\n- TestWireRepositories_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations:\n  proves wireRepositories itself threads migrationsDatabaseURL into the\n  migration step (not databaseURL).\n- ADR-0026: documents the pg_advisory_lock / transaction-pooling\n  incompatibility, cross-references order-management ADR-0029 and\n  warehouse-infra PR #43/#44.\n\nhelm lint and helm template ... | grep MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL both\nverified locally.\n\nmake check, make check-all (coverage gate, arch-test, bdd) and\nmake integration (real Postgres via docker compose + testcontainers)\nall pass.","tree":{"sha":"107ce4535a551e9b03cd06ffce5dacd070845b2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/107ce4535a551e9b03cd06ffce5dacd070845b2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/f7f0704b856eb9a0d216dd4e34c484fd6de705c2","verification":{"payload":"tree 107ce4535a551e9b03cd06ffce5dacd070845b2c\nparent 550b5e7716b4ceee1d0f982a78d15dedf1e0e00a\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790601710 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790601710 -0300\n\nfix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#113)\n\nFleet-wide bug fix, ported from order-management PR #115 (ADR-0029).\ngolang-migrate''s postgres driver takes a session-scoped pg_advisory_lock\nto serialize concurrent migration runs at boot, but DATABASE_URL\n(warehouse-infra PR #43, PgBouncer rollout) points this service at\nPgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode, which does not preserve session\nstate across statements. Two or more wes-work-planning api replicas\nstarting concurrently (an HPA scale-out per ADR-0025, or an ordinary\nrolling deploy with replicas>1) would crash-loop with pq: unnamed\nprepared statement does not exist / pq: canceling statement due to\nstatement timeout for ~1-2 minutes until one wins the advisory-lock\nrace.\n\ncmd/wes/main.go''s wireRepositories (the only migration-running call site\nin this repo -- cmd/mcp opens the pgxpool but never runs migrations\nitself; cmd/wes-projector/cmd/wes-reports already migrate the analytics\nstore via ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL, which was never routed through\nPgBouncer) now reads a new MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env var for the\nmigration step only, falling back to DATABASE_URL when unset:\n\n    migrationsDatabaseURL := getenv(\"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\", databaseURL)\n\nThe pgxpool built right after migrations complete still uses databaseURL\nunchanged -- every request this service serves keeps going through\nPgBouncer exactly as before. The fallback keeps local dev, CI\nintegration tests, and any environment that doesn''t provision the split\nworking byte-identically to before this change.\n\ncharts/wes-work-planning: new database.migrationsExistingSecretKey value\n(default \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders the env var in the api\nDeployment only, sourced from the same existingSecret, with\noptional: true on the secretKeyRef so a secret that predates this key\nstill starts the pod. The mcp Deployment''s template is deliberately left\nuntouched (cmd/mcp has no migration step to redirect).\n\nwarehouse-infra PR #44 (already merged) provisions MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\nas a direct, non-pooled DSN for all 9 OLTP services, wes-work-planning\nincluded -- confirmed live in terraform.tfstate. No warehouse-infra work\nneeded for this PR.\n\nAdds:\n- TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback: proves the getenv fallback in both\n  directions.\n- TestWireRepositories_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations:\n  proves wireRepositories itself threads migrationsDatabaseURL into the\n  migration step (not databaseURL).\n- ADR-0026: documents the pg_advisory_lock / transaction-pooling\n  incompatibility, cross-references order-management ADR-0029 and\n  warehouse-infra PR #43/#44.\n\nhelm lint and helm template ... | grep MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL both\nverified locally.\n\nmake check, make check-all (coverage gate, arch-test, bdd) and\nmake integration (real Postgres via docker compose + testcontainers)\nall pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqumnuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyo8QADYQ0iImDpbUEQe1lXfZpWfg\nes99E+ru5G6qLMVftOtz4XYVhsHKEdkq3bB71eO47g5kNOuuMQ0TJalN55OkmPjV\nHnK7nWRuvgKYXidFB2D6GTxL9DUtqZuJ+tRkbeUwGo988xnyK+4fZ3OtS3QYt2tV\nRXS8J/QBnP5a3hl9x9xpO4giDeDoBaJidF1UL340azz+tMLcm529Kch0mJ+xx9xf\nx+cEfoovS4lZPl42p8KGQVvS8VPuhvUsBVgcw91vQFcFDrbXYQALN/e85LO4SF9e\nOd9mbuPGxpV7Pu1uqpv8TNngvKRrBaYukqufCav7CaUhoVZdVYO4TPKLvhxGHONB\nKBULznnTJAfpotcNZYPxleEyexyZTN4ET8F21bVcHUroiVCY+c4YsHTTbKOeyG34\n8Vq3Rm0pibYfY0E2fgBo2PiGhIc1rfpu7IJyVmOTfJPcszuGPs9uUKrFWYQU6XPL\nf352Dd7d5POQIsKZRXAmEi9Mx/vemDBK18CCXvGLUH6pmWv1bXf84ox48DA/KfFV\nN6iewUshX+5arDJTtLRWg/OfdJOH7/6WRZYlvtpSoRb8tv6uv0yRH3Z+J8LAfbSp\n8NL9Qzarm3iI9tZdkfTq+vhG84wSd4jtcR+Rv+3MOYbt3p7Ucq6ZustVf9u1gyIe\nyLoRARA0xiKjgLbWkkVC\n=Xz3o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T13:21:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_ev