rs_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/326e5322ced14eebbce3c4548cfbb32090ee1174","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBRNoAKDMyNmU1MzIyY2VkMTRlZWJiY2UzYzQ1NDhjZmJiMzIwOTBlZTExNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/43fc4c545cb142eeb56439bcb0021f02a6f506ec","sha":"43fc4c545cb142eeb56439bcb0021f02a6f506ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/43fc4c545cb142eeb56439bcb0021f02a6f506ec"}],"sha":"326e5322ced14eebbce3c4548cfbb32090ee1174","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/326e5322ced14eebbce3c4548cfbb32090ee1174"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/43fc4c545cb142eeb56439bcb0021f02a6f506ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:59:37Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:59:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (ADR 0025) (#110)\n\nPorts order-management''s Phase 3 scalability reference (PR #110, ADR-0026)\nto wes-work-planning.\n\nHPA (autoscaling/v2), one per independently-assessed workload, all\ndefault-disabled via values.yaml so this PR changes nothing on merge:\n\n- api: min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU. Stateless OLTP; its only per-process\n  cache (PATH_CATALOGUE_SOURCE=kafka) already uses a per-process-unique\n  consumer group, and its inbound integration-event consumer uses the\n  fleet''s normal stable shared group. Safe at N>1.\n- analytics-projector: min 1 / max 2 / 70% CPU. Its Kafka consumer group\n  (wes-analytics) is verified stable/shared, and every write is\n  idempotent on event_id, so N replicas share partitions safely. Capped\n  at 2 (not 4) since aggregate-id-keyed ordering and a lightweight\n  upsert workload don''t justify more.\n- analytics-reports: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Stateless read-only reader.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Static asset serving, no state.\n- mcp: deliberately EXCLUDED (no autoscaling.mcp block). Verified from\n  the actual code (internal/adapters/inbound/mcp/server.go) that it\n  wraps the same modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk StreamableHTTPHandler with\n  in-memory per-process Mcp-Session-Id state as order-management''s MCP,\n  behind a plain ClusterIP Service with no sessionAffinity — the exact\n  same real risk, excluded the same way.\n\nEvery Deployment template guards its `replicas:` field with\n`{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so a static replica\ncount never fights the HPA controller. Verified with `helm template`\nboth flags off (0 HPAs, every Deployment keeps replicas:1) and all four\nflags on (exactly 4 HPAs render, those 4 Deployments lose `replicas:`,\nmcp''s Deployment keeps it) and mixed enablement.\n\npgxpool MaxConns + statement_timeout, matching order-management''s exact\nnumbers and AfterConnect-hook pattern:\n\n- OLTP pool (postgres.Connect, cmd/wes + cmd/mcp): MaxConns=10,\n  statement_timeout=5s. Already fronted by PgBouncer (warehouse-infra\n  PR #43, transaction pooling, pool_size=12) via the existing\n  DATABASE_URL Secret — no code change needed for that part. PgBouncer,\n  not this client-side setting, bounds the real server-side connection\n  count, so MaxConns stays generous rather than squeezed defensively.\n- Analytics writer (analyticsstore.NewPool, cmd/wes-projector):\n  MaxConns=5, statement_timeout=10s. Direct to Postgres (no PgBouncer,\n  per PR #43''s own low-QPS/single-consumer reasoning).\n- Analytics reader (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool, cmd/wes-reports):\n  MaxConns=5 (ReportsMaxConns), statement_timeout=15s. Also direct.\n\nProven with a real Postgres via testcontainers\n(pool_limits_integration_test.go, -tags=integration): statement_timeout\nactually cancels a pg_sleep server-side (SQLSTATE 57014) rather than\nbeing silently unenforced, and MaxConns genuinely blocks a further\nAcquire rather than being advisory.\n\nADR 0025 documents both decisions, referencing order-management\nADR-0026, PgBouncer PR #43, and this repo''s specific per-workload HPA\nfindings (verified consumer-group stability, verified MCP session\nstate).\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt clean,\nmake check, make check-all (coverage 99.8%, gate 90%), make arch-test,\ngo test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (all green), helm lint\n--strict, helm template (both HPA states + mixed), and the chart''s own\nService-selector conformance test (tests/test_service_selectors.py).","tree":{"sha":"d254e048e63b7ef6e71563f11ba4347a3f5c9c55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/d254e048e63b7ef6e71563f11ba4347a3f5c9c55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/43fc4c545cb142eeb56439bcb0021f02a6f506ec","verification":{"payload":"tree d254e048e63b7ef6e71563f11ba4347a3f5c9c55\nparent 8ae4684792dd3311a30be4a75f0efe1b8251a5dd\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790567977 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790567977 -0300\n\nfeat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (ADR 0025) (#110)\n\nPorts order-management''s Phase 3 scalability reference (PR #110, ADR-0026)\nto wes-work-planning.\n\nHPA (autoscaling/v2), one per independently-assessed workload, all\ndefault-disabled via values.yaml so this PR changes nothing on merge:\n\n- api: min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU. Stateless OLTP; its only per-process\n  cache (PATH_CATALOGUE_SOURCE=kafka) already uses a per-process-unique\n  consumer group, and its inbound integration-event consumer uses the\n  fleet''s normal stable shared group. Safe at N>1.\n- analytics-projector: min 1 / max 2 / 70% CPU. Its Kafka consumer group\n  (wes-analytics) is verified stable/shared, and every write is\n  idempotent on event_id, so N replicas share partitions safely. Capped\n  at 2 (not 4) since aggregate-id-keyed ordering and a lightweight\n  upsert workload don''t justify more.\n- analytics-reports: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Stateless read-only reader.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Static asset serving, no state.\n- mcp: deliberately EXCLUDED (no autoscaling.mcp block). Verified from\n  the actual code (internal/adapters/inbound/mcp/server.go) that it\n  wraps the same modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk StreamableHTTPHandler with\n  in-memory per-process Mcp-Session-Id state as order-management''s MCP,\n  behind a plain ClusterIP Service with no sessionAffinity — the exact\n  same real risk, excluded the same way.\n\nEvery Deployment template guards its `replicas:` field with\n`{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so a static replica\ncount never fights the HPA controller. Verified with `helm template`\nboth flags off (0 HPAs, every Deployment keeps replicas:1) and all four\nflags on (exactly 4 HPAs render, those 4 Deployments lose `replicas:`,\nmcp''s Deployment keeps it) and mixed enablement.\n\npgxpool MaxConns + statement_timeout, matching order-management''s exact\nnumbers and AfterConnect-hook pattern:\n\n- OLTP pool (postgres.Connect, cmd/wes + cmd/mcp): MaxConns=10,\n  statement_timeout=5s. Already fronted by PgBouncer (warehouse-infra\n  PR #43, transaction pooling, pool_size=12) via the existing\n  DATABASE_URL Secret — no code change needed for that part. PgBouncer,\n  not this client-side setting, bounds the real server-side connection\n  count, so MaxConns stays generous rather than squeezed defensively.\n- Analytics writer (analyticsstore.NewPool, cmd/wes-projector):\n  MaxConns=5, statement_timeout=10s. Direct to Postgres (no PgBouncer,\n  per PR #43''s own low-QPS/single-consumer reasoning).\n- Analytics reader (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool, cmd/wes-reports):\n  MaxConns=5 (ReportsMaxConns), statement_timeout=15s. Also direct.\n\nProven with a real Postgres via testcontainers\n(pool_limits_integration_test.go, -tags=integration): statement_timeout\nactually cancels a pg_sleep server-side (SQLSTATE 57014) rather than\nbeing silently unenforced, and MaxConns genuinely blocks a further\nAcquire rather than being advisory.\n\nADR 0025 documents both decisions, referencing order-management\nADR-0026, PgBouncer PR #43, and this repo''s specific per-workload HPA\nfindings (verified consumer-group stability, verified MCP session\nstate).\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt clean,\nmake check, make check-all (coverage 99.8%, gate 90%), make arch-test,\ngo test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (all green), helm lint\n--strict, helm template (both HPA states + mixed), and the chart''s own\nService-selector conformance test (tests/test_service_selectors.py).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueYpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFXcQAKzlL8+lOR00xxR9da5rsaUe\na4p48r1CGsRD1ldEP7Wy2NSINdz+PhbFCa0i7lbIrgX/2zjlIHqNnCAGnB4OHXeS\nFemGaq1m0Xz+1np9K8dKArQj5zVQlJnnbroWW8uc9KaDqrul/QYsGScZpvckFX/i\nGHlQQjyYx6Cj/8+VVv3m5f6fUaHdYK1ndGK3784HM6gjaIpioMzmrb4tIFVaDem5\nrwm+aiyTqTqV+8eG9zJAC7DG0TWTDLdWDlvN/wYWoCYHSzWaR7EDnzKYsYQlQRoL\nGH4TLvcBitTcO8aaLncIkdD/234N68jgWiWYcYA15dEgBYHvQmMVkWe9Rx/QqZtA\nfQW+yMfhcTER0W/E8+8OaMUe3lrIOaXByBFhzDnCQScKcxATMYpL9Rg70ubpFeOB\n+iOBsn/uUkTCgoTi2P1GsTvH2Ty/c07rlf6wNTmON9nv+aA7pldohCUsClDI8SOG\njWG5T9LwbWxEx72gxbvAh5p+ZK8/HtMKYpVnqQjVBMA/Ssoidu+YLdM0AaviYodf\npnqiIu+kkIwNE3q1JJeuKEk9zHR2TvIutTR1VbS1ijvudoC7OHFE3ddafyv3ly1u\nuN9j4n0OPqk4SESbHNH+XW9d2OMkf0Ktya5rx2zBnJu3rgKu6b3yZAd04iLXzhwa\nJwsTbx5s+KmSgdA2hWHL\n=F8iB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:59:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/43fc4c545cb142eeb56439bcb0021f02a6f506ec","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBRNoAKDQzZmM0YzU0NWNiMTQyZWViNTY0MzliY2IwMDIxZjAyYTZmNTA2ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/8ae4684792dd3311a30be4a75f0efe1b8251a5dd","sha":"8ae4684792dd3311a30be4a75f0efe1b8251a5dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/8ae4684792dd3311a30be4a75f0efe1b8251a5dd"}],"sha":"43fc4c545cb142eeb56439bcb0021f02a6f506ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/43fc4c545cb142eeb56439bcb0021f02a6f506ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/8ae4684792dd3311a30be4a75f0efe1b8251a5dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:34:47Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:34:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(kafka): switch every outbound writer''s Balancer from LeastBytes to Hash (ADR 0024) (#109)\n\nEvery kafka-go Writer this package constructs (Publisher.NewPublisher,\nAnalyticsPublisher.NewAnalyticsPublisher, RelaySink.NewRelaySink) used\n&kafkago.LeastBytes{}, which balances purely by cumulative byte volume\nand completely ignores Message.Key for partition routing. Every\nmessage these adapters build already carries a correct, non-nil\nMessage.Key (Publisher keys by event id; AnalyticsPublisher keys by the\nraising aggregate''s own PathId/WorkUnitId, verified via\nmarshalAnalyticsData) — but the key was silently a no-op for partition\nplacement, invisible while every business topic ran at 1 partition and\na real per-aggregate ordering gap since warehouse-infra PR #42 scaled\nevery business topic (including warehouse.work-planning.events and\nwarehouse.wes.analytics) to 8 partitions.\n\nSame bug, same fix already merged in order-management (ADR-0027, PR\n#111), inventory-storage, and workforce-management.\n\nFix:\n- Switch Publisher.NewPublisher''s, AnalyticsPublisher.NewAnalyticsPublisher''s,\n  and RelaySink.NewRelaySink''s writer Balancer from &kafkago.LeastBytes{}\n  to &kafkago.Hash{} (FNV-1a over Message.Key — the balancer kafka-go\n  actually keys partition placement off).\n- No change to what key is set or by whom; only the writer''s routing\n  behavior changes.\n\nTests:\n- New real-Kafka Testcontainers integration test\n  (balancer_partition_affinity_integration_test.go,\n  TestAnalyticsPublisherKeysMessagesForSameAggregateOntoTheSamePartition)\n  against an 8-partition topic: 3 events for one work unit + 1 for a\n  different work unit are published, every partition is read back, and\n  all 3 same-aggregate messages are asserted onto one partition.\n  Manually confirmed this test FAILS (1 of 3 on the right partition)\n  when the writer''s Balancer is reverted to LeastBytes, and PASSES (3\n  of 3) with Hash — proving a fake-writer unit test alone would not\n  catch this class of bug (a fake Writer.WriteMessages never computes a\n  partition at all).\n- Existing fake-writer unit tests, go vet, gofmt, and the architecture\n  fitness suite (including TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers)\n  all still pass.\n\nAdds ADR 0024 documenting the fix, mirroring order-management''s ADR-0027.\n\nVerified: go build/vet ./..., gofmt -l ., go test ./internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/...\n-race -count=1, go test ./internal/architecture/... -v, go test\n-tags=integration -run TestAnalyticsPublisherKeysMessagesForSameAggregateOntoTheSamePartition\n./internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/... -v -race -count=1 (against a real\nTestcontainers-managed 8-partition broker, both PASS with Hash and FAIL\nwith LeastBytes confirmed).","tree":{"sha":"755ede4bd162f350cee9e24faa583ca5e9ea960b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/755ede4bd162f350cee9e24faa583ca5e9ea960b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/8ae4684792dd3311a30be4a75f0efe1b8251a5dd","verification":{"payload":"tree 755ede4bd162f350cee9e24faa583ca5e9ea960b\nparent 04e11aad7bb013b473e87609749740ac7189dca1\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790566487 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790566487 -0300\n\nfix(kafka): switch every outbound writer''s Balancer from LeastBytes to Hash (ADR 0024) (#109)\n\nEvery kafka-go Writer this package constructs (Publisher.NewPublisher,\nAnalyticsPublisher.NewAnalyticsPublisher, RelaySink.NewRelaySink) used\n&kafkago.LeastBytes{}, which balances purely by cumulative byte volume\nand completely ignores Message.Key for partition routing. Every\nmessage these adapters build already carries a correct, non-nil\nMessage.Key (Publisher keys by event id; AnalyticsPublisher keys by the\nraising aggregate''s own PathId/WorkUnitId, verified via\nmarshalAnalyticsData) — but the key was silently a no-op for partition\nplacement, invisible while every business topic ran at 1 partition and\na real per-aggregate ordering gap since warehouse-infra PR #42 scaled\nevery business topic (including warehouse.work-planning.events and\nwarehouse.wes.analytics) to 8 partitions.\n\nSame bug, same fix already merged in order-management (ADR-0027, PR\n#111), inventory-storage, and workforce-management.\n\nFix:\n- Switch Publisher.NewPublisher''s, AnalyticsPublisher.NewAnalyticsPublisher''s,\n  and RelaySink.NewRelaySink''s writer Balancer from &kafkago.LeastBytes{}\n  to &kafkago.Hash{} (FNV-1a over Message.Key — the balancer kafka-go\n  actually keys partition placement off).\n- No change to what key is set or by whom; only the writer''s routing\n  behavior changes.\n\nTests:\n- New real-Kafka Testcontainers integration test\n  (balancer_partition_affinity_integration_test.go,\n  TestAnalyticsPublisherKeysMessagesForSameAggregateOntoTheSamePartition)\n  against an 8-partition topic: 3 events for one work unit + 1 for a\n  different work unit are published, every partition is read back, and\n  all 3 same-aggregate messages are asserted onto one partition.\n  Manually confirmed this test FAILS (1 of 3 on the right partition)\n  when the writer''s Balancer is reverted to LeastBytes, and PASSES (3\n  of 3) with Hash — proving a fake-writer unit test alone would not\n  catch this class of bug (a fake Writer.WriteMessages never computes a\n  partition at all).\n- Existing fake-writer unit tests, go vet, gofmt, and the architecture\n  fitness suite (including TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers)\n  all still pass.\n\nAdds ADR 0024 documenting the fix, mirroring order-management''s ADR-0027.\n\nVerified: go build/vet ./..., gofmt -l ., go test ./internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/...\n-race -count=1, go test ./internal/architecture/... -v, go test\n-tags=integration -run TestAnalyticsPublisherKeysMessagesForSameAggregateOntoTheSamePartition\n./internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/... -v -race -count=1 (against a real\nTestcontainers-managed 8-partition broker, both PASS with Hash and FAIL\nwith LeastBytes confirmed).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueBXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnCAQAE0eEYUVbjgRjZEcdtzJH8yw\nFcz8Z140A20kpGKJSJrLkV1TdIdHyBnHHRkgLh30MWfq/Mmjrexpup4F2wxVeM8v\nOOsBOfONm/UcaPmSies4YGtFNxfYVA1z4KPedH2aX3NPB5Q6Bjo+L3sNgsEK7kVx\nGoazfeqPW31Ol84mMuFEsaX6rH9cn0pW3cWge6tD4bwFqi6SuejM8qqMw93iK6UY\n/2g1jJjCcn0hWZAgambbzNk9DfI76KIr6yoBeROaU3TFHA89SXhN16OBjWSKke/x\ngqpFaVpPIqn73ub6NwR5KXgp/8CILoWLf79bPlRoEuPHlvvISvzfpx7sM+HdNy2S\n6c1CkQxWbnPutIsYcPKQkuTXMHrQDVToaU3+IqbHmlqeKQ2HLIuqMWR4s2HKeTFJ\nflxuYUqF5whUNegRuKuWW1Vd/HpaAe4ai8PsF1njSwEPW3FUPsECJU6OP3zXqENd\nlix8iji5GL6E6/J55pj+8FhATyKTq6BzpkKPcFGlrdkUYh0hacN3nZvWI18dMX7N\nZMU3n/1O3CB0vGbYjkcK7J+rZWI1bZoaOqILId1fXOZGY2tcSpTrCUw31DequOa+\njpiIEZlU8XlUVAVAdduxetuw1bcnGp0SUo9OP0KeEEhKQXs8OgMGhGJPS/Jfh1r0\nEuHL4lRFkkXcuDVP1Z35\n=ZA2w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:34:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_ur