ceived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/af8044390200ffe860d1a1186ee0e646dd3579c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T21:51:29Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T21:51:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(resilience): per-dependency circuit breakers, read-only retry, Kafka DLQ, graceful shutdown (ADR 0023) (#106)\n\nPorts order-management''s resilience reference (PR #107, ADR-0025) to\nwes-work-planning''s two sync cross-context HTTP clients and its inbound\nKafka consumer:\n\n- internal/resilience: shared circuit-breaker tuning (ReadyToTrip,\n  DefaultMaxRequests/Interval/Timeout) and CallTimeout for\n  context-deadline propagation, ported verbatim (module path only).\n- productclassification.BreakerClient / traveldistance.BreakerClient:\n  one sony/gobreaker/v2 breaker per dependency (never global), each\n  wrapping a newly-split fetch (raw, un-swallowed) + the existing\n  fail-open public method. cenkalti/backoff/v4 jittered retry (max 3\n  attempts) on both -- both are pure GET/reads, unlike order-management\n  where only the read got retry. OPEN-state falls back to each client''s\n  existing PermissiveLookup fail-open contract (ADR-0009, ADR-0017) --\n  no new fallback semantics invented.\n- telemetry.CircuitBreakerMetrics: circuit_breaker.state OTel gauge on\n  the existing global MeterProvider, re-exported as\n  circuit_breaker_state{dependency=...}.\n- Kafka Consumer: per-topic DLQ writers (<topic>.dlq, one per each of\n  the 4 consumed topics), in-process jittered retry (max 3 attempts)\n  before dead-lettering, offset committed past the poison message so\n  the partition is never blocked. Replaces the previous silent-drop-\n  after-one-attempt behaviour.\n- Graceful shutdown: new inboundhttp.Readiness gate backing GET\n  /readyz, flipped to not-ready as the FIRST step of shutdown in\n  cmd/wes/main.go, before the HTTP server/consumer/relay stop.\n  /healthz stays a pure, never-flipped liveness signal.\n  readinessProbe now points at /readyz; terminationGracePeriodSeconds:\n  30 added to the chart (previously unset).\n- ADR-0023 (next available number) documents the full design,\n  explicitly citing order-management''s ADR-0025/PR#107 as the\n  reference this ports.\n\nTesting: unit tests for both breakers (retry-exhaustion, half-open\nrecovery, 404/422-does-not-retry, trip-then-fallback) with a fake\nHTTPDoer; a testcontainers-backed Kafka DLQ integration test\n(consumer_dlq_integration_test.go, -tags=integration, real broker, no\nskip/hardcoded localhost). go build/vet, gofmt, golangci-lint (0\nissues), and the architecture fitness tests all pass. Aggregate\ndomain+application coverage: 99.8% (gate: 90%).\n\nKnown local-environment limitation: the testcontainers Kafka DLQ\nintegration test (and this repo''s pre-existing\nTestConsumer_ProjectsRealBrokerMessages) both time out against this\nsandbox''s Docker/ryuk reaper setup -- confirmed pre-existing, not\nintroduced by this change. Both build and vet clean under\n-tags=integration; CI has a working Docker daemon for these.","tree":{"sha":"2a0c914aecd18ca4f99468198b1c85c246a4c5c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/2a0c914aecd18ca4f99468198b1c85c246a4c5c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/af8044390200ffe860d1a1186ee0e646dd3579c5","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a0c914aecd18ca4f99468198b1c85c246a4c5c0\nparent 50d8d0737fbdaf9ca85698e30427ff840b54ccd7\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790545889 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790545889 -0300\n\nfeat(resilience): per-dependency circuit breakers, read-only retry, Kafka DLQ, graceful shutdown (ADR 0023) (#106)\n\nPorts order-management''s resilience reference (PR #107, ADR-0025) to\nwes-work-planning''s two sync cross-context HTTP clients and its inbound\nKafka consumer:\n\n- internal/resilience: shared circuit-breaker tuning (ReadyToTrip,\n  DefaultMaxRequests/Interval/Timeout) and CallTimeout for\n  context-deadline propagation, ported verbatim (module path only).\n- productclassification.BreakerClient / traveldistance.BreakerClient:\n  one sony/gobreaker/v2 breaker per dependency (never global), each\n  wrapping a newly-split fetch (raw, un-swallowed) + the existing\n  fail-open public method. cenkalti/backoff/v4 jittered retry (max 3\n  attempts) on both -- both are pure GET/reads, unlike order-management\n  where only the read got retry. OPEN-state falls back to each client''s\n  existing PermissiveLookup fail-open contract (ADR-0009, ADR-0017) --\n  no new fallback semantics invented.\n- telemetry.CircuitBreakerMetrics: circuit_breaker.state OTel gauge on\n  the existing global MeterProvider, re-exported as\n  circuit_breaker_state{dependency=...}.\n- Kafka Consumer: per-topic DLQ writers (<topic>.dlq, one per each of\n  the 4 consumed topics), in-process jittered retry (max 3 attempts)\n  before dead-lettering, offset committed past the poison message so\n  the partition is never blocked. Replaces the previous silent-drop-\n  after-one-attempt behaviour.\n- Graceful shutdown: new inboundhttp.Readiness gate backing GET\n  /readyz, flipped to not-ready as the FIRST step of shutdown in\n  cmd/wes/main.go, before the HTTP server/consumer/relay stop.\n  /healthz stays a pure, never-flipped liveness signal.\n  readinessProbe now points at /readyz; terminationGracePeriodSeconds:\n  30 added to the chart (previously unset).\n- ADR-0023 (next available number) documents the full design,\n  explicitly citing order-management''s ADR-0025/PR#107 as the\n  reference this ports.\n\nTesting: unit tests for both breakers (retry-exhaustion, half-open\nrecovery, 404/422-does-not-retry, trip-then-fallback) with a fake\nHTTPDoer; a testcontainers-backed Kafka DLQ integration test\n(consumer_dlq_integration_test.go, -tags=integration, real broker, no\nskip/hardcoded localhost). go build/vet, gofmt, golangci-lint (0\nissues), and the architecture fitness tests all pass. Aggregate\ndomain+application coverage: 99.8% (gate: 90%).\n\nKnown local-environment limitation: the testcontainers Kafka DLQ\nintegration test (and this repo''s pre-existing\nTestConsumer_ProjectsRealBrokerMessages) both time out against this\nsandbox''s Docker/ryuk reaper setup -- confirmed pre-existing, not\nintroduced by this change. Both build and vet clean under\n-tags=integration; CI has a working Docker daemon for these.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquY/hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXhEQAJyuVjgp4bc0A5gLwZovBLZx\n7eGs4dV+AU1Si8dlZmeV9yyhgvV27mzFXSOj1YoOAzUBk07K7aFnquilDRxy62pc\ngXoiBolM13yUeFeuIV+Rq6Lewde7vI+H6HB0T03UMDcrdPBwZMbxWk4rEh/gwIGv\nZrTprjFzlnF6s7hGhesrRLlmCOF7k3ETzrhyCfz2rMINxTeBKAhdl5JCgTc2s6Mh\nNMykH/FDq0edyqWXPHyjYdBJz8tDi6noYPJxGViDanxUwpQSVj3HDWWcc+0SzKxw\n6YN49yQYEOUrxMvH35WKxyrjKggX0KjsrTNsyzyy3rY8Fqy2rOr7og64VFGWmUrx\nHdVtJUdu7fEcyUGBDCDXomckqhCl2rOT8qopTh5Uka4XDXrfatRHSWauShY9/pQS\nKUvHtSun0SlYU1joWIYfs8SnpMxL0/PmLDlhgklwyxNPmX0ela5g89cfsPlbq99Y\n4EIPx9kLsLIg0w5wNWmeoup31X0ovkx/j20G2n+GC2Tm+2i4jv0m6ZVnlnfDY0oB\nQBMOoRe5dJBZug0d5aowfzPDiE+c8lK7QBUYLbjxSmXSrzbyb9+MmSaWjuerVl9x\nMUlw9H5eqUdRdULb4mR6Bj46C32ZhUs5dVYfMZGbW8byJTaOkPhIBb8NWZL6aHqm\nhISo09hej++DNiWG4Est\n=Ke9s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T21:51:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/af8044390200ffe860d1a1186ee0e646dd3579c5","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBRNoAKGFmODA0NDM5MDIwMGZmZTg2MGQxYTExODZlZTBlNjQ2ZGQzNTc5YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/50d8d0737fbdaf9ca85698e30427ff840b54ccd7","sha":"50d8d0737fbdaf9ca85698e30427ff840b54ccd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/50d8d0737fbdaf9ca85698e30427ff840b54ccd7"}],"sha":"af8044390200ffe860d1a1186ee0e646dd3579c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/af8044390200ffe860d1a1186ee0e646dd3579c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/50d8d0737fbdaf9ca85698e30427ff840b54ccd7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:47:59Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:47:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(kafka): EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE for the integration publisher (ADR-0021 Phase 4) (#105)\n\nSplit the outbound integration-topic Publisher''s Encode step to build\neither the legacy flat envelope, the new CloudEvents 1.0 envelope, or\nboth, gated by EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE (flat|cloudevents|dual), default\nflat. Mirrors this repo''s own transactional-outbox Encode/Publish\nseparation.\n\n- flat (default, unset env var): byte-identical to today''s wire\n  format -- golden-file regression tests for WorkReleased and\n  PathCapacityChanged prove it.\n- cloudevents: one CloudEvents 1.0-shaped message per event, schema\n  per apis/asyncapi.yaml (specversion, id==event_id, type via the new\n  pure cloudEventsType(entity, eventName) helper, source, subject,\n  time==occurred_at, datacontenttype, data unchanged).\n- dual: both shapes, two physical Kafka messages per domain event,\n  same topic, same key.\n\nLogs \"event envelope mode\" mode=... once at publisher construction,\nmatching this repo''s PATH_CATALOGUE_SOURCE logging convention.\n\nExisting Encode/Publish tests are unmodified and still pass.\n\nAnalytics publisher/topic (warehouse.wes.analytics) is untouched --\nout of scope per ADR-0021.\n\nThis PR makes ZERO production behavior change on its own:\nEVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE is not set anywhere in warehouse-infra, so every\npublisher keeps running in its current implicit-flat behavior until a\nlater, separate infra phase (ADR-0021 Phase 5) sets the var.\n\nRefs ADR-0021 (CloudEvents 1.0 envelope migration), Phase 4.","tree":{"sha":"03ab7dd6223fd1cf2ed7193f35d93858073d8c2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/03ab7dd6223fd1cf2ed7193f35d93858073d8c2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/50d8d0737fbdaf9ca85698e30427ff840b54ccd7","verification":{"payload":"tree 03ab7dd6223fd1cf2ed7193f35d93858073d8c2a\nparent 6cdb07f2a8136bdc2bc0bf7ce6a68f29e777d4e2\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790520479 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790520479 -0300\n\nfeat(kafka): EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE for the integration publisher (ADR-0021 Phase 4) (#105)\n\nSplit the outbound integration-topic Publisher''s Encode step to build\neither the legacy flat envelope, the new CloudEvents 1.0 envelope, or\nboth, gated by EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE (flat|cloudevents|dual), default\nflat. Mirrors this repo''s own transactional-outbox Encode/Publish\nseparation.\n\n- flat (default, unset env var): byte-identical to today''s wire\n  format -- golden-file regression tests for WorkReleased and\n  PathCapacityChanged prove it.\n- cloudevents: one CloudEvents 1.0-shaped message per event, schema\n  per apis/asyncapi.yaml (specversion, id==event_id, type via the new\n  pure cloudEventsType(entity, eventName) helper, source, subject,\n  time==occurred_at, datacontenttype, data unchanged).\n- dual: both shapes, two physical Kafka messages per domain event,\n  same topic, same key.\n\nLogs \"event envelope mode\" mode=... once at publisher construction,\nmatching this repo''s PATH_CATALOGUE_SOURCE logging convention.\n\nExisting Encode/Publish tests are unmodified and still pass.\n\nAnalytics publisher/topic (warehouse.wes.analytics) is untouched --\nout of scope per ADR-0021.\n\nThis PR makes ZERO production behavior change on its own:\nEVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE is not set anywhere in warehouse-infra, so every\npublisher keeps running in its current implicit-flat behavior until a\nlater, separate infra phase (ADR-0021 Phase 5) sets the var.\n\nRefs ADR-0021 (CloudEvents 1.0 envelope migration), Phase 4.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquSyfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbDMQAKuTItACARYOl3WLKTnR1kVC\nh4BEVf4fNMGnND2mUT72vy6VdN0+FbnWChHZ6EpY0bcAL6U/XbDZ+NK4U0KjX5PR\n165vCkGclViw/nZtMdbjQyQTgP63EsUnyvrUOfszqNItHyKQl2o9mZNhbpZfwfLy\nZZQ13XmOePcT0kqXe2OC0xE4Anm4+7riwlHd46ET6mA4SOWE7D3//wDouNvpuzaG\nR99Net8tQ8BUX3C0v72Hljq2hy/c6Mxs+El9JizytyiBVGG6VNjVlKtivGAIGHsJ\nMucww1VREn7xosPLGs/rTiSpHBDNTyFL7dxvrC29WzpYeydllK7i7iHa4rGhnRke\nSbEYxsbJPl8K39roz4QPKcsLcYKzxrxIyWKfTUJcAsBZKOO0Ec96wdLFN31MUhvo\nKoXiKuSzYxyUj1dZZxtV5o1bMNlnNYUYCzcEFbDYZQ5FKMFVCvzqyU+86cs/vL7Z\nPPdHu4iznsBUFnCW+XgUC2s/UQnP+7fy/Zfzvou2YapeFu/1f7ZREsfZI14UGYBo\nvfXXlaiSKAAuQ/V025hWVkkc+2K6DzFyPC8uxJrIspJDvbSC/M9JXtYJyJa8zpTL\npVOovRvG1lT2vQuyXhH6AX6h0biVqRyJeac4oEbuHL6OBE5+OV2PJXeynelE89Rp\nkzwbsZUHg7Ik3L/e45ER\n=IM/v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T14:48:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/50d8d0737fbdaf9ca85698e30427ff840b54ccd7","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBRNoAKDUwZDhkMDczN2ZiZGFmOWNhODU2OThlMzA0MjdmZjg0MGI1NGNjZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/6cdb07f2a8136bdc2bc0bf7ce6a68f29e777d4e2","sha":"6cdb07f2a8136bdc2bc0bf7ce6a68f29e777d4e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/6cdb07f2a8136bdc2bc0bf7ce6a68f29e777d4e2"}],"sha":"50d8d0737fbdaf9ca85698e30427ff840b54ccd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/50d8d0737fbdaf9ca85698e30427ff840b54ccd7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/6cdb07f2a8136bdc2bc0bf7ce6a68f29e777d4e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:34:41Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:34:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(http): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware for POST /paths/{pathId}/work-units (ADR 0022) (#104)\n\nPorts order-management''s reference implementation (PR #105, ADR 0023)\nto this service''s one genuine resource-creation POST route.\n\nPOST /paths/{pathId}/work-units now requires a caller-supplied\nIdempotency-Key header and processes it transactionally: idempotency\nbookkeeping, the WorkUnit Save, the WorkPool Save, and the outbox\ninsert commit or roll back together as one atomic unit, by reusing\n(not duplicating) the tx-in-context mechanism postgres.UnitOfWork\nalready relies on since the outbox rollout.\n\nRoute audit (confirmed fresh from router.go, not assumed):\n- POST /paths/{pathId}/charge and POST /paths/{pathId}/plan are both\n  INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (path_id) DO UPDATE upserts keyed by the\n  caller-supplied path_id -- idempotent by construction, ruled out.\n- POST /paths/{pathId}/release acts on whichever existing pending\n  entry the release policy currently ranks highest, not a\n  caller-identified new resource -- ruled out.\n- POST /paths/{pathId}/work-units creates a brand-new work_units row\n  keyed by a caller-supplied (but server-persisted) workUnitId with\n  no natural-key upsert protection -- the true candidate, protected\n  here.\n- EnqueueWorkUnit already calls .WithUnitOfWork(uow) in cmd/wes/main.go\n  from the merged outbox rollout; zero changes needed to its own\n  atomically()/UnitOfWork.Execute call to pick up the middleware''s\n  transaction (verified with a real test, not assumed).\n\nWhat changed:\n- Migration 0006_idempotency_keys: same table shape as order-management''s\n  0008 (key, method, path, request_hash, status_code/response_body/\n  response_headers nullable until completion, created_at, completed_at)\n  plus a created_at index for a future TTL job (deferred, flagged in\n  the ADR).\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency.go: RequireIdempotencyKey,\n  applied route-scoped (r.With(...)) to POST /paths/{pathId}/work-units\n  only in router.go -- never the whole router.\n- internal/pgtx (new package): the tx-in-context key/WithTx/TxFrom pair,\n  extracted out of postgres/unit_of_work.go''s previously-unexported\n  mechanism so both the inbound HTTP middleware and the outbound\n  Postgres adapter can bind/read the exact same transaction without\n  either importing the other''s package -- this repo''s arch-go fitness\n  tests forbid that dependency in both directions. postgres.withTx/\n  txFrom now delegate to it; no behavior change for any existing caller\n  (make arch-test passes unchanged).\n- README endpoint doc + curl examples updated for the new required\n  header; Idempotency section cross-references ADR-0022 vs. the\n  existing Kafka consumer de-duplication section.\n- docs/docs/adr/0022-idempotency-key-middleware.md (next free ADR\n  number in this repo) plus the adr/index.md table row and\n  docs/sidebars.ts entry.\n\nTests: all real, testcontainers-only Postgres, no t.Skip, no hardcoded\nlocalhost. internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency_integration_test.go\ndrives the real chi router with real net/http requests: fresh key\ncreates the work unit; replay with same key+body returns the identical\nresponse with exactly one work_units row created; same key+different\nbody -> 422; missing header -> 400; five real concurrent goroutines\nwith the same key+body -> exactly one work_units row (the real\nDB-lock-serialization proof, not a sequential simulation); a genuine\ndomain validation error (empty reference) is cached as its real 400\nand replayed verbatim on retry rather than re-validated.\n\nVerification (real output, this branch):\n  go build ./...                                    clean\n  go vet ./...                                       clean\n  go build -tags=integration ./...                   clean\n  go vet -tags=integration ./...                     clean\n  gofmt -l .                                         empty\n  make check                                         fmt/vet/build/lint(0 issues)/test -race: all PASS\n  make arch-test                                     TestHexagonalDependencyRule + siblings: all PASS\n  go test -tags=integration ./internal/adapters/inbound/http/... -race -count=1\n                                                      all PASS, 6 new idempotency scenarios included\n  go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1      whole module: all PASS, no flakes\n  make coverage (before, on develop)                  99.8% (gate: 90%)\n  make coverage (after, this branch)                  99.8% (gate: 90%) -- unchanged","tree":{"sha":"07a389476ead50cd1b9bc6d94072388fa7a2c215","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/07a389476ead50cd1b9bc6d94072388fa7a2c215"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/6cdb07f2a8136bdc2bc0bf7ce6a68f29e777d4e2","verification":{"payload":"tree 07a389476ead50cd1b9bc6d94072388fa7a2c215\nparent 5e07f0e94fa50e89640121ab740a0a67a20fcedf\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790516081 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790516081 -0300\n\nfeat(http): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware for POST /paths/{pathId}/work-units (ADR 0022) (#104)\n\nPorts order-management''s reference implementation (PR #105, ADR 0023)\nto this service''s one genuine resource-creation POST route.\n\nPOST /paths/{pathId}/work-units now requires a caller-supplied\nIdempotency-Key header and processes it transactionally: idempotency\nbookkeeping, the WorkUnit Save, the WorkPool Save, and the outbox\ninsert commit or roll back together as one atomic unit, by reusing\n(not duplicating) the tx-in-context mechanism postgres.UnitOfWork\nalready relies on since the outbox rollout.\n\nRoute audit (confirmed fresh from router.go, not assumed):\n- POST /paths/{pathId}/charge and POST /paths/{pathId}/plan are both\n  INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (path_id) DO UPDATE upserts keyed by the\n  caller-supplied path_id -- idempotent by construction, ruled out.\n- POST /paths/{pathId}/release acts on whichever existing pending\n  entry the release policy currently ranks highest, not a\n  caller-identified new resource -- ruled out.\n- POST /paths/{pathId}/work-units creates a brand-new work_units row\n  keyed by a caller-supplied (but server-persisted) workUnitId with\n  no natural-key upsert protection -- the true candidate, protected\n  here.\n- EnqueueWorkUnit already calls .WithUnitOfWork(uow) in cmd/wes/main.go\n  from the merged outbox rollout; zero changes needed to its own\n  atomically()/UnitOfWork.Execute call to pick up the middleware''s\n  transaction (verified with a real test, not assumed).\n\nWhat changed:\n- Migration 0006_idempotency_keys: same table shape as order-management''s\n  0008 (key, method, path, request_hash, status_code/response_body/\n  response_headers nullable until completion, created_at, completed_at)\n  plus a created_at index for a future TTL job (deferred, flagged in\n  the ADR).\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency.go: RequireIdempotencyKey,\n  applied route-scoped (r.With(...)) to POST /paths/{pathId}/work-units\n  only in router.go -- never the whole router.\n- internal/pgtx (new package): the tx-in-context key/WithTx/TxFrom pair,\n  extracted out of postgres/unit_of_work.go''s previously-unexported\n  mechanism so both the inbound HTTP middleware and the outbound\n  Postgres adapter can bind/read the exact same transaction without\n  either importing the other''s package -- this repo''s arch-go fitness\n  tests forbid that dependency in both directions. postgres.withTx/\n  txFrom now delegate to it; no behavior change for any existing caller\n  (make arch-test passes unchanged).\n- README endpoint doc + curl examples updated for the new required\n  header; Idempotency section cross-references ADR-0022 vs. the\n  existing Kafka consumer de-duplication section.\n- docs/docs/adr/0022-idempotency-key-middleware.md (next free ADR\n  number in this repo) plus the adr/index.md table row and\n  docs/sidebars.ts entry.\n\nTests: all real, testcontainers-only Postgres, no t.Skip, no hardcoded\nlocalhost. internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency_integration_test.go\ndrives the real chi router with real net/http requests: fresh key\ncreates the work unit; replay with same key+body returns the identical\nresponse with exactly one work_units row created; same key+different\nbody -> 422; missing header -> 400; five real concurrent goroutines\nwith the same key+body -> exactly one work_units row (the real\nDB-lock-serialization proof, not a sequential simulation); a genuine\ndomain validation error (empty reference) is cached as its real 400\nand replayed verbatim on retry rather than re-validated.\n\nVerification (real output, this branch):\n  go build ./...                                    clean\n  go vet ./...                                       clean\n  go build -tags=integration ./...                   clean\n  go vet -tags=integration ./...                     clean\n  gofmt -l .                                         empty\n  make check                                         fmt/vet/build/lint(0 issues)/test -race: all PASS\n  make arch-test                                     TestHexagonalDependencyRule + siblings: all PASS\n  go test -tags=integration ./internal/adapters/inbound/http/... -race -count=1\n                                                      all PASS, 6 new idempotency scenarios included\n  go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1      whole module: all PASS, no flakes\n  make coverage (before, on develop)                  99.8% (gate: 90%)\n  make coverage (after, this branch)                  99.8% (gate: 90%) -- unchanged","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquRtxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPGUQAGHSpFZvetENnVXHAjCkAiTj\nHWJkP+O2fimZHnLxP2HHb0HBWsdd28i3Ztg5knb8xyl5zqJeQlcNsshSX4blduG4\nxtJEB3vtHkQR/FBsoQyoa1FMAqxizcJQyMvR0wmLG69jKTNwgx5sva4KlPjRgJZs\ncVDJDAjxZuZXcgXnIgW2b9idF/UE/QZp0y7tCPo+wp9q5TPJJVdDwiyCTRsljmlr\nZ+tKmO0cfn4J+MYtO7mQEbiVKI3+Y3kEJj/5RZO7bo8LLXvaF4zksFhh0zNqAn4v\nJsLw3dXk4lse76G10md0bj+hOajn36CJfIA7FpZCo/TJsJnfRWLL/BVNyPKZsRJD\naQhbankcJ1kwMGGg7LeFCD0zdIY1j2Nj6cyvb8sCBaU0+O46kdtog5je9rF7Fz0p\nRcMHlUh5N1Grpnbke8Do/MqoaIHirV2qzmA4LdELMhYHPD7hY6zPr8rXHNg/9ETv\nX20/YrXknIWHfwuXPP2JDi+XwmIvZ/6CT+eI5ZFPtDQEaOfhzk4NOUzv2vohDdfb\nntxYMMsZz7VeTmT1pI7yoCFYqDJRWEBlK2pAJBwxjZRT6jknxmDYVL3+ILu0/n5q\n86AjKbIXOg59JNbDDNKVmSgmFrBnhtrZBtouf/f5ne2nGGuErbO74+tEklDLlH9F\nKQkOo1CS5CWOMXQhMgVO\n=BzZf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T13:34:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/6cdb07f2a8136bdc2bc0bf7ce6a68f29e777d4e2","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBRNoAKDZjZGIwN2YyYTgxMzZiZGMyYmMwYmY3Y2U2YTY4ZjI5ZTc3N2Q0ZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commit/5e07f0e94fa50e89640121ab740a0a67a20fcedf","sha":"5e07f0e94fa50e89640121ab740a0a67a20fcedf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/5e07f0e94fa50e89640121ab740a0a67a20fcedf"}],"sha":"6cdb07f2a8136bdc2bc0bf7ce6a68f29e777d4e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/6cdb07f2a8136bdc2bc0bf7ce6a68f29e777d4e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/commits/5e07f0e94fa50e89640121ab740a0a67a20fcedf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:13:56Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:13:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(kafka): dual-read CloudEvents envelope for TaskCompleted (ADR-0021 Phase 2, Task 2c) (#103)\n\nUpgrades the fulfillmentReader path in\ninternal/adapters/inbound/kafka/consumer.go to dual-read\nfulfillment-execution''s TaskCompleted event in either the legacy flat\nenvelope shape or the new CloudEvents 1.0 structured envelope shape,\nper ADR-0021 (mirrored as fulfillment-execution''s ADR-0027).\n\n- decodeFulfillmentEnvelope peeks the raw JSON for a `specversion` key\n  to pick the decode path, normalizing either shape to the existing\n  envelope.Envelope representation before handing off unchanged to\n  handleFulfillmentEvent -> RecordCompletion. No business logic is\n  duplicated across the two decode paths.\n- The CloudEvents `type` field\n  (com.warehouse.wes.fulfillment-execution.task.TaskCompleted, taken\n  verbatim from fulfillment-execution''s apis/asyncapi.yaml) is\n  stripped back to the bare \"TaskCompleted\" name the existing\n  switch/case logic already keys on.\n- An unrecognized specversion fails soft (log + commit, no\n  redelivery), mirroring this repo''s existing malformed-message\n  posture.\n- Every other reader on this Consumer (workforce, inventory,\n  order-management) is untouched — only the fulfillmentReader/\n  TaskCompleted path changed.\n- No env var: dual-read is unconditional and purely additive per the\n  ADR''s Phase 2 design.\n\nTests (all real, run locally):\n- Unit: flat-shaped fixture decodes identically to today (regression).\n- Unit: CloudEvents-shaped fixture (real schema/type string) decodes\n  to the same normalized result as its flat equivalent.\n- Unit: unrecognized specversion and malformed JSON both fail soft.\n- Unit: same event_id across a flat + CloudEvents pair invokes\n  RecordCompletion exactly once (processed_events idempotency gate).\n- Integration (testcontainers Kafka, no KAFKA_BROKERS skip-gate):\n  publishes one flat and one CloudEvents-shaped TaskCompleted message\n  with the same event_id/id on a throwaway warehouse.fulfillment.events\n  topic and asserts the use case fires exactly once — the idempotency\n  safety ADR-0021 Section 3 calls load-bearing for the later\n  dual-write phase.\n\nmake check and make check-all pass locally (fmt-check, vet, build,\nlint, test -race, 90% coverage gate at 99.8%, arch-test, bdd).\n\nRefs: ADR-0021 (wes-work-planning), companion ADR-0027\n(fulfillment-execution), Phase 2 Task 2c.","tree":{"sha":"f6f8309397c07efb788089e9b517e4c38f3fc902","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/trees/f6f8309397c07efb788089e9b517e4c38f3fc902"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/wes-work-planning/git/commits/5e07f0e94fa50e89640121ab740a0a67a20fcedf","verification":{"payload":"tree f6f8309397c07efb788089e9b517e4c38f3fc902\nparent df9475430d740d03171577a4b165e2a2bf53fd3f\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790514836 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790514836 -0300\n\nfeat(kafka): dual-read CloudEvents envelope for TaskCompleted (ADR-0021 Phase 2, Task 2c) (#103)\n\nUpgrades the fulfillmentReader path in\ninternal/adapters/inbound/kafka/consumer.go to dual-read\nfulfillment-execution''s TaskCompleted event in either the legacy flat\nenvelope shape or the new CloudEvents 1.0 structured envelope shape,\nper ADR-0021 (mirrored as fulfillment-execution''s ADR-0027).\n\n- decodeFulfillmentEnvelope peeks the raw JSON for a `specversion` key\n  to pick the decode path, normalizing either shape to the existing\n  envelope.Envelope representation before handing off unchanged to\n  handleFulfillmentEvent -> RecordCompletion. No business logic is\n  duplicated across the two decode paths.\n- The CloudEvents `type` field\n  (com.warehouse.wes.fulfillment-execution.task.TaskCompleted, taken\n  verbatim from fulfillment-execution''s apis/asyncapi.yaml) is\n  stripped back to the bare \"TaskCompleted\" name the existing\n  switch/case logic already keys on.\n- An unrecognized specversion fails soft (log + commit, no\n  redelivery), mirroring this repo''s existing malformed-message\n  posture.\n- Every other reader on this Consumer (workforce, inventory,\n  order-management) is untouched — only the fulfillmentReader/\n  TaskCompleted path changed.\n- No env var: dual-read is unconditional and purely additive per the\n  ADR''s Phase 2 design.\n\nTests (all real, run locally):\n- Unit: flat-shaped fixture decodes identically to today (regression).\n- Unit: CloudEvents-shaped fixture (real schema/type string) decodes\n  to the same normalized result as its flat equivalent.\n- Unit: unrecognized specversion and malformed JSON both fail soft.\n- Unit: same event_id across a flat + CloudEvents pair invokes\n  RecordCompletion exactly once (processed_events idempotency gate).\n- Integration (testcontainers Kafka, no KAFKA_BROKERS skip-gate):\n  publishes one flat and one CloudEvents-shaped TaskCompleted message\n  with the same event_id/id on a throwaway warehouse.fulfillment.events\n  topic and asserts the use case fires exactly once — the idempotency\n  safety ADR-0021 Section 3 calls load-bearing for the later\n  dual-write phase.\n\nmake check and make check-all pass locally (fmt-check, vet, build,\nlint, test -race, 90% coverage gate at 99.8%, arch-test, bdd).\n\nRefs: ADR-0021 (wes-work-planning), companion ADR-0027\n(fulfillment-execution), Phase 2 Task 2c.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquRaUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUEMQAB09tX2ZlTMUDGwcbEz7MnHu\nFhKc38CvoDJhR8vDWdnP+uaPLhy8cXHL19C8Quh6Plg9qILZf8Yx4njBxPkZVdTK\nSJv8sSGemZa2JxbVssGlwdxYnNF58x2bCSC3ipEr/JVOvtDtQ1mb0lfdDF1jW/26\nYuXa7XbgKEF2jyyeS5S54IHFKSy9ARubqYuO366gRheczX/VnbCK21EqVOhKyPzV\nJLZiNcN2BZg9CPCN6avZmSh0x7C14ONk+wEUAKGe56t2nvJim3S70IehpSE7cb6Z\nDVBivCpud1P+nkoVEJ+f/fqvabyXjwJqcfa7V+Ilml1Jx1oMe1U+nfFPjVicZnJm\nJct/ow7QcCJ6O5B74FpYUwmEC39uGy9HNFWw9/nJSiYGM4SOftLSHg8jq1+XBWnH\nCxJkTKqvN5TQqcNTGDH5nOlAjms+DOEgUd5PZ/lN3NdQuhTEslwkm8tM7nfklrcX\nNY2PKh9fVLo1Isk+/WMPackVpSPnz8ZoJ+7DJyM8MZ4I7T6UZNNte1kmg+XPsLX9\nZGC3XhgPJ89y1NKazSmZHhQZel0MFpcUs8ERpgxZddWSKWKMNqOOQHEP53VdskNK\nfAZGA4QhivOLcn3MtCThWufAxrqbHAVfo6pYLzFch5TLDf9fFAi67E1QCVde3sBU\ncwznGY+/1CfKJeCu+3UL\n=e7sq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T13:13:56Z"}},"committer":{"avata