,"following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/df28af08236ba14ad3b5dbfad594f67fab47afb4","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBuNoAKGRmMjhhZjA4MjM2YmExNGFkM2I1ZGJmYWQ1OTRmNjdmYWI0N2FmYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/3b6bfa6136b1453ba1c3a287a81e75f78c04509e","sha":"3b6bfa6136b1453ba1c3a287a81e75f78c04509e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/3b6bfa6136b1453ba1c3a287a81e75f78c04509e"}],"sha":"df28af08236ba14ad3b5dbfad594f67fab47afb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/df28af08236ba14ad3b5dbfad594f67fab47afb4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/3b6bfa6136b1453ba1c3a287a81e75f78c04509e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:48:13Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:48:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: reservations store line_no; confirm picks per line (decision 18) (#158)\n\n* feat(reservation): store line_no; POST /reservations accepts lineNo (decision 18)\n\n- Reservation aggregate gains an optional LineNo (NewForLine / RehydrateForLine;\n  New/Rehydrate unchanged = unknown). 0/negative -> ErrInvalidLineNo.\n- Migration 0035: nullable reservations.line_no INTEGER, CHECK (>= 1). Additive,\n  no backfill (the line was never stored).\n- Postgres repo writes/reads line_no (FindByID, FindByDemandRef); the upsert\n  never rewrites it. The memory repo stores the aggregate, so it carries it.\n- ReserveStock.ExecuteForLine; the replay guard also compares the line when the\n  request names one (two same-SKU/qty lines stay two reservations); an ACTIVE\n  line-less reservation still answers a line-aware retry (no double hold).\n- REST: optional lineNo on POST /reservations (400 invalid-line-no for < 1);\n  lineNo returned on create/GET responses, omitted when unknown.\n\n* feat(confirm-pick): confirm exactly the picked line when TaskCompleted carries line_no (decision 18)\n\n- PickCompletion gains LineNo; the consumer decodes the optional line_no\n  (absent/null = unknown; non-integer = poison -> DLQ; < 1 = malformed -> DLQ).\n- ConfirmPicksForOrder, with a line: confirm the ACTIVE reservation(s) of\n  (demand_ref, line_no) via ConfirmPick; skip CONFIRMED/REVOKED/EXPIRED\n  (expired counted and WARNed). No order_pick_progress write on this path.\n  If the order has no reservation for that line but has line-less (legacy)\n  ones, fall back to the ADR 0035 last-pick counting over those only; if it has\n  none, LINE_NOT_FOUND (a successful no-op). Without a line: unchanged.\n- All inside the same UnitOfWork as the event-id claim; redelivery is a no-op.\n- Tests: unit table (mixed order 1+3 confirmed / 2 stays ACTIVE, revoked\n  attempt + active retry, legacy fallback, mixed legacy/line-aware, expired,\n  redelivery, rollback), consumer decode tests, and a testcontainers\n  Kafka+Postgres end-to-end mixed-order test.\n\n* docs(api): openapi lineNo on POST /reservations + asyncapi line_no on TaskCompleted (ADR 0036)\n\n- openapi: optional nullable lineNo (>= 1) on ReserveStockRequest, lineNo on\n  Reservation, invalid-line-no 400 example, replay/idempotency note.\n- asyncapi: the consumed TaskCompleted gains the optional line_no; the\n  operation now describes the per-line path and the ADR 0035 counting fallback.\n  `asyncapi validate`: 0 errors (only pre-existing warnings).\n- docs API reference regenerated exactly like ci.yml''s docs-api-drift job\n  (clean-api-docs then gen-api-docs).\n\n* docs: ADR 0036 (per-line confirm-pick) and the DDD pack, README and ecosystem pages\n\n- New ADR 0036 (Accepted); ADR 0035''s status line points to it (body untouched);\n  ADR index and sidebar updated.\n- Sequence diagram 13 and message flow 5 now show the per-line path and the\n  ADR 0035 counting fallback; ER diagram gains reservations.line_no (0035);\n  aggregate canvas, use cases, class diagram, domain events, eventstorming\n  (H7/H9), bounded-context canvas, context relationships, context map,\n  integration and README updated; \"one pick early\" is recorded as closed for\n  line-aware events.\n- Mermaid validated (31/31), docs build passes.\n\n* test(postgres): migrate to head before hydrating legacy reservations in the 0008 backfill test\n\nThe repository now selects reservations.line_no (migration 0035), so the test\nthat stops at version 8 and reads through the repo failed with \"column line_no\ndoes not exist\". Bring the database to head for the repo reads; the test''s own\ndown-migration to 0007 still walks all the way back (passes).","tree":{"sha":"27eddfc5f9c514a2c4131f2d0822bc90167429f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/trees/27eddfc5f9c514a2c4131f2d0822bc90167429f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/commits/3b6bfa6136b1453ba1c3a287a81e75f78c04509e","verification":{"payload":"tree 27eddfc5f9c514a2c4131f2d0822bc90167429f4\nparent 242f47ec70abcee773d58046e591aea86f060573\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791420493 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791420493 -0300\n\nfeat: reservations store line_no; confirm picks per line (decision 18) (#158)\n\n* feat(reservation): store line_no; POST /reservations accepts lineNo (decision 18)\n\n- Reservation aggregate gains an optional LineNo (NewForLine / RehydrateForLine;\n  New/Rehydrate unchanged = unknown). 0/negative -> ErrInvalidLineNo.\n- Migration 0035: nullable reservations.line_no INTEGER, CHECK (>= 1). Additive,\n  no backfill (the line was never stored).\n- Postgres repo writes/reads line_no (FindByID, FindByDemandRef); the upsert\n  never rewrites it. The memory repo stores the aggregate, so it carries it.\n- ReserveStock.ExecuteForLine; the replay guard also compares the line when the\n  request names one (two same-SKU/qty lines stay two reservations); an ACTIVE\n  line-less reservation still answers a line-aware retry (no double hold).\n- REST: optional lineNo on POST /reservations (400 invalid-line-no for < 1);\n  lineNo returned on create/GET responses, omitted when unknown.\n\n* feat(confirm-pick): confirm exactly the picked line when TaskCompleted carries line_no (decision 18)\n\n- PickCompletion gains LineNo; the consumer decodes the optional line_no\n  (absent/null = unknown; non-integer = poison -> DLQ; < 1 = malformed -> DLQ).\n- ConfirmPicksForOrder, with a line: confirm the ACTIVE reservation(s) of\n  (demand_ref, line_no) via ConfirmPick; skip CONFIRMED/REVOKED/EXPIRED\n  (expired counted and WARNed). No order_pick_progress write on this path.\n  If the order has no reservation for that line but has line-less (legacy)\n  ones, fall back to the ADR 0035 last-pick counting over those only; if it has\n  none, LINE_NOT_FOUND (a successful no-op). Without a line: unchanged.\n- All inside the same UnitOfWork as the event-id claim; redelivery is a no-op.\n- Tests: unit table (mixed order 1+3 confirmed / 2 stays ACTIVE, revoked\n  attempt + active retry, legacy fallback, mixed legacy/line-aware, expired,\n  redelivery, rollback), consumer decode tests, and a testcontainers\n  Kafka+Postgres end-to-end mixed-order test.\n\n* docs(api): openapi lineNo on POST /reservations + asyncapi line_no on TaskCompleted (ADR 0036)\n\n- openapi: optional nullable lineNo (>= 1) on ReserveStockRequest, lineNo on\n  Reservation, invalid-line-no 400 example, replay/idempotency note.\n- asyncapi: the consumed TaskCompleted gains the optional line_no; the\n  operation now describes the per-line path and the ADR 0035 counting fallback.\n  `asyncapi validate`: 0 errors (only pre-existing warnings).\n- docs API reference regenerated exactly like ci.yml''s docs-api-drift job\n  (clean-api-docs then gen-api-docs).\n\n* docs: ADR 0036 (per-line confirm-pick) and the DDD pack, README and ecosystem pages\n\n- New ADR 0036 (Accepted); ADR 0035''s status line points to it (body untouched);\n  ADR index and sidebar updated.\n- Sequence diagram 13 and message flow 5 now show the per-line path and the\n  ADR 0035 counting fallback; ER diagram gains reservations.line_no (0035);\n  aggregate canvas, use cases, class diagram, domain events, eventstorming\n  (H7/H9), bounded-context canvas, context relationships, context map,\n  integration and README updated; \"one pick early\" is recorded as closed for\n  line-aware events.\n- Mermaid validated (31/31), docs build passes.\n\n* test(postgres): migrate to head before hydrating legacy reservations in the 0008 backfill test\n\nThe repository now selects reservations.line_no (migration 0035), so the test\nthat stops at version 8 and reads through the repo failed with \"column line_no\ndoes not exist\". Bring the database to head for the repo reads; the test''s own\ndown-migration to 0007 still walks all the way back (passes).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxuhNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9s0QADJ+Mn8UfWDnTOC47ODoKh4w\nd3wKNXLGxbCBwpEf6R3oz6/KJHh9A/xhLH7455zXaQzOmYXFrAGupu+OzwfL08hi\nLUXUvNXCLHJed7khrCeKhvLtj7rMaCwsTvB8svnpJ1JrHhPdM9/K5Hc1RQQ+VcYy\nRyGU0XBesKY9otgPzg4gwNHW2C4q/Iwqcc/B8oklk2d225JfXgtVAsaRNO2rBKXL\nFVqInxbMYRU47ZGjBwwStfgbtI+dHpzjriVzY9AGvUwnNWdluV8ZYI1eu/fd7ZJE\nGJPNVYtFpxf2vQmkkINLqzrWQ4dTI6sjuf6JMgnvT8tQAxy/D5M36YZKdOWIur8H\nsR9e7frMs/e51BcHgJ2vdzVlg3+dMHmCMq5qGWnOzoxHMfU0bMXtU5hZrzk6+2uI\n25uEtn+tBSq7j9IJctptCSO2zWrn8r9lhUo8PqIF5x8+Epn1DZE0kqnqfNlkVuE+\n1blJR4kcusettkFnWqLU2cj4m3jEOzITbFnFfhEyiHB9lWCeB76FCCW9rCgnKhJk\nyLDzKDv4rkJ/62LsOYvbjXCa8aaZFCj1y0NWEnU+NlV8/6rs4jr9sCb0TuWygzXx\ntd82t1pUntK/nkM0Ygb6jZVlKRXYYoe07R2LthsIAXZ7I0ur90+oAHoWMIyV4bf/\n/dPwVW6kUiQfVKgVUX4b\n=tUF5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T00:48:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5