lowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/242f47ec70abcee773d58046e591aea86f060573","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBuNoAKDI0MmY0N2VjNzBhYmNlZTc3M2Q1ODA0NmU1OTFhZWE4NmYwNjA1NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/983e44aaeff9f340e07ae2465a476aa622f0c4d0","sha":"983e44aaeff9f340e07ae2465a476aa622f0c4d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/983e44aaeff9f340e07ae2465a476aa622f0c4d0"}],"sha":"242f47ec70abcee773d58046e591aea86f060573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/242f47ec70abcee773d58046e591aea86f060573"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/983e44aaeff9f340e07ae2465a476aa622f0c4d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:26:22Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:26:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: confirm an order''s picked reservations on its LAST pick from TaskCompleted (audit decisions 17, 17a) (#155)\n\n* feat(usecases): ConfirmPicksForOrder confirms an order''s active reservations\n\nConfirms every ACTIVE reservation whose demand_ref equals the completed PICK\ntask''s order_ref, reusing ConfirmPick. The CloudEvents id claim and all\nconfirmations run in one UnitOfWork; expired/revoked/picked reservations are\nskipped and counted (ports.PickConfirmationMetrics), no reservations is a\nsuccessful no-op, a redelivery confirms nothing new.\n\n* feat(kafka): consume TaskCompleted to confirm picked reservations\n\nFixed-group, state-mutating consumer on warehouse.fulfillment.events:\nFetchMessage/commit-after-settle, dispatch on the full TaskCompleted type,\nbounded retry then dead-letter (<topic>.dlq) for transient failures,\nimmediate dead-letter for malformed payloads, sampled WARN for non-CloudEvents.\nWired in the composition root behind TASK_COMPLETED_CONSUMER_MODE (default\noff) / TASK_COMPLETED_CONSUMER_GROUP with a bootretry broker dial, plus the\ninventory.pick_confirmations counter.\n\n* test(integration): TaskCompleted confirms an order''s picks exactly once\n\nTestcontainers Kafka (shared kafkatc helper) + Postgres: a PICK TaskCompleted\nconfirms the order''s ACTIVE reservations, decrements stock and bin capacity\nonce, queues StockPicked once; expired lines are skipped (stock returned), other\norders untouched; a duplicate id and a second PICK for the same order change\nnothing. A forced outbox failure rolls the claim and every confirmation back and\nthe retry converges. A malformed payload is dead-lettered and the stream goes on.\nPer-run ids, verified with -count=2.\n\n* feat(config): chart values, README and AsyncAPI for the TaskCompleted consumer\n\nTASK_COMPLETED_CONSUMER_MODE (default off) and TASK_COMPLETED_CONSUMER_GROUP in\nthe chart and the README env table; apis/asyncapi.yaml documents the consumed\nwarehouse.fulfillment.events channel (TaskCompleted with the additive optional\norder_ref), the DLQ and the short-pick limitation.\n\n* docs(adr): 0035 confirm picks from TaskCompleted; supersede 0032\n\nNew ADR 0035 (Accepted): event-driven, order granularity, why that is the correct\ngranularity (a Task has no SKU or quantity), the expired-reservation rule, the\nconsumer''s retry/DLQ shape, and the explicit limitation that short picks are not\nmodelled. ADR 0032 gets its Status line set to Superseded (body untouched); ADR\nindex and sidebar updated (the sidebar also lacked 0034).\n\n* docs(ddd): confirm-pick resolved - event-driven from TaskCompleted (ADR 0035)\n\nHotspot \"no sibling calls confirm-pick\" becomes \"Decided 2026-10-06:\nevent-driven, order granularity (ADR 0035)\" in the context canvas, context map,\ncontext relationships, event storming (H7, plus H9 for the short-pick\nlimitation), domain events, use cases (new #12), aggregate canvas and\nintegration page; new sequence diagram 13 and domain message flow 5. Mermaid\nvalidated (25/25) and the docs site builds.\n\n* test(integration): do not leave unpublished outbox rows on the shared database\n\nThe confirm-pick integration test queues analytics-topic StockPicked and\nReservationExpired rows. Another test''s relay pass takes the oldest unpublished\nrow and failed with \"Unknown Topic Or Partition\" on warehouse.inventory.analytics\n(TestIntegration_TransferReceipt_StageThenStow_RaisesDestinationUsableOnce failed\nin make integration). Mark each seeded reservation''s rows published at the end of\nthe test, after their existence has been asserted.\n\n* fix(usecases): confirm an order''s reservations on the LAST pick, not the first\n\nA fulfillment-execution PICK task is per order LINE and every one publishes\nthe same order_ref; a Reservation has no line identity. Confirming every\nACTIVE reservation on the first completion marked other lines'' stock picked\nbefore anyone picked it, with no undo (ADR 0035, decision log row 17a).\n\nConfirmPicksForOrder now counts completed PICK tasks per order in the new\norder_pick_progress table (migration 0034), in the SAME unit of work as the\nprocessed-event claim, and confirms the order''s ACTIVE reservations (reusing\nConfirmPick) only when the count reaches ACTIVE + CONFIRMED reservations.\nREVOKED and EXPIRED do not count. Earlier picks record progress and return\nnil. Orders with nothing confirmable leave no progress row. A redelivered\nevent is short-circuited by the claim before it can touch the counter.\n\nThe housekeeping sweeper deletes progress rows not updated for\nORDER_PICK_PROGRESS_RETENTION (default 720h; chart value\nconfig.orderPickProgressRetention, 0 disables).\n\n* docs: confirm-pick on the order''s last pick (ADR 0035, decision 17a)\n\nEdit the unmerged ADR 0035 and its index text to record the corrected\nsemantics: a PICK task is per order line and a Reservation has no line\nidentity, so the consumer counts the order''s picks (order_pick_progress) and\nconfirms only on the last; why late is safe and early is wrong; the retention\nrule; short picks still unmodelled; the future per-line path.\n\nUpdate the docs pack to match: sequence diagram 13, message flow 5,\neventstorming (H7/H9 and the diagram), domain events, use case 12, bounded\ncontext canvas, context relationships, aggregate canvases, the ER diagram (new\norder_pick_progress table, plus processed_events which the page said did not\nexist), ecosystem context map and integration pages, README, AsyncAPI and the\nchart values comment. Mermaid validated; docs build green.","tree":{"sha":"e78d2cee167f8f211135f570134820eac9ff4106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/trees/e78d2cee167f8f211135f570134820eac9ff4106"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/commits/983e44aaeff9f340e07ae2465a476aa622f0c4d0","verification":{"payload":"tree e78d2cee167f8f211135f570134820eac9ff4106\nparent 9759217f62ae585d997cf8c8600b046695054c0f\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791368782 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791368782 -0300\n\nfeat: confirm an order''s picked reservations on its LAST pick from TaskCompleted (audit decisions 17, 17a) (#155)\n\n* feat(usecases): ConfirmPicksForOrder confirms an order''s active reservations\n\nConfirms every ACTIVE reservation whose demand_ref equals the completed PICK\ntask''s order_ref, reusing ConfirmPick. The CloudEvents id claim and all\nconfirmations run in one UnitOfWork; expired/revoked/picked reservations are\nskipped and counted (ports.PickConfirmationMetrics), no reservations is a\nsuccessful no-op, a redelivery confirms nothing new.\n\n* feat(kafka): consume TaskCompleted to confirm picked reservations\n\nFixed-group, state-mutating consumer on warehouse.fulfillment.events:\nFetchMessage/commit-after-settle, dispatch on the full TaskCompleted type,\nbounded retry then dead-letter (<topic>.dlq) for transient failures,\nimmediate dead-letter for malformed payloads, sampled WARN for non-CloudEvents.\nWired in the composition root behind TASK_COMPLETED_CONSUMER_MODE (default\noff) / TASK_COMPLETED_CONSUMER_GROUP with a bootretry broker dial, plus the\ninventory.pick_confirmations counter.\n\n* test(integration): TaskCompleted confirms an order''s picks exactly once\n\nTestcontainers Kafka (shared kafkatc helper) + Postgres: a PICK TaskCompleted\nconfirms the order''s ACTIVE reservations, decrements stock and bin capacity\nonce, queues StockPicked once; expired lines are skipped (stock returned), other\norders untouched; a duplicate id and a second PICK for the same order change\nnothing. A forced outbox failure rolls the claim and every confirmation back and\nthe retry converges. A malformed payload is dead-lettered and the stream goes on.\nPer-run ids, verified with -count=2.\n\n* feat(config): chart values, README and AsyncAPI for the TaskCompleted consumer\n\nTASK_COMPLETED_CONSUMER_MODE (default off) and TASK_COMPLETED_CONSUMER_GROUP in\nthe chart and the README env table; apis/asyncapi.yaml documents the consumed\nwarehouse.fulfillment.events channel (TaskCompleted with the additive optional\norder_ref), the DLQ and the short-pick limitation.\n\n* docs(adr): 0035 confirm picks from TaskCompleted; supersede 0032\n\nNew ADR 0035 (Accepted): event-driven, order granularity, why that is the correct\ngranularity (a Task has no SKU or quantity), the expired-reservation rule, the\nconsumer''s retry/DLQ shape, and the explicit limitation that short picks are not\nmodelled. ADR 0032 gets its Status line set to Superseded (body untouched); ADR\nindex and sidebar updated (the sidebar also lacked 0034).\n\n* docs(ddd): confirm-pick resolved - event-driven from TaskCompleted (ADR 0035)\n\nHotspot \"no sibling calls confirm-pick\" becomes \"Decided 2026-10-06:\nevent-driven, order granularity (ADR 0035)\" in the context canvas, context map,\ncontext relationships, event storming (H7, plus H9 for the short-pick\nlimitation), domain events, use cases (new #12), aggregate canvas and\nintegration page; new sequence diagram 13 and domain message flow 5. Mermaid\nvalidated (25/25) and the docs site builds.\n\n* test(integration): do not leave unpublished outbox rows on the shared database\n\nThe confirm-pick integration test queues analytics-topic StockPicked and\nReservationExpired rows. Another test''s relay pass takes the oldest unpublished\nrow and failed with \"Unknown Topic Or Partition\" on warehouse.inventory.analytics\n(TestIntegration_TransferReceipt_StageThenStow_RaisesDestinationUsableOnce failed\nin make integration). Mark each seeded reservation''s rows published at the end of\nthe test, after their existence has been asserted.\n\n* fix(usecases): confirm an order''s reservations on the LAST pick, not the first\n\nA fulfillment-execution PICK task is per order LINE and every one publishes\nthe same order_ref; a Reservation has no line identity. Confirming every\nACTIVE reservation on the first completion marked other lines'' stock picked\nbefore anyone picked it, with no undo (ADR 0035, decision log row 17a).\n\nConfirmPicksForOrder now counts completed PICK tasks per order in the new\norder_pick_progress table (migration 0034), in the SAME unit of work as the\nprocessed-event claim, and confirms the order''s ACTIVE reservations (reusing\nConfirmPick) only when the count reaches ACTIVE + CONFIRMED reservations.\nREVOKED and EXPIRED do not count. Earlier picks record progress and return\nnil. Orders with nothing confirmable leave no progress row. A redelivered\nevent is short-circuited by the claim before it can touch the counter.\n\nThe housekeeping sweeper deletes progress rows not updated for\nORDER_PICK_PROGRESS_RETENTION (default 720h; chart value\nconfig.orderPickProgressRetention, 0 disables).\n\n* docs: confirm-pick on the order''s last pick (ADR 0035, decision 17a)\n\nEdit the unmerged ADR 0035 and its index text to record the corrected\nsemantics: a PICK task is per order line and a Reservation has no line\nidentity, so the consumer counts the order''s picks (order_pick_progress) and\nconfirms only on the last; why late is safe and early is wrong; the retention\nrule; short picks still unmodelled; the future per-line path.\n\nUpdate the docs pack to match: sequence diagram 13, message flow 5,\neventstorming (H7/H9 and the diagram), domain events, use case 12, bounded\ncontext canvas, context relationships, aggregate canvases, the ER diagram (new\norder_pick_progress table, plus processed_events which the page said did not\nexist), ecosystem context map and integration pages, README, AsyncAPI and the\nchart values comment. Mermaid validated; docs build green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxh5OCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA9oQAD/DGHfxJ4VxY3v2FnUN7CBw\ntJHK/eRR/z7qA5INWLA9nyzjhl587be70dlbC/UQ9uKX9W3bsevJyEr0OT+dEbiZ\n9V8UtX7ReOw44NFlvlvRocBmr59Znd8SCFiRVybkKkzSS/fuFJodFnp9AVyaOtGd\nn1SfWkJsWW6GgkEqNyhCbpRCNMpMacwb4TIOLNTKi1Ufu20ej8TOhLdI7HObFWfG\ndBg4Jj0rrUI2TuCjQ+aAobChNgni0tw65Nsj/j2pR17Kwg40a1P+CBDrxWWyzSdv\nNFBcxzWlnVnXu332OuBbdIbu+v06Io+MY7jCLHZ9ccRqvHMqR72yFenw/NyzpYha\ngKfuIRzwjRjfYpa40ACIaecNGysgRSRwGQgYT0msYxWiLNI39atNGdxtnc4s986N\nnQPZC2VRDSjaqw1zpc4a8NFGRqymsheQVIGmY+hO/0gEwAGznLD71L05j9iJKrOU\n3KwEzCQLXnIDHWgpq/jI5LGhLtT8b+AozIowZU04DGghzSdz5AGlCZPiMfPquQRY\nVNQIePpphcN78E240suMD5fpIFOVN8NvRwl3kGPH7DNntpJL/3foch6JpWF8gDLI\nErQIY5esvQ4aL8RCRdFm1rMMeV1dNHoaA8vBbvRzg4TStMeVCRooFu9pTT3s3v1I\n7eUgEO+phenYxqEwvWmS\n=bE1U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T10:26:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/983e44aaeff9f340e07ae2465a476aa622f0c4d0","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBuNoAKDk4M2U0NGFhZWZmOWYzNDBlMDdhZTI0NjVhNDc2YWE2MjJmMGM0ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/9759217f62ae585d997cf8c8600b046695054c0f","sha":"9759217f62ae585d997cf8c8600b046695054c0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/9759217f62ae585d997cf8c8600b046695054c0f"}],"sha":"983e44aaeff9f340e07ae2465a476aa622f0c4d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/983e44aaeff9f340e07ae2465a476aa622f0c4d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/9759217f62ae585d997cf8c8600b046695054c0f/c