:"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/3970a42bbbc23b20705274b5e20b33a3b4ec59fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:37:31Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:37:31Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"message":"docs(executive): add executive briefing deck\n\nAdds `executive/index.html`: a self-contained reveal.js executive deck covering strategy, architecture, observability, competitive position and next steps for this repo. Open it in a browser (loads reveal.js 6.0.0 from jsDelivr, pinned with an SRI hash; no vendored library code in this repo); no build step. Full source text is in the speaker notes (press S).\n\nNo code, config, workflow or chart changes; the folder is outside `.github/`, `charts/` and the docs site, so `repo_lint` and the docs build are unaffected. Fleet-wide gap analysis lives in `warehouse-docs/executive/competitive-gaps.html`.","tree":{"sha":"9e75835937fc460285bde0781083225d258b9c85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/trees/9e75835937fc460285bde0781083225d258b9c85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/commits/3970a42bbbc23b20705274b5e20b33a3b4ec59fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/3970a42bbbc23b20705274b5e20b33a3b4ec59fe","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBuNoAKDM5NzBhNDJiYmJjMjNiMjA3MDUyNzRiNWUyMGIzM2EzYjRlYzU5ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/197eaf29f8dc521e113578aeaff7bf6686608c42","sha":"197eaf29f8dc521e113578aeaff7bf6686608c42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/197eaf29f8dc521e113578aeaff7bf6686608c42"}],"sha":"3970a42bbbc23b20705274b5e20b33a3b4ec59fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/3970a42bbbc23b20705274b5e20b33a3b4ec59fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/197eaf29f8dc521e113578aeaff7bf6686608c42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:15:13Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:15:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: publish ProductClassified; confirm-pick direction (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#147)\n\n* feat(events): publish ProductClassified through the outbox on both topics\n\nAudit decision 9b (2026-10-06): ProductClassification is SKU master data\nowned here, so classify/re-classify now raises ProductClassified on\nwarehouse.inventory.events and warehouse.inventory.analytics via the\ntransactional outbox (same UnitOfWork as the aggregate save), letting\nsiblings keep a local copy instead of polling GET /products/{sku}/classification.\n\n- type com.warehouse.wms.inventory-storage.product.ProductClassified,\n  subject and Kafka key = SKU (reclassifications stay ordered),\n  dataschema ...:events:ProductClassified:v1 / ...:analytics:ProductClassified:v1\n- data {sku, handling_tags, temperature_class?, dot_hazard_class?} - a\n  full-state replacement, no PII; optional fields omitted when unset\n- the direct EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka path forwards it too\n- LocationRecorded stays in-process (no consumer) - pinned by a test\n- the analytics projector ignores the new type (regression test)\n\nTests: exact-JSON goldens on both topics, direct-publish tests, and a\ntestcontainers Postgres outbox integration test proving the rows commit\nwith the classification (and roll back with it when the second topic''s\nencoder fails). Additive: no existing type or payload changes.\n\n* docs(contract): ADR 0031 and AsyncAPI for the published ProductClassified\n\n- new ADR 0031 (Accepted): publish ProductClassified through the outbox on\n  both topics; supersedes ONLY the \"in-process only\" clause of ADR 0024 for\n  this event; records that LocationRecorded stays in-process (no consumer)\n- apis/asyncapi.yaml: additive ProductClassified message on both channels,\n  ProductClassifiedEvent schema (const type/dataschema, closed enums), two\n  examples, `product` tag; spectral lint clean\n- README, docs/api-reference/events.md and the analytics page now say the\n  event is published and that the projector ignores it\n\n* docs: record the 2026-10-06 decisions (ADR 0032, DDD pack, ecosystem)\n\n- ADR 0032 (Proposed): confirm-pick direction is event-driven (consume a\n  fulfillment-execution pick-completion event, no sync REST/MCP); blocked\n  because TaskCompleted carries no reservation correlation, SKU or picked\n  quantity - the exact missing fields and owning repos are named; lazy\n  reservation expiry stays (ADR 0003)\n- ADR index and sidebar list 0031 and 0032\n- DDD pack: hotspot/gap rows changed from \"Hotspot\" to \"Decided 2026-10-06\"\n  (LOCATION_LOOKUP_MODE kept permissive; ProductClassified published;\n  lazy expiry kept; confirm-pick event-driven), with Mermaid fixed in\n  eventstorming, domain-events, sequence-diagrams (ClassifyProduct,\n  ConfirmPick), domain-message-flow and the ecosystem context map; open\n  questions in the bounded-context canvas resolved\n- Mermaid validated with warehouse-docs/scripts/validate-mermaid.cjs;\n  `npm run build` passes, no REST API-docs drift","tree":{"sha":"8991129c68aaf6f799495af848c122cff563a602","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/trees/8991129c68aaf6f799495af848c122cff563a602"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/commits/197eaf29f8dc521e113578aeaff7bf6686608c42","verification":{"payload":"tree 8991129c68aaf6f799495af848c122cff563a602\nparent 9e47dca6ee7fa9acfff0818a9c3a74006867c3ff\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791328513 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791328513 -0300\n\nfeat: publish ProductClassified; confirm-pick direction (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#147)\n\n* feat(events): publish ProductClassified through the outbox on both topics\n\nAudit decision 9b (2026-10-06): ProductClassification is SKU master data\nowned here, so classify/re-classify now raises ProductClassified on\nwarehouse.inventory.events and warehouse.inventory.analytics via the\ntransactional outbox (same UnitOfWork as the aggregate save), letting\nsiblings keep a local copy instead of polling GET /products/{sku}/classification.\n\n- type com.warehouse.wms.inventory-storage.product.ProductClassified,\n  subject and Kafka key = SKU (reclassifications stay ordered),\n  dataschema ...:events:ProductClassified:v1 / ...:analytics:ProductClassified:v1\n- data {sku, handling_tags, temperature_class?, dot_hazard_class?} - a\n  full-state replacement, no PII; optional fields omitted when unset\n- the direct EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka path forwards it too\n- LocationRecorded stays in-process (no consumer) - pinned by a test\n- the analytics projector ignores the new type (regression test)\n\nTests: exact-JSON goldens on both topics, direct-publish tests, and a\ntestcontainers Postgres outbox integration test proving the rows commit\nwith the classification (and roll back with it when the second topic''s\nencoder fails). Additive: no existing type or payload changes.\n\n* docs(contract): ADR 0031 and AsyncAPI for the published ProductClassified\n\n- new ADR 0031 (Accepted): publish ProductClassified through the outbox on\n  both topics; supersedes ONLY the \"in-process only\" clause of ADR 0024 for\n  this event; records that LocationRecorded stays in-process (no consumer)\n- apis/asyncapi.yaml: additive ProductClassified message on both channels,\n  ProductClassifiedEvent schema (const type/dataschema, closed enums), two\n  examples, `product` tag; spectral lint clean\n- README, docs/api-reference/events.md and the analytics page now say the\n  event is published and that the projector ignores it\n\n* docs: record the 2026-10-06 decisions (ADR 0032, DDD pack, ecosystem)\n\n- ADR 0032 (Proposed): confirm-pick direction is event-driven (consume a\n  fulfillment-execution pick-completion event, no sync REST/MCP); blocked\n  because TaskCompleted carries no reservation correlation, SKU or picked\n  quantity - the exact missing fields and owning repos are named; lazy\n  reservation expiry stays (ADR 0003)\n- ADR index and sidebar list 0031 and 0032\n- DDD pack: hotspot/gap rows changed from \"Hotspot\" to \"Decided 2026-10-06\"\n  (LOCATION_LOOKUP_MODE kept permissive; ProductClassified published;\n  lazy expiry kept; confirm-pick event-driven), with Mermaid fixed in\n  eventstorming, domain-events, sequence-diagrams (ClassifyProduct,\n  ConfirmPick), domain-message-flow and the ecosystem context map; open\n  questions in the bounded-context canvas resolved\n- Mermaid validated with warehouse-docs/scripts/validate-mermaid.cjs;\n  `npm run build` passes, no REST API-docs drift","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxYEBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW7kQABdMRsA1AJxfI5BC2E4esYP7\nL9MxtJTDBHQPjd4v8JnMyOh3qHJ41f9HA+ZG7HYtDr7GvZwDk02AxxYntpKVUREM\nmv6wz38qcoZZ/8mbB5e68vVNwaF5Ej32Csiya+POCvC1z5FviVOfUhCwilaR9bCq\nixcnb0y/t94rPZiW21RmjebPHVAUAe9ovmroLZcSlHDdhZJ+qT9bg4AaCE0x5yVF\nVcb8R7TMOC6cB3bmQ924I0svD4Oe5uQGuyBXj+nSD2SiFIWWdqLTzgQxgPjwPS8K\n33T28HfNPIIFAm0WMFTW9feIcNUexH6YXFXKPq3aTRKWyWD2QcPlEridiDq1BYXP\npG64n9sN3Ra7FBvVIEgoU7Pxpzj+e+OgkzAP5kJtP2hd6TZ78Nue52SbaVPc05gw\nIzRAiaCyOBG8q1r4MjYEICZY7ZR7XpBpIEyeTuLPeRrjJRq7DfrEmHD1GNt6Dks5\nY7dAC0p+3LJhMQyTM3P/9loXRkCLs1rhMsUVl8x3FRb3HIMtM3xTADUzcs+JxAVx\nDpPxziupF1hhFPEQoeWNxAY8TuhmvBkv9wlBuEmLzZnrCz1Ijru/DIPwAk/lvMyi\n5oExVkY8q3yb5nqDtz6jHYm9Y07JHwTmPpTXk7daKCKcje/RO7K3nRfNe8ADulxl\nbexs/Hp9552Ts0Y2FUsu\n=aj1E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T23:15:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/197eaf29f8dc521e113578aeaff7bf6686608c42","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBuNoAKDE5N2VhZjI5ZjhkYzUyMWUxMTM1NzhhZWFmZjdiZjY2ODY2MDhjNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/9e47dca6ee7fa9acfff0818a9c3a74006867c3ff","sha":"9e47dca6ee7fa9acfff0818a9c3a74006867c3ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/9e47dca6ee7fa9acfff0818a9c3a74006867c3ff"}],"sha":"197eaf29f8dc521e113578aeaff7bf6686608c42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/197eaf29f8dc521e113578aeaff7bf6686608c42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/9e47dca6ee7fa9acfff0818a9c3a74006867c3ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:09:46Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:09:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): deflake the transfer-allocation integration test; build docs on PRs (#146)\n\n* test(integration): deflake the transfer-allocation test at its root cause\n\nTestIntegration_TransferAllocation_DuplicateCommand_OneReservationOneDecrement\nfailed on develop and on the release PR with \"timed out waiting for the\ntransfer consumer to settle; Run: (still running)\", then passed on re-run.\n\nRoot cause: it is the first test that joins a Kafka consumer group on a\nfreshly booted broker. A broker that accepts connections is not yet a\ngroup coordinator: the first group request creates __consumer_offsets and\nis answered [15] Group Coordinator Not Available until it exists.\nkafka-go then sleeps its fixed 5 s JoinGroupBackoff before every retry\n(reproduced: first join at 8.4 s vs 0.03 s once the coordinator is warm),\nand on a loaded runner the offsets topic needs several cycles, exhausting\nthe test''s 45 s window. The consumer itself is correct (FetchMessage,\ncommit after the handler, retry-not-skip) - no consumer defect.\n\nFix (synchronisation, timeout and assertions unchanged):\n- wait for the group coordinator (FindCoordinator) once, after the broker\n  boots, instead of racing it inside the first test''s timed window;\n- make the scenarios repeatable (-count=N) and independent: per-run ids\n  and per-line outbox counts instead of global counts on the shared DB;\n- the duplicate test now waits until the group has committed past all\n  three commands, so \"one reservation, one decrement, one reply\" is\n  asserted AFTER the duplicates were consumed, not before.\n\n* ci(docs): build the Docs site on pull requests\n\ndocs.yml only ran on push to main, so the ADR 0030 missing-id break\n(fixed in #144) reached main before anything built the site.\n\nAdd a pull_request trigger (docs/**, apis/**, the workflow) that runs\nthe SAME build job. Publishing stays main-only: the Pages artifact upload\nand the deploy job are skipped for pull_request (fleet pattern, see\nwarehouse-planning / wes-work-planning). Pinned action SHAs unchanged.\npush now also watches apis/** (the generated API reference is built from\nit by the prebuild step). A PR build uses its own concurrency group so it\ncannot cancel or be dropped behind a deploy.","tree":{"sha":"2b7ebfcc69d7a70fb6d6ba368317768e3dc0cb23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/trees/2b7ebfcc69d7a70fb6d6ba368317768e3dc0cb23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/commits/9e47dca6ee7fa9acfff0818a9c3a74006867c3ff","verification":{"payload":"tree 2b7ebfcc69d7a70fb6d6ba368317768e3dc0cb23\nparent b1484eba07f65d076f62fbdbc862cdaeb6431a54\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791328186 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791328186 -0300\n\nfix(ci): deflake the transfer-allocation integration test; build docs on PRs (#146)\n\n* test(integration): deflake the transfer-allocation test at its root cause\n\nTestIntegration_TransferAllocation_DuplicateCommand_OneReservationOneDecrement\nfailed on develop and on the release PR with \"timed out waiting for the\ntransfer consumer to settle; Run: (still running)\", then passed on re-run.\n\nRoot cause: it is the first test that joins a Kafka consumer group on a\nfreshly booted broker. A broker that accepts connections is not yet a\ngroup coordinator: the first group request creates __consumer_offsets and\nis answered [15] Group Coordinator Not Available until it exists.\nkafka-go then sleeps its fixed 5 s JoinGroupBackoff before every retry\n(reproduced: first join at 8.4 s vs 0.03 s once the coordinator is warm),\nand on a loaded runner the offsets topic needs several cycles, exhausting\nthe test''s 45 s window. The consumer itself is correct (FetchMessage,\ncommit after the handler, retry-not-skip) - no consumer defect.\n\nFix (synchronisation, timeout and assertions unchanged):\n- wait for the group coordinator (FindCoordinator) once, after the broker\n  boots, instead of racing it inside the first test''s timed window;\n- make the scenarios repeatable (-count=N) and independent: per-run ids\n  and per-line outbox counts instead of global counts on the shared DB;\n- the duplicate test now waits until the group has committed past all\n  three commands, so \"one reservation, one decrement, one reply\" is\n  asserted AFTER the duplicates were consumed, not before.\n\n* ci(docs): build the Docs site on pull requests\n\ndocs.yml only ran on push to main, so the ADR 0030 missing-id break\n(fixed in #144) reached main before anything built the site.\n\nAdd a pull_request trigger (docs/**, apis/**, the workflow) that runs\nthe SAME build job. Publishing stays main-only: the Pages artifact upload\nand the deploy job are skipped for pull_request (fleet pattern, see\nwarehouse-planning / wes-work-planning). Pinned action SHAs unchanged.\npush now also watches apis/** (the generated API reference is built from\nit by the prebuild step). A PR build uses its own concurrency group so it\ncannot cancel or be dropped behind a deploy.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxX+6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASG4QAEXJadM2oZUSMNX+S9Dtxq0Q\nxW2rLRrK8i6kBFoqZglAMCy4ftZ2TCxjYuEj9m