to 0030.","tree":{"sha":"83c6ac0e354d01faa7043e22ec9b57c2d55d9b18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/trees/83c6ac0e354d01faa7043e22ec9b57c2d55d9b18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/commits/b1484eba07f65d076f62fbdbc862cdaeb6431a54","verification":{"payload":"tree 83c6ac0e354d01faa7043e22ec9b57c2d55d9b18\nparent a7e79c10c1018f20ba0a98738c572c62c2628c2b\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791325074 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791325074 -0300\n\nfix(docs): give ADR 0030 an explicit doc id so the sidebar resolves (#144)\n\nDocusaurus strips the leading number from a file name when deriving a doc id, so ''adr/0030-site-scoped-transfer-allocation'' in sidebars.ts matched nothing and the Docs build on main failed with ''Invalid sidebar file''. Every other ADR sets id explicitly; add it (and sidebar_label/position) to 0030.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxXOSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWZ8QACkOvgb3Q1Dne7ObpVvRedDV\n8NafoGgjV24O8t4kdfaSxSwiHem6NA3IL+5FWAz+yJjnbJ3SCiA8wjUAZQnktllC\nZJb60sQypyTDnN/hVI+9kj9Wr4Se838Xp289aJRnisS2ZgcgyZLGXLpMHLmhUYIG\nKcquwus8X7nPYqLlmZagNkj8x1C9dRYCp+SJ4zFM2/Uco4gfx4Sx66BJyCjXzXy0\nTFz21Em86SBiHptgUjsw70PT606rAIgjac0niA+LketD0ocVNSEZ5/hVPPZOMj2n\nwBMGkoIE0suSphmJ4nyFgIhXouVjiNGgVTJXn8+rhOuZakBcFoi3f9rcWvn/iQtb\nea+qFSq9rfpvgOrkLL8BhFof9f0jWI5RB9hmJ4SouN5+uS6B3tRYqT8eNiRWO6eB\nY75KRsImy2SMzx525ckODZAri3CEy9N+jh4ey3/Iube9VZgdvOH0TggjrIXkuxNv\nYNoa4sdyrWUgArP4Wx7tSjLvrsZUoBgHI6QnDo3LvGqhFYcGaZM8dFP9hy2nNtF4\nlu5La9zG54164os3vCcE7q+tLrmqQntsQo/9W9gLLxcGeq64wq7rgxPnMPhByhCS\niWJmqak3edUKc6qhsdfnpjeVe2hE/2x/wnsRRhQp/SHQMvYBlKvk9t1l8Dbx2d5v\nyFfAt1eqZP9McSloxrec\n=HFuo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T22:17:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/b1484eba07f65d076f62fbdbc862cdaeb6431a54","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBuNoAKGIxNDg0ZWJhMDdmNjVkMDc2ZjYyZmJkYmM4NjJjZGFlYjY0MzFhNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/a7e79c10c1018f20ba0a98738c572c62c2628c2b","sha":"a7e79c10c1018f20ba0a98738c572c62c2628c2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/a7e79c10c1018f20ba0a98738c572c62c2628c2b"}],"sha":"b1484eba07f65d076f62fbdbc862cdaeb6431a54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/b1484eba07f65d076f62fbdbc862cdaeb6431a54"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/a7e79c10c1018f20ba0a98738c572c62c2628c2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:26:32Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:26:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(transfer): site-scoped transfer allocation command consumer (#142)\n\nPhase 2 of the network transfer saga: inventory-storage consumes\nnetwork-inventory-planning''s TransferAllocationRequested commands\n(CloudEvents 1.0 on warehouse.network-inventory-planning.events) and\ndecides them through AllocateTransferStock — stock decrements,\nReservation, transfer_allocations ledger row and the\nTransferStockAllocated/Rejected reply event''s outbox row in ONE\nUnitOfWork transaction, idempotent on transfer_line_id at the database\nlevel.\n\n- domain: SiteID VO, site custody on StockUnit (nullable — legacy\n  site-less rows stay unallocatable), transfer Allocation ledger\n  aggregate with replay/conflict semantics\n- adapters: inbound kafka Consumer (FetchMessage/CommitMessages,\n  deterministic-poison commit-past, capped backoff retry of transient\n  failures), postgres TransferAllocationRepo, memory repo for tests\n- migrations: 0030 site custody columns, 0031 transfer_allocations\n  ledger (incl. decided_at — the repo SQL writes it; its absence was\n  the real cause of the consumer-group integration stalls, masked by\n  a discard logger)\n- composition root: TRANSFER_ALLOCATION_CONSUMER_MODE=kafka opt-in\n- tests: consumer unit tests (race-safe fakes), use-case tests,\n  postgres repo integration test, golden wire test, and the 4-scenario\n  end-to-end proof on real Kafka+Postgres (duplicate command, other\n  site untouched, insufficient stock, outbox-failure rollback — the\n  last now asserting the outbox DELTA on the shared database)\n\nmake check-all green; full -tags=integration suite green.","tree":{"sha":"e0d6bb77c721aed51c7cdef8577cd1fdebc50ee1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/trees/e0d6bb77c721aed51c7cdef8577cd1fdebc50ee1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/commits/a7e79c10c1018f20ba0a98738c572c62c2628c2b","verification":{"payload":"tree e0d6bb77c721aed51c7cdef8577cd1fdebc50ee1\nparent 0e38e4416e179b6f22d53207b95aec7d03ebf772\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791307592 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791307592 -0300\n\nfeat(transfer): site-scoped transfer allocation command consumer (#142)\n\nPhase 2 of the network transfer saga: inventory-storage consumes\nnetwork-inventory-planning''s TransferAllocationRequested commands\n(CloudEvents 1.0 on warehouse.network-inventory-planning.events) and\ndecides them through AllocateTransferStock — stock decrements,\nReservation, transfer_allocations ledger row and the\nTransferStockAllocated/Rejected reply event''s outbox row in ONE\nUnitOfWork transaction, idempotent on transfer_line_id at the database\nlevel.\n\n- domain: SiteID VO, site custody on StockUnit (nullable — legacy\n  site-less rows stay unallocatable), transfer Allocation ledger\n  aggregate with replay/conflict semantics\n- adapters: inbound kafka Consumer (FetchMessage/CommitMessages,\n  deterministic-poison commit-past, capped backoff retry of transient\n  failures), postgres TransferAllocationRepo, memory repo for tests\n- migrations: 0030 site custody columns, 0031 transfer_allocations\n  ledger (incl. decided_at — the repo SQL writes it; its absence was\n  the real cause of the consumer-group integration stalls, masked by\n  a discard logger)\n- composition root: TRANSFER_ALLOCATION_CONSUMER_MODE=kafka opt-in\n- tests: consumer unit tests (race-safe fakes), use-case tests,\n  postgres repo integration test, golden wire test, and the 4-scenario\n  end-to-end proof on real Kafka+Postgres (duplicate command, other\n  site untouched, insufficient stock, outbox-failure rollback — the\n  last now asserting the outbox DELTA on the shared database)\n\nmake check-all green; full -tags=integration suite green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxS9ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3J4QACecOZ/paU75bXCN4zKNj/yg\nLkQu7JIjTi8rF94V6CXwFi3U8E9bSGklFDUi31jPDamKajeE1nPeSzBsQKgpbsOR\nRm2Rkixcl7PRCt2sDtPAFK5A630BE5tcOMFOnvkrAZkagEk7wsnccNBWFS1uMNw8\nttQ8QheNJ52qMVBmCnl7P9LvU2B7Psm/6+CGmLu3cOsBzNeZ08v8lpAuocOpk5Tq\nU6JiYBqtofWyhEm03fkU/FlUCepZVITKgRod0zrd9SkOcaeDxI4t69Dgi6wGi2c5\n/kDFP/UkCWCJh939MFCJz0+hESAZiRL3aPnvk0rh4iMRCb/U8HASdFdRADEZm0+U\nuWSS3dD16YONKXHw+W+R4bpVJfhbHVgRPMgEjdQY/HCpOTcC6/xW3hJDMhit54du\nHnRYKoF8nIG2Wpapj6VMbNyVfMjFCVK1XLlKc+KT1NpmAGAtHxFpAHsz2Zu8imH2\n47Ag7qxqInqd+/YRS4jQfkniCONczRH5twGQIRt2G8WxkuXoAuz8ywcdUWyhC5Og\nAxxR1VvCzJ3QOj6+JybKG3iE2ggBvcTDQ440PfUhJL4zP/wCislJxAsTVjgUbbrJ\ntaQcSjqDdK8k/d6aOK3u9YAU+jN0r7Y5+tsHFnIY4YwpntXUwjyZQumTdduNIPXh\n/CNMhP1W2Ydifpm7zILD\n=WfCi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T17:26:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/a7e79c10c1018f20ba0a98738c572c62c2628c2b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBuNoAKGE3ZTc5YzEwYzEwMThmMjBiYTBhOTg3MzhjNTcyYzYyYzI2MjhjMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/0e38e4416e179b6f22d53207b95aec7d03ebf772","sha":"0e38e4416e179b6f22d53207b95aec7d03ebf772","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/0e38e4416e179b6f22d53207b95aec7d03ebf772"}],"sha":"a7e79c10c1018f20ba0a98738c572c62c2628c2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/a7e79c10c1018f20ba0a98738c572c62c2628c2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/0e38e4416e179b6f22d53207b95aec7d03ebf772/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:01:29Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:01:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: tier-2 (wire tags out of domain, split main.go, one container per package) (#141)\n\n* test(events): pin LogPublisher JSON for every domain event (1a prep)\n\nGolden captured from the pre-refactor output where the domain events still carried json tags; the next commit moves the tags into adapter-owned DTOs and must keep this test green.\n\n* refactor(events): move JSON wire shape out of domain events (1a)\n\nshared.base lost its json tags; LogPublisher now maps every domain event (incl. product.ProductClassified) to adapter-owned DTOs in adapters/outbound/events/log_payload.go. Kafka/CloudEvents payloads were already adapter DTOs. Output is byte-identical (TestLogPublisher_PayloadMatchesGolden, captured pre-change). New fitness sensor TestDomainHasNoWireStructTags forbids json/db tags under internal/domain/**.\n\n* refactor(cmd/inventory): split the 680-line composition root by concern (2a)\n\nmain.go 680 -> 92 lines; config/telemetry/adapters/postgres/housekeeping/lookup/server/shutdown each in their own file, same package main. No function > 53 lines (run 118 -> 53, buildAdapters 97 -> 14). buildAdapters now returns an adapterSet instead of 9 values; the two callers in tests are updated mechanically. Startup/shutdown order, env vars and defaults unchanged. cmd/mcp (323 lines) left untouched per the >500-line rule.\n\n* test(postgres): one container per package, database per test","tree":{"sha":"8db8fb5e706d5c8e96bf2d67d1316cfac9393b72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/trees/8db8fb5e706d5c8e96bf2d67d1316cfac9393b72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/commits/0e38e4416e179b6f22d53207b95aec7d03ebf772","verification":{"payload":"tree 8db8fb5e706d5c8e96bf2d67d1316cfac9393b72\nparent 5f88dd5ef8e373a46c04094284207b1aa633e20e\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791291689 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791291689 -0300\n\nrefactor: tier-2 (wire tags out of domain, split main.go, one container per package) (#141)\n\n* test(events): pin LogPublisher JSON for every domain event (1a prep)\n\nGolden captured from the pre-refactor output where the domain events still carried json tags; the next commit moves the tags into adapter-owned DTOs and must keep this test green.\n\n* refactor(events): move JSON wire shape out of domain events (1a)\n\nshared.base lost its json tags; LogPublisher now maps every domain event (incl. product.ProductClassified) to adapter-owned DTOs in adapters/outbound/events/log_payload.go. Kafka/CloudEvents payloads were already adapter DTOs. Output is byte-identical (TestLogPublisher_PayloadMatchesGolden, captured pre-change). New fitness sensor TestDomainHasNoWireStructTags forbids json/db tags under internal/domain/**.\n\n* refactor(cmd/inventory): split the 680-line composition root by concern (2a)\n\nmain.go 680 -> 92 lines; config/telemetry/adapters/postgres/housekeeping/lookup/server/shutdown each in their own file, same package main. No function > 53 lines (run 118 -> 53, buildAdapters 97 -> 14). buildAdapters now returns an adapterSet instead of 9 values; the two callers in tests are updated mechanically. Startup/shutdown order, env vars and defaults unchanged. cmd/mcp (323 lines) left untouched per the >500-line rule.\n\n* test(postgres): one container per package, database per test","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxPEpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA470QAAW+up1dre7w1zoU9BIczois\n/l5iDk1umkpucROGDUoZwqG1prbKGPDDkWbdyA2+ZpqAmZSafYuz+A9J5hG1Awms\nGVQ1+o3N/ELXlgW3VjA1WzR5Nl3ShTgrGRl2fzdvDV0Jh4sd26Y+OF7KWabh6HnS\nj3v9G9hJg3KLeb1uQK30rvbJVVaKJJ2heCYjwC