ttps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/00c2f42fc4429d525208b0336ad60b771f85cc2e","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjBuNoAKDAwYzJmNDJmYzQ0MjlkNTI1MjA4YjAzMzZhZDYwYjc3MWY4NWNjMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/inventory-storage/commit/0b63336384fc35b418f8e06d567184cd3f9464f1","sha":"0b63336384fc35b418f8e06d567184cd3f9464f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/0b63336384fc35b418f8e06d567184cd3f9464f1"}],"sha":"00c2f42fc4429d525208b0336ad60b771f85cc2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/00c2f42fc4429d525208b0336ad60b771f85cc2e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/commits/0b63336384fc35b418f8e06d567184cd3f9464f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:07:38Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:07:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: ADR-conformance gaps from the 2026-10-04 audit (MCP outbox, metrics, idempotency docs, sweeper, ADR drift) (#130)\n\n* fix(mcp): publish revocations via transactional outbox; add otel HTTP metrics to MCP and reports routers; allow Idempotency-Key in CORS\n\n* docs(adr): ADR-0017 cmd/mcp now publishes via outbox; ADR-0016 H1 and router coverage\n\n* docs(api): document Idempotency-Key, all 14 missing problem slugs, /readyz and /reports/* in openapi; regenerate API reference; update ADR-0005/0018\n\nReports tag excluded from the Schemathesis run (served by the separate inventory-reports binary).\n\n* fix(resilience): facility-layout client honors ctx/CallTimeout (no fixed 5s client timeout); DLQ writer uses Hash+RequireAll\n\nItem 5 (ADR-0020).\n\n* fix(kafka): key analytics reservation-lifecycle events by reservation id (ADR-0021 amendment)\n\nStockReserved/StockPicked were keyed by SKU while ReservationRevoked/Expired were keyed by reservation id, so one reservation spanned partitions. Adds a testcontainers 8-partition affinity test; amends ADR-0021/0004/0011, asyncapi and integration.md (Hash balancer, not LeastBytes).\n\n* docs(adr): ADR-0019 matches code (no RETURNING; aggregate version not advanced after Save); fix comments citing ADR 0018 for optimistic concurrency\n\nItem 7.\n\n* feat(housekeeping): sweeper for idempotency_keys (TTL 24h) and published outbox_events (7d); chart values for lookup mode, facility URL, relay interval and sweeper\n\nItems 9 + chart part of item 8. ADR-0026. Testcontainers tests for the sweeper and the cmd/inventory env wiring.\n\n* docs(adr): fix drift in ADR-0001/0008/0009/0012; add ADR-0027 (MCP eval/governance), 0028 (bootretry), 0029 (extra fitness tests); CORS Idempotency-Key preflight test\n\nItem 8 + item 10 (+ CORS test for item 2).\n\n* test(kafka): satisfy the testcontainers-Kafka fitness rule in the analytics partition test\n\n* fix(openapi): drop minLength on Idempotency-Key (contract run accepts an empty header in in-memory mode); regenerate API docs\n\n* test(kafka): give the real-broker tests their own kafka-go Transport (the global DefaultTransport''s metadata cache made a second topic''s first write fail)","tree":{"sha":"3cf9429812e8ec1c05192f28e96d6a9582cfc5d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/trees/3cf9429812e8ec1c05192f28e96d6a9582cfc5d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/inventory-storage/git/commits/0b63336384fc35b418f8e06d567184cd3f9464f1","verification":{"payload":"tree 3cf9429812e8ec1c05192f28e96d6a9582cfc5d0\nparent e60c64a2b5324fbff796e06c1ed27c691aa9f37f\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791155258 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791155258 -0300\n\nfix: ADR-conformance gaps from the 2026-10-04 audit (MCP outbox, metrics, idempotency docs, sweeper, ADR drift) (#130)\n\n* fix(mcp): publish revocations via transactional outbox; add otel HTTP metrics to MCP and reports routers; allow Idempotency-Key in CORS\n\n* docs(adr): ADR-0017 cmd/mcp now publishes via outbox; ADR-0016 H1 and router coverage\n\n* docs(api): document Idempotency-Key, all 14 missing problem slugs, /readyz and /reports/* in openapi; regenerate API reference; update ADR-0005/0018\n\nReports tag excluded from the Schemathesis run (served by the separate inventory-reports binary).\n\n* fix(resilience): facility-layout client honors ctx/CallTimeout (no fixed 5s client timeout); DLQ writer uses Hash+RequireAll\n\nItem 5 (ADR-0020).\n\n* fix(kafka): key analytics reservation-lifecycle events by reservation id (ADR-0021 amendment)\n\nStockReserved/StockPicked were keyed by SKU while ReservationRevoked/Expired were keyed by reservation id, so one reservation spanned partitions. Adds a testcontainers 8-partition affinity test; amends ADR-0021/0004/0011, asyncapi and integration.md (Hash balancer, not LeastBytes).\n\n* docs(adr): ADR-0019 matches code (no RETURNING; aggregate version not advanced after Save); fix comments citing ADR 0018 for optimistic concurrency\n\nItem 7.\n\n* feat(housekeeping): sweeper for idempotency_keys (TTL 24h) and published outbox_events (7d); chart values for lookup mode, facility URL, relay interval and sweeper\n\nItems 9 + chart part of item 8. ADR-0026. Testcontainers tests for the sweeper and the cmd/inventory env wiring.\n\n* docs(adr): fix drift in ADR-0001/0008/0009/0012; add ADR-0027 (MCP eval/governance), 0028 (bootretry), 0029 (extra fitness tests); CORS Idempotency-Key preflight test\n\nItem 8 + item 10 (+ CORS test for item 2).\n\n* test(kafka): satisfy the testcontainers-Kafka fitness rule in the analytics partition test\n\n* fix(openapi): drop minLength on Idempotency-Key (contract run accepts an empty header in in-memory mode); regenerate API docs\n\n* test(kafka): give the real-broker tests their own kafka-go Transport (the global DefaultTransport''s metadata cache made a second topic''s first write fail)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwtw6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAEoQAHRn9+SvQpfpdltRIOJkdya/\nv3cEYN6gOV6GTIwGWyRrrTbO8fw5FgYazyM6aUp3ci5YsbN0nTomPIkIOfQBAFMw\n2iR1JvoZsBbZaXOR9SAufjLWUeFDBiW/o0KqwddCAm6k589bz1tgQXLHG0x1SJc8\nu4ld8BiOcJHkesEpWLYTVlLWU4172xqDmfdRsqfjvsvib+yGGtd2HhLBmQkVtkRR\naAqV+nMRrAyYW/LFQrdHdx40JTeQEVTWSXHYVDXoDkJXJPFEV/lf5L+XXh0NR2gx\nyYwxbgTbFVOzP+i5HGHVraWaiApxRWMjy62De9mHYCDtjO5XmQnGAmnpXC8V0y9P\nEPhF7+sJeouaG8pMQQpZanGgcDjljAtIlYuAi9kPprDZLJAWFS5yFF8g/qo3qlhr\nrBSGoiJk2YKL/kNHB4C6yBNxsVIycmEqkXjnn8eEU+2Xim8drvlLO22I2g7fURHr\n8/yyfHjDuMwqpDW2Ni/QfdpplyfY6qCV8d999JEL3/YQ4jBeZ/5Azm58zA13xzhJ\nvLMj5GuOMwTOT/Ow9MZfaq8hiTpwFQSVtkQf/6S9Qdt36Ins9wgcicAl1DXAs0hr\n3DrDcVhHHDgxpFSn